window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0015", [{"word":"enormous","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈnɔːməs/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈnɔːrməs/","definition_zh":"巨大的；庞大的；极大的；异常的；（古义）骇人的","definition_en":"extremely large in size, amount, or importance, far beyond the usual measure","core_image":"木工尺量不住的一块石头：尺寸越出规矩之外","scene":"A single enormous wave broke over the harbour wall.","sceneCN":"这里 enormous 是「尺寸巨大、远超常规」（第 1 个义项：尺寸远远超出常规量度）；句意：一道巨浪越过港口的防波堤。图中可辨识物件：巨浪、防波堤、码头、被水花打湿的渔船。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"巨大的；庞大的；极大的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"an enormous amount of","zh":"大量的……"},{"phrase":"an enormous number of","zh":"数目极大的……"},{"phrase":"enormous impact","zh":"巨大的影响"},{"phrase":"enormous pressure","zh":"巨大的压力"},{"phrase":"enormous potential","zh":"巨大的潜力"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more enormous"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most enormous"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"enormously","pos":"adv.","zh":"极其；非常"},{"word":"enormousness","pos":"n.","zh":"巨大；庞大"},{"word":"enormity","pos":"n.","zh":"巨大；穷凶极恶（保留“骇人”的古义）"},{"word":"enorm","pos":"adj.","zh":"（古）巨大的；骇人的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Beyond the rule: larger than the measure allows","titleCN":"越出规矩：大到量度装不下","definition":"extremely large in size, far beyond what is usual or expected","definitionCN":"尺寸极大，远远超出通常或预期的大小","example":"An enormous boulder blocked the narrow trail.","exampleCN":"一块巨石堵住了狭窄的小径。","why":"Latin enormis joined ex- 'out of' to norma 'carpenter's square, rule'. Something enormous literally goes outside the measuring rule, so size that breaks the norm is the core sense.","whyCN":"拉丁语 enormis 把 ex-“出”加在 norma“木工尺、规矩”上。enormous 字面上就是“走出量度之外”，因此“大到破坏常规”是核心义。"},{"no":"02","title":"Great in amount: too many to count by the usual measure","titleCN":"数量巨大：多到常规量法数不清","definition":"existing in very large amounts, used of quantities that are hard to count","definitionCN":"以极大的数量存在，用于难以计数的量","example":"The archive holds an enormous amount of climate data.","exampleCN":"该档案馆保存着数量巨大的气候数据。","why":"Once the rule is broken in size, the same image transfers to number and amount: a quantity too large to fit the normal measure.","whyCN":"一旦尺寸越出规矩，同一意象就转到数目与数量上：多到常规量度装不下的量。"},{"no":"03","title":"Great in importance: weight that dominates","titleCN":"分量极重：支配一切的重要性","definition":"very great in importance, influence, or seriousness","definitionCN":"在重要性、影响力或严重性上极大","example":"The discovery had an enormous impact on medicine.","exampleCN":"这一发现对医学产生了巨大影响。","why":"Importance is measured on a scale too. When something outweighs every other factor, it goes off the same scale, so enormous extends to influence.","whyCN":"重要性同样是被量度的。当某物压过其他所有因素，它就超出了同一把尺，于是 enormous 延伸到影响力。"},{"no":"04","title":"A task beyond ordinary effort","titleCN":"超出常规人力的任务","definition":"very great in scale or difficulty, used of work and effort","definitionCN":"规模或难度极大，用于工作与付出","example":"Rebuilding the bridge was an enormous task.","exampleCN":"重建这座桥是一项艰巨的任务。","why":"Effort is measured in hours and strength. Work that no ordinary measure contains becomes enormous in the same 'out of measure' sense.","whyCN":"付出用时间和力气来量。常规量度装不下的工作，就以同一个“越出量度”的意思变成 enormous。"},{"no":"05","title":"Astronomical and geographic scale","titleCN":"天文与地理的尺度","definition":"used of distances and scales far beyond human experience","definitionCN":"用于远远超出人类经验的距离与尺度","example":"The telescope measures enormous distances between galaxies.","exampleCN":"这台望远镜测量星系之间巨大的距离。","why":"Space gives the oldest image its largest canvas: distances so far outside any human rule that only the word enormous fits.","whyCN":"宇宙为这个最古老的意象提供了最大的画布：距离远到超出任何人类尺度，只有 enormous 才装得下。"},{"no":"06","title":"Informal intensifier with abstract nouns","titleCN":"口语强调：与抽象名词连用","definition":"used informally before abstract nouns to mean 'very great', as in enormous fun or enormous help","definitionCN":"口语中用于抽象名词前，表示“非常”，如 enormous fun、enormous help","example":"Your help was enormous; we finished in half the time.","exampleCN":"你的帮助非常大，我们只用一半时间就完成了。","why":"In speech the norm-breaking size fades into pure emphasis, but the grammar is the same: an abstract noun is placed beyond the ordinary measure.","whyCN":"口语中“越出常规的尺寸”淡化为纯粹的强调，但语法相同：把抽象名词放到常规量度之外。"},{"no":"07","title":"Archaic 'monstrous': the sense kept in enormity","titleCN":"古义“骇人”：保留在 enormity 里","definition":"in older use, monstrous or outrageously bad, a sense now carried mainly by enormity","definitionCN":"旧时用法指“骇人的、穷凶极恶的”，今主要由 enormity 承担","example":"Early writers called the massacre an enormous crime, meaning monstrous rather than merely large.","exampleCN":"早期作家把这场屠杀称为 enormous crime，意思是“骇人”而非仅仅“规模大”。","why":"The 1530s sense was 'abnormal, outrageous', and enormity keeps that moral branch; modern enormous kept only the size branch.","whyCN":"16 世纪 30 年代的义项是“异常、骇人”，enormity 保留了这条道德分支；现代 enormous 只留下尺寸分支。"},{"no":"08","title":"Out of proportion to its setting","titleCN":"与所处框架不成比例","definition":"the quality of being out of proportion to its surroundings, which enormous adds to plain size words","definitionCN":"与周围环境不成比例的性质，这是 enormous 比一般尺寸词多出来的一层","example":"The tiny hall held an enormous chandelier that almost touched the walls.","exampleCN":"小小的厅里挂着一盏巨大的枝形吊灯，几乎碰到墙壁。","why":"Because norma is a rule, enormous does not merely say 'big'; it says the thing does not fit its frame. Near-synonyms such as huge describe size without that judgment.","whyCN":"因为 norma 是“规矩”，enormous 不只是说“大”，还说这东西装不进自己的框架。huge 等近义词只描述尺寸，不带这层判断。"},{"no":"09","title":"Enormous appetite: a natural drive on a large scale","titleCN":"巨大的胃口：自然欲望的极大量","definition":"used of strong natural drives such as appetite, energy, or curiosity, meaning very great in degree","definitionCN":"用于胃口、精力、好奇心等强烈本能，表示程度极大","example":"The kittens had an enormous appetite and finished the whole bowl.","exampleCN":"这些小猫胃口极大，把整碗都吃光了。","why":"Appetite is measured against what a body normally needs. A drive far past that measure repeats the same ex plus norma pattern in a living context.","whyCN":"胃口是相对身体正常所需来量的。远超这个量度的欲望，在生命语境里重复了同一个 ex + norma 结构。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Enormous entered English in the 1530s from Latin enormis, literally 'out of rule'. The 'very large' sense followed within a decade, while the older moral sense survives in enormity.","cn":"enormous 于 16 世纪 30 年代从拉丁语 enormis 进入英语，字面是“出了规矩”。不到十年内又出现“极大”义，而较早的道德义保存在 enormity 中。"},"items":[{"era":"1530S","en":"First recorded with the sense 'abnormal, extraordinary', often with disapproval rather than admiration.","cn":"最早记录的义项是“异常的、非凡的”，常带贬义而非赞叹。"},{"era":"1540S","en":"By the 1540s the meaning 'of great size' appears; the older moral force then moved to enormity.","cn":"到 16 世纪 40 年代出现“尺寸巨大”义；较早的道德力量随后转移到 enormity。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin enormis 'out of rule, irregular, shapeless; extraordinary, immense', built on ex- 'out of' plus norma 'carpenter's square, rule'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 enormis“出规、不规则、无形；非凡、极大”，由 ex-“出”加 norma“木工尺、规矩”构成。"},{"era":"LATIN / UNCERTAIN","en":"Norma's own origin is unknown. Klein suggested it came through Etruscan from Greek gnomon 'carpenter's square, judge', so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"norma 本身的来源不明。Klein 认为它经伊特鲁里亚语借自希腊语 gnomon“木工尺、判者”，因此最深层来源不确定。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps enormous for size and leaves the 'monstrous' sense to enormity; enormousness names the state and enormously the adverb.","cn":"现代英语用 enormous 表示尺寸，把“骇人”义留给 enormity；enormousness 是状态名词，enormously 是副词。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"enormity","ipa":"/ɪˈnɔːməti/","tag":"false friend","definition":"great wickedness or seriousness, not physical size. It keeps the older 'monstrous' sense that enormous has lost.","definitionCN":"穷凶极恶；严重性，而非物理尺寸。它保留了 enormous 已失去的“骇人”古义。"},{"word":"anonymous","ipa":"/əˈnɒnɪməs/","tag":"shared -ous","definition":"having an unknown name. It shares the -ous ending but starts from Greek onyma 'name', not from norma.","definitionCN":"匿名的。它同样以 -ous 结尾，但词源是希腊语 onyma“名字”，与 norma 无关。"},{"word":"ginormous","ipa":"/dʒaɪˈnɔːməs/","tag":"informal blend","definition":"very large, blending gigantic and enormous. It is informal and adds no norm-breaking judgment.","definitionCN":"极大的。由 gigantic 与 enormous 混合而成，属口语，不带“破坏常规”的判断。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"huge","ipa":"/hjuːdʒ/","tag":"plain size","definition":"very large in size or amount. It states size plainly, while enormous adds that the size breaks the normal measure.","definitionCN":"巨大的。它只平实地说明尺寸，而 enormous 额外表示“尺寸越出常规量度”。"},{"word":"immense","ipa":"/ɪˈmens/","tag":"immeasurable","definition":"extremely large or great, literally 'not measurable'. It stresses immeasurability more than the broken rule.","definitionCN":"极大的，字面是“不可测量”。它更强调“无法丈量”，而不是“破坏规矩”。"},{"word":"vast","ipa":"/vɑːst/","tag":"extent","definition":"extremely great in area, extent, or scope. It suits spaces and ranges, while enormous suits single things and amounts.","definitionCN":"辽阔的；巨大的。它适合空间与范围，enormous 更适合单个物体和数量。"},{"word":"gigantic","ipa":"/dʒaɪˈɡæntɪk/","tag":"creature comparison","definition":"extremely large like a giant. It uses a comparison with a creature rather than a measuring rule.","definitionCN":"巨大的。它用“像巨人一样”作比较，而不是用“量度规矩”作参照。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin parts ex plus norma, the norma family of norm and normal, and the historical split between enormous and enormity.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁成分 ex + norma、norm 与 normal 的 norma 词族，以及 enormous 与 enormity 的历史分工。"},"normal":[{"en":"ex- 'out of' plus norma 'carpenter's square' gives 'out of rule': the thing is too big for the measuring tool.","cn":"ex-“出”加 norma“木工尺”就是“出了规矩”：这东西大到量具装不下。"},{"en":"norm, normal and abnormal all keep norma, the rule that enormous literally goes outside of.","cn":"norm、normal、abnormal 都保留了 norma 这把尺，而 enormous 字面上正是走到这把尺之外。"},{"en":"enormity is the moral cousin: it kept the 'monstrous' sense while enormous kept the size sense.","cn":"enormity 是道德上的同族词：它保留了“骇人”义，而 enormous 保留了尺寸义。"},{"en":"enormousness is the noun for sheer size, and enormously is the adverb of degree.","cn":"enormousness 是表示“巨大”的名词，enormously 是表示程度极高的副词。"},{"en":"an enormous amount of and an enormous number of are the standard frames for quantity.","cn":"an enormous amount of 与 an enormous number of 是表示数量的标准搭配框架。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a stone so wide that the carpenter's square cannot span it: the tool is left lying beside the object.","cn":"想象一块宽到木工尺跨不过去的石头：量具只能被搁在旁边。"},{"en":"The same 'outside the frame' feeling can be drawn around a crowd, a debt, a distance, or a responsibility.","cn":"同一种“出了框架”的感觉，可以画在一群人、一笔债、一段距离或一份责任上。"},{"en":"When the frame disappears, size becomes emphasis: enormous help is help that no ordinary amount can contain.","cn":"当框架消失，尺寸就变成强调：enormous help 是常规分量装不下的帮助。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"An enormous rock had fallen across the only road out of the village.","cn":"一块巨石横落在出村唯一的一条路上。"},{"en":"The project required an enormous amount of time and patience.","cn":"这个项目需要大量的时间和耐心。"},{"en":"Even the enormous oak looked small beside the new tower.","cn":"在那座新塔旁，连巨大的橡树也显得矮小。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一挪冒石」——挪开一步就冒出一块巨石 → enormous 巨大的、庞大的","word":"enormous"},"root":"源自拉丁语 enormis“超出规矩、不规则”= ex-“出”+ norma“木工尺、规矩”，核心是“尺寸越出量度”；norma 更深来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of enormous all start from one picture: a thing too large for the carpenter's square. The same broken measure then moves from physical size to amount, importance, effort, space and emphasis.","cn":"enormous 的九个义项都从同一幅画出发：一个东西大到木工尺量不住。同一把被撑破的尺，随后从实体尺寸走到数量、重要性、付出、宇宙尺度和强调。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a stone too large for the carpenter's square.","cn":"核心意象：一块大到木工尺量不住的石头。"},"chain":["MEASURE","EXCEED THE RULE","TOO LARGE TO HOLD","GREAT IN AMOUNT","BEYOND ORDINARY SCALE","OUT OF PROPORTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"THE BROKEN RULE: physical size beyond the norm, and the extra sense that the thing does not fit its setting.","cn":"被撑破的规矩：超出常规的实体尺寸，以及“装不进所处框架”的附加意味。"},{"senses":"S2 · S9","en":"AMOUNT AND DRIVE: the same excess applied to quantities and to natural appetites.","cn":"数量与欲望：同一种“过量”用在数目和本能欲望上。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"WEIGHT AND EFFORT: importance that dominates, and work too great for ordinary strength.","cn":"分量与付出：支配一切的重要性，以及超出常规人力的工作。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"COSMIC SCALE: distances so far out that the human measure disappears entirely.","cn":"宇宙尺度：距离远到人类量度完全消失。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"EMPHASIS AND THE OLD MORAL: informal intensifier use, and the 'monstrous' sense that now lives in enormity.","cn":"强调与旧道德义：口语强调用法，以及今由 enormity 承担的“骇人”义。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Enormous is built from the Latin stem enorm- plus the adjective suffix -ous. English then adds -ly, -ness and -ity, and the bare root norma also survives in norm, normal and abnormal.","cn":"enormous 由拉丁词干 enorm- 加形容词后缀 -ous 构成。英语随后又加 -ly、-ness、-ity，而光秃的词根 norma 也活在 norm、normal、abnormal 中。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin enormis (ex- 'out of' + norma 'rule') is the direct source; norma itself is of uncertain origin, possibly through Etruscan from Greek gnomon.","cn":"拉丁语 enormis（ex-“出”+ norma“规矩”）是直接来源；norma 本身来源不明，可能经伊特鲁里亚语来自希腊语 gnomon。"},"items":[{"word":"enormous","structure":"enorm- (out of measure) + -ous (adjective)","meaning":"extremely large, beyond the normal measure","meaningCN":"巨大的；超出常规量度的（-ous 构成形容词）","example":"They live in an enormous house near the park.","exampleCN":"他们住在公园附近一栋巨大的房子里。"},{"word":"enormously","structure":"enormous + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"to a very great degree","meaningCN":"极其；非常（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The city has grown enormously since 1990.","exampleCN":"这座城市自 1990 年以来发展极其迅速。"},{"word":"enormousness","structure":"enormous + -ness (state noun)","meaning":"the quality of being enormous","meaningCN":"巨大；庞大（-ness 构成状态名词）","example":"The enormousness of the hall surprised the visitors.","exampleCN":"大厅的庞大规模让参观者吃惊。"},{"word":"enormity","structure":"enorm- + -ity (state noun)","meaning":"great size, or great wickedness","meaningCN":"巨大；凶残（-ity 构成名词，今多指道德上的严重）","example":"The enormity of the crime shocked the court.","exampleCN":"罪行的严重程度震惊了法庭。"},{"word":"enorm","structure":"enorm- (bare stem used as adjective)","meaning":"archaic: monstrous or huge","meaningCN":"（古）骇人的；巨大的（词干直接作形容词）","example":"The old chronicle speaks of an enorm beast.","exampleCN":"那部古老编年史提到一只骇人的巨兽。"},{"word":"norm","structure":"norma (carpenter's square, rule)","meaning":"a standard or rule","meaningCN":"规范；准则（来自同一词根 norma）","example":"Working from home has become the norm.","exampleCN":"居家办公已成为常态。"},{"word":"normal","structure":"norm + -al (adjective)","meaning":"following the usual standard","meaningCN":"正常的；标准的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The test results were normal.","exampleCN":"检查结果正常。"},{"word":"abnormal","structure":"ab- (away from) + normal","meaning":"departing from the usual rule","meaningCN":"异常的（ab-“离开”+ normal，即离开常规）","example":"The scan showed an abnormal growth.","exampleCN":"扫描显示有一处异常增生。"},{"word":"normalize","structure":"normal + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to make standard or normal","meaningCN":"使正常化；使标准化（-ize 构成动词）","example":"The two countries agreed to normalize relations.","exampleCN":"两国同意使关系正常化。"},{"word":"normative","structure":"norm + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"prescribing a standard","meaningCN":"规范的；标准性的（-ative 构成形容词）","example":"The paper discusses normative rules of grammar.","exampleCN":"这篇论文讨论语法的规范性规则。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"enormis","structure":"ex- (out of) + norma (rule)","meaning":"out of rule, irregular; extraordinary, immense","meaningCN":"出规的；不规则的；非凡的；极大的"},{"word":"norma","structure":"norma (noun)","meaning":"carpenter's square, rule, standard","meaningCN":"木工尺；规矩；标准（更深来源不确定）"},{"word":"enormitas","structure":"enormis + -itas","meaning":"enormousness; monstrosity","meaningCN":"巨大；骇人；穷凶极恶"}]}},{"word":"ensure","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈʃʊə/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈʃʊr/","definition_zh":"确保；保证；担保；使安全（古义）","definition_en":"to make something certain to happen, especially by taking action in advance","core_image":"把一件事钉牢在“一定发生”的板上，不留缺口","scene":"The nurse checked the drip twice to ensure the dose was correct.","sceneCN":"这里 ensure 是「确保、查明无误」（第 1 个义项：采取行动使某事一定成立）；句意：护士检查了两次输液装置，以确保剂量正确。图中可辨识物件：输液袋、滴管、剂量标签、护士的记事板。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"确保；保证；担保"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"ensure that","zh":"确保……"},{"phrase":"ensure the safety of","zh":"确保……的安全"},{"phrase":"ensure compliance with","zh":"确保遵守……"},{"phrase":"ensure access to","zh":"确保获得……"},{"phrase":"ensure accuracy","zh":"确保准确性"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"ensures"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"ensured"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"ensured"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"ensuring"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"assure","pos":"v.","zh":"向……保证；使安心（同出 securus 词族）"},{"word":"assurance","pos":"n.","zh":"保证；信心（assure 的名词）"},{"word":"insure","pos":"v.","zh":"投保；为……保险（ensure 的拼写变体分化而来）"},{"word":"insurance","pos":"n.","zh":"保险"},{"word":"secure","pos":"adj./v.","zh":"安全的；使安全；获得"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Make certain: see that something happens","titleCN":"确保：让某事一定发生","definition":"to make something certain to happen, especially by taking action","definitionCN":"使某事一定发生，尤指通过采取行动","example":"Please ensure that the door is locked before you leave.","exampleCN":"离开前请确保门已锁好。","why":"Old French enseurer joined en- 'make' to seur 'sure', from Latin securus 'free from care'. The verb literally means 'make sure', and that is its core.","whyCN":"古法语 enseurer 把 en-“使”加在 seur“确定”上，seur 来自拉丁语 securus“无忧”。这个动词字面就是“使确定”，这就是核心义。"},{"no":"02","title":"Guarantee an outcome by planning","titleCN":"通过安排保证结果","definition":"to arrange matters so that a result is guaranteed","definitionCN":"把各项事宜安排好，使结果得到保证","example":"The backup generator ensures power during storms.","exampleCN":"备用发电机确保暴风雨期间仍有电力。","why":"Making sure is not only a wish but a design: the plan removes the chance of failure, so the result is guaranteed.","whyCN":"“确保”不只是愿望，而是一种设计：计划消除了失败的可能，于是结果得到保证。"},{"no":"03","title":"Provide for a need: make sure someone has something","titleCN":"供给所需：确保某人得到某物","definition":"to make sure that someone has what they need","definitionCN":"确保某人的所需得到满足","example":"The school ensures every child a free lunch.","exampleCN":"学校确保每个孩子都有一份免费午餐。","why":"If a need is met in advance, nothing is left to chance; providing is one concrete way of making sure.","whyCN":"如果需求被提前满足，就没有什么留给偶然；供给就是“确保”的一种具体做法。"},{"no":"04","title":"Keep safe: the older 'make secure' sense","titleCN":"使安全：较早的“使无虞”义","definition":"in older or formal use, to keep someone or something safe from harm","definitionCN":"在较旧或正式用法中，使某人某物免受伤害","example":"The treaty ensured the small state against invasion.","exampleCN":"该条约使这个小国免遭入侵。","why":"Securus meant 'free from care', and the earliest sense was 'make safe'. The modern 'make certain' is that safety applied to outcomes.","whyCN":"securus 意为“无忧”，最早义项是“使安全”。现代的“确保”就是这种安全被应用到结果上。"},{"no":"05","title":"Ensure reliability in research","titleCN":"研究中确保可靠性","definition":"to take steps so that measurements, samples, or procedures meet a standard","definitionCN":"采取措施使测量、样本或程序达到标准","example":"To ensure reliability, each sample was tested twice.","exampleCN":"为确保可靠性，每个样本都测了两次。","why":"In the laboratory, making sure means controlling the procedure. The word turns a promise about an outcome into a method.","whyCN":"在实验室里，“确保”意味着控制程序。这个词把对结果的承诺变成了一套方法。"},{"no":"06","title":"Legal and contractual guarantee","titleCN":"法律与合同上的保证","definition":"of a contract or rule, to guarantee a right, payment, or condition","definitionCN":"（合同或规则）保证一项权利、付款或条件","example":"The contract ensures payment within thirty days.","exampleCN":"合同确保三十天内付款。","why":"A contract makes a future act certain by binding it to a rule, which is the legal form of 'make sure'.","whyCN":"合同通过把未来行为绑定到规则上而使之确定，这就是“确保”的法律形式。"},{"no":"07","title":"Ensure vs assure: facts, not people","titleCN":"ensure 与 assure：确保事实，而非安抚人","definition":"to make a fact certain, in contrast with assure, which calms a person","definitionCN":"使一个事实确定，与 assure（安抚某人）相对","example":"The doctor assured the patient, while the nurse ensured that the consent form was signed.","exampleCN":"医生安慰病人，而护士则确保同意书已经签字。","why":"Assure comes from the same seur but takes a person as object: it makes someone feel sure. Ensure takes a fact or event, so the two split by object.","whyCN":"assure 同出 seur，但宾语是人：它使某人感到确定。ensure 的宾语是事实或事件，两者因此按宾语分工。"},{"no":"08","title":"Ensure vs insure: guarantee versus buy cover","titleCN":"ensure 与 insure：保证发生，还是购买保障","definition":"to guarantee that something happens, in contrast with insure, which buys protection against loss","definitionCN":"保证某事发生，与 insure（为损失购买保障）相对","example":"You insure the house against fire; you ensure that the smoke alarms work.","exampleCN":"你为房子投保火灾险；你要确保烟雾报警器正常工作。","why":"Insure kept the 'make safe' branch in the insurance business from the mid-17c. Ensure stayed with the guarantee of events, so only insure names a policy.","whyCN":"从 17 世纪中期起，insure 在保险业中保留了“使安全”分支；ensure 留在“保证事件发生”上，因此只有 insure 能指保单。"},{"no":"09","title":"Ensure in policy language: secure equal access","titleCN":"政策语中的 ensure：保障平等获得","definition":"used of public commitments to guarantee access, rights, or fair treatment","definitionCN":"用于公共承诺，保证获得机会、权利或公平对待","example":"The new law ensures equal access to public transport.","exampleCN":"新法律确保平等使用公共交通的机会。","why":"When a state promises a right, it claims to make the future certain for everyone; the same verb carries the guarantee into policy.","whyCN":"当国家承诺一项权利，它声称要为所有人把未来变得确定；同一个动词把这种保证带进了政策。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Ensure was formed in Anglo-French in the late 14th century from en- 'make' plus seur 'sure'. It shares a root with assure, insure and secure, and the three English verbs later divided the work.","cn":"ensure 于 14 世纪晚期在英法双语中由 en-“使”加 seur“确定”构成。它与 assure、insure、secure 同根，后来三个英语动词分了工。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"Ensure is recorded as 'make sure, make safe', formed in Anglo-French rather than inherited from Old English.","cn":"ensure 最早记录为“使确定、使安全”，是在英法双语中构成的，而非从古英语继承。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"enseurer = en- 'make' + seur 'sure, secure', influenced by asseurer, the source of English assure.","cn":"enseurer = en-“使”+ seur“确定、安全”，并受 asseurer（英语 assure 的来源）影响。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"seur goes back to Latin securus 'free from care' = se- 'free from' + cura 'care'. The same base gives secure and security.","cn":"seur 可追溯到拉丁语 securus“无忧”= se-“免于”+ cura“忧虑”。同一词基也给出 secure 和 security。"},{"era":"MID-15C.","en":"Insure appears in the mid-15th century as a spelling variant of ensure; for centuries the two were interchangeable.","cn":"insure 于 15 世纪中期作为 ensure 的拼写变体出现；数百年间两者可互换。"},{"era":"MID-17C.","en":"The insurance business fixed insure for 'buy cover' in the mid-17th century, leaving ensure to the guarantee of events.","cn":"保险业在 17 世纪中期把 insure 固定为“购买保障”，把 ensure 留给“保证事件发生”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the object split: ensure a fact, assure a person, insure a risk.","cn":"现代英语保持宾语分工：ensure 接事实，assure 接人，insure 接风险。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning. The assure and insure entries show why the three verbs are so often confused.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选。assure 与 insure 两条说明这三个动词为何常被混淆。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"ensue","ipa":"/ɪnˈsjuː/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to happen after and because of something. It looks close to ensure but means 'follow', from Latin sequi 'to follow'.","definitionCN":"随后发生；因而产生。它看起来接近 ensure，但意思是“跟随”，来自拉丁语 sequi“跟随”。"},{"word":"assurance","ipa":"/əˈʃʊərəns/","tag":"shared -sure","definition":"a promise or a feeling of confidence. It is the noun of assure, not of ensure, and often names a person's calm.","definitionCN":"保证；信心。它是 assure 的名词，不是 ensure 的，常指一个人的安心。"},{"word":"reassure","ipa":"/ˌriːəˈʃʊə/","tag":"shared root","definition":"to make someone feel less worried. It is re- 'again' plus assure, so it works on a person, not on a fact.","definitionCN":"使某人不再担心。它是 re-“再次”+ assure，作用于人，而不是事实。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"assure","ipa":"/əˈʃʊə/","tag":"person as object","definition":"to tell someone confidently so that they feel sure. It takes a person as object, while ensure takes a fact or event.","definitionCN":"向某人肯定地说明，使其安心。它的宾语是人，而 ensure 的宾语是事实或事件。"},{"word":"insure","ipa":"/ɪnˈʃʊə/","tag":"buy cover","definition":"to buy protection against loss by paying a premium. The 'make safe' branch went into insurance, while ensure stayed with guarantees.","definitionCN":"支付保费以防范损失。它的“使安全”分支进入了保险业，而 ensure 留在“保证”上。"},{"word":"guarantee","ipa":"/ˌɡærənˈtiː/","tag":"stronger","definition":"to promise that a result will certainly happen, often with legal force. It is stronger and more formal than ensure.","definitionCN":"承诺某一结果必定发生，常带法律效力。它比 ensure 更强、更正式。"},{"word":"secure","ipa":"/sɪˈkjʊə/","tag":"obtain or protect","definition":"to obtain something firmly or make it safe. It stresses getting or protecting, while ensure stresses that an event is certain.","definitionCN":"牢牢获得某物或使其安全。它强调取得或保护，而 ensure 强调事件一定发生。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the en- plus seur structure, the securus family behind sure, and the historical division among ensure, assure and insure.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：en- + seur 结构、sure 背后的 securus 词族，以及 ensure、assure、insure 的历史分工。"},"normal":[{"en":"en- 'make' plus seur 'sure' literally spells 'make sure', which is the whole meaning of ensure.","cn":"en-“使”加 seur“确定”字面就是“使确定”，这就是 ensure 的全部意思。"},{"en":"securus = se- 'free from' + cura 'care', so sure, secure, security and ensure all carry the idea of being free from worry.","cn":"securus = se-“免于”+ cura“忧虑”，所以 sure、secure、security、ensure 都带着“免于忧虑”的意思。"},{"en":"assure takes a person, ensure takes a fact: you assure a nervous patient and ensure a correct dose.","cn":"assure 接人，ensure 接事实：你安慰紧张的病人（assure），确保剂量正确（ensure）。"},{"en":"insure is the spelling that went into the insurance business, so it names buying cover rather than making events certain.","cn":"insure 是进入保险业的那个拼写，因此它指购买保障，而不是使事件确定。"},{"en":"The standard frame is ensure that plus a clause, or ensure plus a noun such as safety, accuracy, access.","cn":"标准框架是 ensure that 加从句，或 ensure 加 safety、accuracy、access 这类名词。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a hand pressing a nail through a board until the future cannot slip loose.","cn":"想象一只手把钉子钉穿木板，直到未来再也滑不掉。"},{"en":"Ensuring is not hoping: it closes every gap through which failure could enter.","cn":"ensure 不是祈愿：它把失败可能钻进来的每个缝隙都封上。"},{"en":"The same closed gap can protect a child, a payment, a sample, or a right.","cn":"同一个被封住的缝隙，可以保护一个孩子、一笔付款、一个样本或一项权利。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Please ensure that all windows are closed before the storm arrives.","cn":"请在暴风雨到来前确保所有窗户都已关好。"},{"en":"The helmet ensures that a fall will not injure your head.","cn":"头盔确保摔倒时不会伤到你的头部。"},{"en":"The rules were written to ensure fair treatment for every applicant.","cn":"这些规则是为了确保每位申请者都得到公平对待。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「因守」——因为一直守着门口，所以确保没人乱闯 → ensure 确保、保证","word":"ensure"},"root":"源自古法语 enseurer = en-“使”+ seur“确定、安全”，seur 来自拉丁语 securus“无忧”，核心是“把一件事变成一定发生”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of ensure share one action: nailing 'it will happen' to the board. The nail can fix an event, an outcome, a supply, a person's safety, a procedure, a contract, or a public right.","cn":"ensure 的九个义项共用一个动作：把“它一定发生”钉在板上。这枚钉子可以钉住事件、结果、供给、人身安全、程序、合同或公共权利。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand nailing the future to a board so it cannot slip.","cn":"核心意象：一只手把未来钉在板上，使它滑不掉。"},"chain":["MAKE SURE","REMOVE CHANCE","GUARANTEE OUTCOME","PROVIDE A NEED","KEEP SAFE","BIND BY RULE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"CERTAINTY: the plain act of making something sure, and the planned arrangement that guarantees a result.","cn":"确定性：使某事确定的直白动作，以及通过安排保证结果的做法。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"PROVISION AND SAFETY: making sure a need is met, and the older branch of keeping someone safe.","cn":"供给与安全：确保需求得到满足，以及较早的“使某人安全”分支。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"METHOD AND CONTRACT: reliability built into a procedure, and a guarantee written into a contract.","cn":"方法与合同：把可靠性做进程序，以及把保证写进合同。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"THE THREE VERBS: ensure takes facts, assure takes people, and insure buys cover.","cn":"三个动词的分工：ensure 接事实，assure 接人，insure 购买保障。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"PUBLIC PROMISE: the state claims to make access and rights certain for everyone.","cn":"公共承诺：国家声称要为所有人把机会与权利变得确定。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Ensure is en- plus the French stem seur. The same stem, through Latin securus, builds assure, insure, secure, security and reassurance.","cn":"ensure 是 en- 加法语词干 seur。同一词干经拉丁语 securus，构成 assure、insure、secure、security 和 reassurance。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin securus 'free from care' (se- 'free from' + cura 'care') is the base of the whole family; securitas gives security, and cura itself gives cure and curious.","cn":"拉丁语 securus“无忧”（se-“免于”+ cura“忧虑”）是整个词族的基础；securitas 给出 security，cura 本身给出 cure 与 curious。"},"items":[{"word":"ensure","structure":"en- (make) + seur (sure)","meaning":"to make certain","meaningCN":"确保；保证（en- 使 + seur 确定）","example":"We must ensure that the data is correct.","exampleCN":"我们必须确保数据正确。"},{"word":"sure","structure":"seur (certain, secure)","meaning":"certain; free from doubt","meaningCN":"确定的；有把握的（来自 seur）","example":"Are you sure the key is in your bag?","exampleCN":"你确定钥匙在包里吗？"},{"word":"assure","structure":"as- (ad-, to) + sure","meaning":"to make a person feel certain","meaningCN":"向某人保证；使安心（as- 朝向 + sure）","example":"The doctor assured her that the test was normal.","exampleCN":"医生向她保证检查结果正常。"},{"word":"assurance","structure":"assure + -ance (noun)","meaning":"a promise; confidence","meaningCN":"保证；信心（-ance 构成名词）","example":"He gave us an assurance that the work would be finished.","exampleCN":"他向我们保证工作会完成。"},{"word":"insure","structure":"in- (make) + sure","meaning":"to make safe; to buy insurance","meaningCN":"为……投保；使有保障（in- 使 + sure）","example":"They insure the gallery against theft.","exampleCN":"他们为画廊投保防盗险。"},{"word":"insurance","structure":"insure + -ance (noun)","meaning":"protection bought against loss","meaningCN":"保险（-ance 构成名词）","example":"The insurance covers damage from floods.","exampleCN":"这份保险涵盖洪水造成的损失。"},{"word":"secure","structure":"se- (free from) + cura (care)","meaning":"safe; to make safe or obtain","meaningCN":"安全的；使安全；获得（se- 免于 + cura 忧虑）","example":"Please secure the door before you leave.","exampleCN":"离开前请把门锁好。"},{"word":"security","structure":"secure + -ity (noun)","meaning":"the state of being safe","meaningCN":"安全；安全保障（-ity 构成名词）","example":"Airport security checked every bag.","exampleCN":"机场安检检查了每个包。"},{"word":"insecure","structure":"in- (not) + secure","meaning":"not safe; lacking confidence","meaningCN":"不安全的；缺乏信心的（in- 表否定）","example":"The old bridge feels insecure in high winds.","exampleCN":"那座旧桥在大风中让人感觉不安全。"},{"word":"reassure","structure":"re- (again) + assure","meaning":"to make someone feel less worried","meaningCN":"使安心；再次安慰（re- 再次 + assure）","example":"She reassured the child that the dog was friendly.","exampleCN":"她安慰孩子说那条狗很友善。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"securus","structure":"se- (free from) + cura (care)","meaning":"free from care, safe","meaningCN":"无忧的；安全的"},{"word":"cura","structure":"cura (noun)","meaning":"care, concern","meaningCN":"关心；忧虑"},{"word":"securitas","structure":"securus + -itas","meaning":"freedom from care, security","meaningCN":"无忧；安全"}]}},{"word":"environment","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","definition_zh":"环境；自然环境；周围状况；氛围","definition_en":"the conditions, objects, and forces that surround a person, animal, or thing","core_image":"围在人身外的一圈：空气、水、人、规则都在圈里","scene":"The biologist recorded the temperature and humidity of the forest environment.","sceneCN":"这里 environment 是「（生物所处的）环境条件」（第 3 个义项：生物生活的周围条件）；句意：生物学家记录了森林环境的温度和湿度。图中可辨识物件：温湿度计、森林、记录本、树冠与苔藓。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"环境；周围状况"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the natural environment","zh":"自然环境"},{"phrase":"protect the environment","zh":"保护环境"},{"phrase":"a learning environment","zh":"学习环境"},{"phrase":"environmental protection","zh":"环境保护"},{"phrase":"environment variables","zh":"环境变量"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"environments"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"environmental","pos":"adj.","zh":"环境的；周围状况的"},{"word":"environmentally","pos":"adv.","zh":"在环境方面；环保地"},{"word":"environmentalist","pos":"n.","zh":"环境保护主义者"},{"word":"environmentalism","pos":"n.","zh":"环境保护主义"},{"word":"environs","pos":"n.","zh":"（城镇的）周边地区；近郊"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The act of surrounding: what lies around","titleCN":"环绕：围在四周的东西","definition":"the conditions, objects, or forces that surround a person, animal, or thing","definitionCN":"环绕着人、动物或事物的条件、物体或力量","example":"The laboratory environment must be kept free of dust.","exampleCN":"实验室环境必须保持无尘。","why":"Environ came from Old French environer 'to surround', built on viron 'a circle'. Environment first named the state of being encircled, then the things doing the encircling.","whyCN":"environ 来自古法语 environer“环绕”，建立在 viron“圆圈”上。environment 最初指“被围住的状态”，随后指做包围的那些东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"The natural world: air, water, land, and life","titleCN":"自然世界：空气、水、土地与生命","definition":"the natural world, especially as affected by human activity","definitionCN":"自然世界，尤指受到人类活动影响时","example":"Plastic waste is one of the biggest threats to the environment.","exampleCN":"塑料垃圾是对环境的最大威胁之一。","why":"From the 1950s ecology gave the surrounding circle a planetary meaning: the whole natural system that surrounds and supports life.","whyCN":"20 世纪 50 年代起，生态学给了这个包围圈一层行星级含义：围绕并支撑生命的整个自然系统。"},{"no":"03","title":"Living conditions: where an organism lives","titleCN":"生存条件：生物生活的地方","definition":"the conditions in which a person, animal, or plant lives or operates","definitionCN":"人、动物或植物生活或运作所处的条件","example":"Cacti grow well in a dry environment.","exampleCN":"仙人掌在干燥环境中长得好。","why":"For a living thing, the circle that surrounds it is made of climate, food, and shelter; the general surround narrows to a habitat.","whyCN":"对生物来说，围住它的那个圈由气候、食物和庇护所构成；泛泛的“周围”缩小成了栖息环境。"},{"no":"04","title":"Social and cultural surroundings","titleCN":"社会与文化氛围","definition":"the social, cultural, or economic conditions that shape behaviour","definitionCN":"塑造行为的社会、文化或经济条件","example":"Children raised in a bilingual environment switch languages easily.","exampleCN":"在双语环境中长大的孩子切换语言很轻松。","why":"People are surrounded by customs as much as by air. The circle becomes social, so environment names the culture that shapes a person.","whyCN":"人既被空气包围，也被习俗包围。这个圈变成社会的，于是 environment 指塑造一个人的文化。"},{"no":"05","title":"Learning environment: conditions for study","titleCN":"学习环境：学习的条件","definition":"in education, the physical and social conditions in which learning takes place","definitionCN":"教育中指学习发生的物理与社会条件","example":"A quiet environment helps students concentrate.","exampleCN":"安静的环境有助于学生集中注意力。","why":"Classrooms are a designed circle: lighting, noise, and relationships together set what a learner can do.","whyCN":"教室是一个被设计出来的圈：灯光、噪音和人际关系共同决定学习者能做什么。"},{"no":"06","title":"Computing environment: the system a program runs in","titleCN":"计算环境：程序运行所在的系统","definition":"in computing, the hardware and software conditions in which a program runs","definitionCN":"计算机领域指程序运行所依赖的硬件与软件条件","example":"The old software will not run in a 64-bit environment.","exampleCN":"这个旧软件无法在 64 位环境中运行。","why":"A program is surrounded by an operating system and settings; computing simply names that technical circle with the same word.","whyCN":"程序被操作系统和各项设置包围；计算机领域只是用同一个词命名这个技术性的圈。"},{"no":"07","title":"The environment as a policy object","titleCN":"作为政策对象的环境","definition":"the environment, with the definite article, as the target of protection and regulation","definitionCN":"带定冠词时，指保护与监管的对象","example":"The agency was created to protect the environment.","exampleCN":"这个机构是为了保护环境而设立的。","why":"Once the natural circle is threatened, it becomes a thing to defend; the definite article marks the shared surroundings of all people.","whyCN":"一旦自然之圈受到威胁，它就变成要捍卫的对象；定冠词标记的是所有人共享的周围世界。"},{"no":"08","title":"Business or market environment","titleCN":"商业或市场环境","definition":"the conditions under which a company or market operates","definitionCN":"公司或市场运作所处的条件","example":"Low interest rates created a favourable environment for startups.","exampleCN":"低利率为初创企业创造了有利的环境。","why":"Firms are surrounded by prices, rules, and rivals. The same circle, drawn around a market, gives the business sense.","whyCN":"公司被价格、规则和对手包围。把同一个圈画在市场周围，就得到商业义。"},{"no":"09","title":"Environment vs surroundings: the whole set, not the items","titleCN":"environment 与 surroundings：整体条件，而非物件清单","definition":"the total set of conditions, as opposed to surroundings, which stresses the nearby objects","definitionCN":"条件的整体集合，与强调附近物件的 surroundings 相对","example":"The patient's whole environment, not just the ward, affected recovery.","exampleCN":"影响病人康复的是他的整个环境，而不只是病房。","why":"Environment names the enclosing system as a whole; surroundings counts the things nearby. The -ment ending marks the state of being surrounded, not a list of objects.","whyCN":"environment 命名整个包围系统；surroundings 数的是附近的物件。-ment 词尾标记“被包围的状态”，而不是一份物件清单。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Environment began around 1600 as 'the state of being surrounded'. It grew from the verb environ 'to surround', and only in the 19th and 20th centuries did it become the word for natural and social conditions.","cn":"environment 约 1600 年以“被环绕的状态”出现。它由动词 environ“环绕”生长而来，直到 19、20 世纪才成为表示自然与社会条件的词。"},"items":[{"era":"C. 1600","en":"First recorded meaning 'state of being environed', a noun of state built on the verb environ plus -ment.","cn":"最早记录义为“被环绕的状态”，是由动词 environ 加 -ment 构成的状态名词。"},{"era":"LATE 14C. ENVIRON","en":"The verb environ 'to surround, encircle' is recorded in late 14th-century English.","cn":"动词 environ“环绕、围住”记录于 14 世纪晚期的英语。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French environer, from environ 'around' = en- 'in' + viron 'circle, circuit', from virer 'to turn'.","cn":"来自古法语 environer，源自 environ“周围”= en-“内”+ viron“圆圈、一圈”，后者来自 virer“转”。"},{"era":"1827","en":"The sense 'the conditions in which a person or thing lives' is recorded in 1827, when Carlyle used it to translate German Umgebung.","cn":"“人或物所处条件的总和”这一义项记录于 1827 年，卡莱尔用它翻译德语 Umgebung。"},{"era":"1956","en":"Ecology gives 'the natural world' its modern currency from 1956, and the environmental movement spreads it further.","cn":"生态学从 1956 年起让“自然世界”义流行起来，环保运动又把它传播得更广。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English extends environment to computing and business; the old verb survives mainly in the plural noun environs, 'the outskirts'.","cn":"现代英语把 environment 扩展到计算机与商业领域；旧动词主要保留在复数名词 environs“近郊”中。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"environs","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənz/","tag":"plural noun","definition":"the area around a town or place. It names the outskirts, not the total conditions.","definitionCN":"城镇周边的地区；近郊。它指外围地带，而不是条件的总和。"},{"word":"environmental","ipa":"/ɪnˌvaɪrənˈmentl/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"relating to the environment. It is the adjective formed from the noun.","definitionCN":"环境的；与环境有关的。它是由该名词构成的形容词。"},{"word":"environ","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrən/","tag":"rare verb","definition":"to surround, a rare formal verb. Environment is the noun built from it with -ment.","definitionCN":"环绕；围住，是罕用的正式动词。environment 是它加 -ment 构成的名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"surroundings","ipa":"/səˈraʊndɪŋz/","tag":"nearby things","definition":"the things and conditions near someone. It counts nearby objects, while environment names the whole system.","definitionCN":"周围的事物与条件。它数的是附近物件，而 environment 指整个系统。"},{"word":"setting","ipa":"/ˈsetɪŋ/","tag":"background","definition":"the place or background where something happens. It is narrower and often used of stories or scenes.","definitionCN":"某事发生的地点或背景。它更窄，常用于故事或场景。"},{"word":"habitat","ipa":"/ˈhæbɪtæt/","tag":"species home","definition":"the natural home of a plant or animal. It is a biologist's term for one species' environment.","definitionCN":"动植物的天然栖息地。它是生物学术语，指某一物种的环境。"},{"word":"milieu","ipa":"/mɪˈljuː/","tag":"social background","definition":"the social and cultural background of a person or group. It is literary and almost always social.","definitionCN":"个人或群体的社会文化背景。它偏文学，几乎总指社会层面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: environ plus -ment, the viron 'circle' inside the word, and the surviving relatives environ, environs and environmental.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：environ + -ment、词内的 viron“圆圈”，以及仍活着的同族词 environ、environs、environmental。"},"normal":[{"en":"environ means 'to surround', and -ment turns the action into a state: environment is the state of being surrounded.","cn":"environ 意为“环绕”，-ment 把动作变成状态：environment 就是“被围住的状态”。"},{"en":"viron meant 'circle, circuit' in Old French, and virer 'to turn' is the same source as English veer.","cn":"viron 在古法语中意为“圆圈、一圈”，而 virer“转”与英语 veer 同源。"},{"en":"environs keeps the old verb alive: it means the area that circles a town.","cn":"environs 让旧动词继续活着：它指环绕城镇的那片外围地区。"},{"en":"environmental, environmentally, environmentalist and environmentalism are the modern derivatives built on the noun.","cn":"environmental、environmentally、environmentalist、environmentalism 都是在这个名词上构成的现代派生词。"},{"en":"the environment, with the definite article, is the shared natural circle that policy tries to protect.","cn":"带定冠词的 the environment，是政策试图保护的那个共享自然之圈。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Draw a circle around a body: inside it put air, water, food, people and rules.","cn":"在一个身体周围画一个圈：圈里放空气、水、食物、人和规则。"},{"en":"The same circle can shrink to a classroom, a lab, or a server, and expand to the whole planet.","cn":"同一个圈可以缩小到一间教室、一间实验室或一台服务器，也可以扩大到整个星球。"},{"en":"What surrounds also shapes: the circle is not a backdrop but a set of forces acting on what lives inside.","cn":"包围者也在塑造：这个圈不是背景板，而是一组作用于圈内生命的力量。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The desert environment is harsh for both plants and animals.","cn":"沙漠环境对植物和动物都很严酷。"},{"en":"She grew up in an environment where books were always available.","cn":"她在书籍随手可及的环境中长大。"},{"en":"The program stores its settings in an environment file.","cn":"该程序把设置保存在一个环境文件里。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「因围门」——因为四周都围上了门，圈出一块地方 → environment 环境、周围状况","word":"environment"},"root":"源自古法语 environ“环绕”= en-“内”+ viron“圆圈”← virer“转”，核心是“围在人或物外面的一圈条件”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of environment all come from one circle drawn around a person, animal, or thing. The circle can shrink to a room or a server, or expand to the whole natural world.","cn":"environment 的九个义项都来自画在人、动物或事物外面的同一个圈。这个圈可以缩小到一间房或一台服务器，也可以扩大到整个自然世界。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a circle drawn around a body, holding air, water, people and rules.","cn":"核心意象：围绕一个身体画出的圈，圈里装着空气、水、人与规则。"},"chain":["SURROUND","DRAW A CIRCLE","CONDITIONS AROUND","NATURAL WORLD","TOTAL SETTING","WHAT SHAPES LIFE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S9","en":"THE CIRCLE ITSELF: the state of being surrounded, and the total set as opposed to a list of nearby objects.","cn":"圈本身：被包围的状态，以及相对于附近物件清单的整体条件。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"NATURE AND HABITAT: the planetary natural system, and the narrower conditions in which one organism lives.","cn":"自然与栖息地：行星级的自然系统，以及某一生物生活的较窄条件。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"PEOPLE AND LEARNING: social and cultural surroundings, and the designed conditions of a classroom.","cn":"人与学习：社会文化氛围，以及教室这类被设计的学习条件。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"TECHNICAL AND MARKET CIRCLES: the system around a program, and the conditions around a firm.","cn":"技术与市场之圈：程序周围的系统，以及公司周围的条件。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"POLICY: the shared natural circle becomes a thing the state protects.","cn":"政策：共享的自然之圈变成国家保护的对象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Environment is en- plus viron 'circle' plus -ment, a noun of state. English builds environmental, environmentally, environmentalist and environmentalism on top, and keeps the bare verb environ.","cn":"environment 是 en- + viron“圆圈”+ -ment 构成的状态名词。英语在其上构成 environmental、environmentally、environmentalist、environmentalism，并保留光秃的动词 environ。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no reliable Latin ancestor to list. The word comes from Old French environer, and the deeper origin of viron and virer is uncertain, with only a possible link to Latin vibrare 'to shake'.","cn":"没有可靠的拉丁祖先可列。这个词来自古法语 environer，viron 与 virer 的更深来源不确定，只有与拉丁语 vibrare“摇动”的可能联系。"},"items":[{"word":"environment","structure":"en- (in) + viron (circle) + -ment (state noun)","meaning":"the state of being surrounded; the surrounding conditions","meaningCN":"被环绕的状态；周围条件（-ment 构成状态名词）","example":"A calm environment helps children learn.","exampleCN":"平静的环境有助于孩子学习。"},{"word":"environ","structure":"en- (in) + viron (circle)","meaning":"to surround, to encircle","meaningCN":"环绕；围住（罕用的正式动词）","example":"Tall hedges environ the old garden.","exampleCN":"高高的树篱环绕着这座老花园。"},{"word":"environs","structure":"environ + -s (plural)","meaning":"the surrounding area, the outskirts","meaningCN":"周边地区；近郊（-s 构成复数名词）","example":"Many commuters live in the environs of the city.","exampleCN":"许多通勤者住在城市近郊。"},{"word":"environmental","structure":"environment + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to the environment","meaningCN":"环境的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The report lists the main environmental risks.","exampleCN":"报告列出了主要的环境风险。"},{"word":"environmentally","structure":"environmental + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in relation to the environment","meaningCN":"在环境方面；环保地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The building is environmentally friendly.","exampleCN":"这栋建筑对环境友好。"},{"word":"environmentalist","structure":"environmental + -ist (person)","meaning":"a person who works to protect the environment","meaningCN":"环境保护主义者（-ist 表示人）","example":"The environmentalist opposed the new road.","exampleCN":"那位环保人士反对修建新公路。"},{"word":"environmentalism","structure":"environmental + -ism (doctrine)","meaning":"the movement to protect the natural world","meaningCN":"环境保护主义（-ism 表示主义、运动）","example":"Environmentalism grew quickly in the 1970s.","exampleCN":"环境保护主义在 20 世纪 70 年代迅速发展。"},{"word":"veer","structure":"virer (to turn) > veer","meaning":"to change direction suddenly","meaningCN":"突然转向（与 virer“转”同源）","example":"The boat veered away from the rocks.","exampleCN":"小船突然转向，避开了礁石。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"equivalent","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/","definition_zh":"相等的；等价的；相当的；对应物；等值物","definition_en":"equal in value, function, or meaning to something else","core_image":"天平两端放上形状不同、却正好等重的东西","scene":"One kilogram is equivalent to about 2.2 pounds.","sceneCN":"这里 equivalent 是「（数值上）等值」（第 1 个义项：价值或数量相等）；句意：一千克约等于 2.2 磅。图中可辨识物件：天平、千克砝码、磅砝码、换算表。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"相等的；等价的；相当的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"等价物；对应物；等值物"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"be equivalent to","zh":"等同于；相当于"},{"phrase":"the equivalent of","zh":"……的等价物"},{"phrase":"roughly equivalent","zh":"大致相当"},{"phrase":"equivalent value","zh":"等值"},{"phrase":"logically equivalent","zh":"逻辑等价的"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"equivalents"},{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more equivalent"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most equivalent"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"equivalence","pos":"n.","zh":"相等；等价"},{"word":"equivalently","pos":"adv.","zh":"等价地；同样地"},{"word":"equivalency","pos":"n.","zh":"等价；等效（常指学历或资格的等同）"},{"word":"inequivalent","pos":"adj.","zh":"不等价的；不相等的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Equal in value: the same worth","titleCN":"价值相等：同样的分量","definition":"having the same value, amount, or significance as something else","definitionCN":"在价值、数量或意义上与另一事物相同","example":"One mile is equivalent to about 1.6 kilometres.","exampleCN":"一英里约等于 1.6 公里。","why":"Late Latin aequivalentem joined aequus 'equal' to valere 'to be worth'. The core is equal worth, not equal shape.","whyCN":"晚期拉丁语 aequivalentem 把 aequus“相等”与 valere“有价值”结合起来。核心是价值相等，而不是形状相同。"},{"no":"02","title":"Equal in function: doing the same job","titleCN":"功能相等：承担同样的作用","definition":"having the same function or effect as something else","definitionCN":"与另一事物具有相同的功能或效果","example":"A smartphone is equivalent to a pocket computer.","exampleCN":"智能手机相当于一台口袋电脑。","why":"Value can be measured by what a thing does. When two objects do the same job, their worth matches even if their form differs.","whyCN":"价值可以按一个东西能做什么来衡量。当两个物件承担同样的作用，即使形态不同，它们的分量也相当。"},{"no":"03","title":"Equal in meaning: the translation test","titleCN":"意义相等：翻译的检验","definition":"of words or statements, having the same meaning in another language or form","definitionCN":"（词语或说法）在另一种语言或形式中具有相同意义","example":"The French phrase has no exact English equivalent.","exampleCN":"这个法语短语在英语中没有完全对应的说法。","why":"Meaning is a kind of value. A translation is equivalent when it carries the same sense, not the same sounds.","whyCN":"意义也是一种价值。译文若承载同样的意思，就是 equivalent；它不要求声音相同。"},{"no":"04","title":"Noun: the counterpart with the same worth","titleCN":"名词：分量相同的对应物","definition":"a thing that has the same value, function, or meaning as another","definitionCN":"在价值、功能或意义上与另一事物相同的东西","example":"She earns the equivalent of a year's rent in a month.","exampleCN":"她一个月挣的钱相当于一年的房租。","why":"The adjective became a noun around 1500: the equivalent is the thing standing on the other side of the balance.","whyCN":"这个形容词约 1500 年转为名词：the equivalent 就是站在天平另一端的那件东西。"},{"no":"05","title":"Academic: matched conditions in an experiment","titleCN":"学术：实验中条件匹配","definition":"of groups or conditions, made equal in relevant respects so a comparison is fair","definitionCN":"（群体或条件）在相关方面被拉平，使比较公平","example":"The two groups were equivalent in age and prior training.","exampleCN":"两组在年龄和先前训练上相当。","why":"An experiment needs its pans balanced. Researchers make groups equivalent by removing every difference except the one being tested.","whyCN":"实验需要天平两侧平衡。研究者通过去掉被测因素之外的所有差异，让各组变得 equivalent。"},{"no":"06","title":"Logical equivalence: same truth value","titleCN":"逻辑等价：真值相同","definition":"in logic, having the same truth conditions, so each follows from the other","definitionCN":"逻辑中指真值条件相同，因此各自都能推出对方","example":"The two statements are logically equivalent.","exampleCN":"这两个陈述在逻辑上等价。","why":"Logic measures value as truth. Two claims are equivalent when neither can be true while the other is false.","whyCN":"逻辑把价值衡量为真值。两个命题 equivalent，指的是不可能一个真而另一个假。"},{"no":"07","title":"Chemistry: a combining amount","titleCN":"化学：化合当量","definition":"in chemistry, the amount of a substance that combines with or replaces one unit of another","definitionCN":"化学中指能与一个单位的另一物质化合或取代它的量","example":"One equivalent of acid neutralized the base.","exampleCN":"一当量酸中和了这种碱。","why":"Chemistry counts worth as combining power: an equivalent is the quantity that exactly matches another substance's capacity.","whyCN":"化学把价值算作化合能力：equivalent 就是恰好匹配另一物质能力的数量。"},{"no":"08","title":"Equivalent vs equal: worth against quantity","titleCN":"equivalent 与 equal：论价值，还是论数量","definition":"having the same worth or role, in contrast with equal, which stresses the same number or degree","definitionCN":"具有相同的价值或作用，与强调数目或程度相同的 equal 相对","example":"The two cups are equal in volume, but a cup and a glass are equivalent for holding water.","exampleCN":"两个杯子容量相等，但杯子和玻璃杯在盛水这件事上是相当的。","why":"Aequus gives both words, but equal keeps the plain 'same measure' and equivalent adds valere 'be worth': equal counts, equivalent weighs.","whyCN":"两个词都出自 aequus，但 equal 保留朴素的“同一量度”，equivalent 则加上 valere“有价值”：equal 数数，equivalent 称重。"},{"no":"09","title":"The equivalent of: one thing in another's form","titleCN":"the equivalent of：同一件事换一种形式","definition":"in the phrase the equivalent of, the same thing expressed in a different form or unit","definitionCN":"用于 the equivalent of，表示同一件事以不同形式或单位表达","example":"For a plant, a drought is the equivalent of a long fast for an animal.","exampleCN":"对植物来说，干旱相当于动物长时间的禁食。","why":"The phrase sets two different kinds of thing on the same scale, saying that in this respect they weigh the same.","whyCN":"这个短语把两类不同事物放到同一架天平上，说在这一层面上它们分量相同。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Equivalent came from Late Latin aequivalentem, 'of equal worth', formed from aequus 'equal' and valere 'to be worth'. It entered English as an adjective in the early 15th century and as a noun around 1500. Aequus itself is of unknown origin in standard references, so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"equivalent 来自晚期拉丁语 aequivalentem“等值”，由 aequus“相等”与 valere“有价值”构成。它于 15 世纪早期以形容词进入英语，约 1500 年又作名词。aequus 自身的更早来源在通行资料中不明，故最深层来源不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"EARLY 15C.","en":"Equivalent is first recorded in English as an adjective meaning 'equal in value or worth'.","cn":"equivalent 最早在英语中记录为形容词，意为“价值相等”。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN","en":"From Late Latin aequivalentem 'of equal worth' = aequus 'equal' + valere 'to be worth, be strong'.","cn":"来自晚期拉丁语 aequivalentem“等值”= aequus“相等”+ valere“有价值、强健”。"},{"era":"C. 1500 NOUN","en":"The noun use is recorded around 1500, naming the thing that has equal value.","cn":"名词用法约 1500 年出现，指具有相等价值的那件东西。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Valere goes back to PIE *wal- 'be strong', the same root behind value, valid, prevail, valiant and ambivalent.","cn":"valere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *wal-“强”，同一词根也支撑 value、valid、prevail、valiant、ambivalent。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses equivalent for worth, function, meaning and logic; equal keeps the plain 'same measure'.","cn":"现代英语用 equivalent 表示价值、功能、意义与逻辑上的相当；equal 保留朴素的“同一量度”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning. The equal entry states the difference that the word pair keeps testing.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选。equal 一条点明这对词反复被考查的差别。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"equivalence","ipa":"/ɪˈkwɪvələns/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the state of being equivalent. It is the noun, while equivalent is the adjective or the thing itself.","definitionCN":"等价；相等状态。它是名词，而 equivalent 是形容词或那件东西本身。"},{"word":"equivocal","ipa":"/ɪˈkwɪvəʊkəl/","tag":"shared equi-","definition":"unclear or ambiguous. It shares equi- but comes from vocare 'to call', so it means 'two voices', not equal worth.","definitionCN":"含糊的；模棱两可的。它同样以 equi- 开头，但来自 vocare“呼叫”，意为“两个声音”，与等值无关。"},{"word":"equilibrium","ipa":"/ˌiːkwɪˈlɪbriəm/","tag":"shared equi-","definition":"a state of balance. It joins aequus with libra 'scales', and names balance rather than equal worth.","definitionCN":"平衡状态。它把 aequus 与 libra“天平”结合，命名的是平衡而非等值。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"equal","ipa":"/ˈiːkwəl/","tag":"same measure","definition":"the same in number, size, or degree. It counts and measures, while equivalent weighs worth or function.","definitionCN":"在数目、大小或程度上相同。它数数量、量程度，而 equivalent 称价值或功能。"},{"word":"comparable","ipa":"/ˈkɒmpərəbl/","tag":"similar enough","definition":"able to be compared, often similar in size or quality. It stops short of saying the worth is the same.","definitionCN":"可比较的，常指大小或质量相近。它没有说到“价值相同”这一步。"},{"word":"counterpart","ipa":"/ˈkaʊntəpɑːt/","tag":"matching item","definition":"a person or thing with the same role in another place or system. It names the matching item, not the equality of value.","definitionCN":"在另一地或另一体系中角色相同的人或物。它命名的是对应项，而不是价值的相等。"},{"word":"tantamount","ipa":"/ˈtæntəməʊnt/","tag":"equal in effect","definition":"equivalent in effect, usually of something bad. It is formal and almost always followed by to.","definitionCN":"效果上等同于，通常指不好的事。它偏正式，几乎总接 to。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: equi- 'equal' plus val- 'be worth', the valere family of value and valid, and the equal versus equivalent contrast.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：equi-“相等”+ val-“有价值”、value 与 valid 的 valere 词族，以及 equal 与 equivalent 的对比。"},"normal":[{"en":"equi- means 'equal' and val- means 'be worth', so equivalent literally says 'of equal worth'.","cn":"equi- 意为“相等”，val- 意为“有价值”，所以 equivalent 字面就是“价值相等”。"},{"en":"valere gives value, valid, prevail, valiant and ambivalent, all built on the idea of strength or worth.","cn":"valere 给出 value、valid、prevail、valiant、ambivalent，它们都建立在“力量或价值”这一概念上。"},{"en":"equivalence is the noun and equivalently the adverb; equivalency often names official equivalence of qualifications.","cn":"equivalence 是名词，equivalently 是副词；equivalency 常指学历或资格的官方等同。"},{"en":"be equivalent to is the standard frame, used for units, functions and meanings alike.","cn":"be equivalent to 是标准框架，单位、功能和意义都可以用它。"},{"en":"equal and equivalent share aequus, but equal measures quantity while equivalent weighs worth.","cn":"equal 与 equivalent 同出 aequus，但 equal 量数量，equivalent 称价值。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two pans of a balance holding objects of different shape and the same weight.","cn":"想象天平的两个托盘里放着形状不同、重量相同的物件。"},{"en":"Translation is the same balance: a sentence in another language is placed on the other pan.","cn":"翻译就是同一架天平：把另一种语言里的句子放到另一个托盘上。"},{"en":"Swapping units does not change the amount; it only changes the label on the same weight.","cn":"换算单位不改变分量，只是换了同一个重量上的标签。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A week of hard work is equivalent to a month of steady effort.","cn":"一周的苦干相当于一个月的持续努力。"},{"en":"There is no exact equivalent for this word in English.","cn":"这个词在英语中没有完全对应的说法。"},{"en":"The two qualifications are regarded as equivalent by most employers.","cn":"大多数雇主认为这两种资格是等同的。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一魁万两」——一魁（一堆）抵得上万两银子，价值对等 → equivalent 等价的、相当的","word":"equivalent"},"root":"源自晚期拉丁语 aequivalentem = aequus“相等”+ valere“有价值”，核心是“价值相等，而不只是数量相等”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of equivalent all stand on one balance: two things of different shape, but the same value, function, or meaning.","cn":"equivalent 的九个义项都站在同一架天平上：两样形状不同的东西，在价值、功能或意义上分量相同。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a balance holding two unlike objects that weigh the same.","cn":"核心意象：一架天平，两端放着形状不同却等重的东西。"},"chain":["EQUAL MEASURE","EQUAL WORTH","MATCH FUNCTION","MATCH MEANING","BALANCE THE PANS","SAME IN ANOTHER FORM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"WORTH ON THE BALANCE: equal value, and the thing that sits on the other pan.","cn":"天平上的价值：相等的价值，以及坐在另一托盘上的那件东西。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"FUNCTION AND MEANING: doing the same job, and carrying the same sense in another language.","cn":"功能与意义：承担同样的作用，以及在另一种语言中承载同样的意思。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"ACADEMIC BALANCE: matched groups in an experiment, and matched truth values in logic.","cn":"学术上的平衡：实验中条件匹配的组，以及逻辑中真值相同的命题。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"CHEMICAL MATCH: the amount that exactly matches another substance's combining power.","cn":"化学上的匹配：恰好匹配另一物质化合能力的量。"},{"senses":"S8 · S9","en":"THE PHRASE AT WORK: equal counts while equivalent weighs, and the equivalent of puts one thing in another's form.","cn":"短语的运作：equal 数数而 equivalent 称重；the equivalent of 把一件事换成另一种形式。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Equivalent is equi- 'equal' plus val- 'be worth' plus -ent. The equi- branch also gives equal and equate, and the val- branch gives value, valid, prevail and ambivalent.","cn":"equivalent 是 equi-“相等”+ val-“有价值”+ -ent 构成。equi- 这一支也给出 equal 与 equate，val- 这一支给出 value、valid、prevail、ambivalent。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Late Latin aequivalentem is built from aequus 'level, equal' and valere 'be strong, be worth'; aequus also gives aequalitas, and valere gives valor and validus.","cn":"晚期拉丁语 aequivalentem 由 aequus“平的、相等”与 valere“强健、有价值”构成；aequus 也给出 aequalitas，valere 给出 valor 与 validus。"},"items":[{"word":"equivalent","structure":"equi- (equal) + val- (be worth) + -ent (adjective)","meaning":"of equal worth, function, or meaning","meaningCN":"价值、功能或意义相等的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"One dollar is equivalent to about seven yuan.","exampleCN":"一美元约相当于七元人民币。"},{"word":"equivalence","structure":"equivalent + -ence (noun)","meaning":"the state of being equivalent","meaningCN":"等价；相等（-ence 构成名词）","example":"The study tests the equivalence of the two methods.","exampleCN":"这项研究检验两种方法是否等价。"},{"word":"equivalently","structure":"equivalent + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in an equivalent way","meaningCN":"等价地；同样地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The two conditions can be stated equivalently.","exampleCN":"这两个条件可以用等价的方式表述。"},{"word":"equivalency","structure":"equivalent + -ency (noun)","meaning":"official equivalence, especially of qualifications","meaningCN":"等同；等效（常指学历或资格的官方等同）","example":"The board issued a certificate of equivalency.","exampleCN":"委员会颁发了一份同等学历证明。"},{"word":"inequivalent","structure":"in- (not) + equivalent","meaning":"not equivalent","meaningCN":"不等价的；不相等的（in- 表否定）","example":"The two samples were inequivalent in purity.","exampleCN":"这两个样本在纯度上并不等同。"},{"word":"equal","structure":"aequ- (level, equal) + -al (adjective)","meaning":"the same in measure or degree","meaningCN":"相等的；同等的（-al 构成形容词，强调同一量度）","example":"The two ropes are equal in length.","exampleCN":"两条绳子长度相等。"},{"word":"equate","structure":"equ- (equal) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to treat as equal","meaningCN":"使等同；把……视为相等（-ate 构成动词）","example":"Do not equate wealth with happiness.","exampleCN":"不要把财富等同于幸福。"},{"word":"equation","structure":"equate + -ion (noun)","meaning":"a statement that two expressions are equal","meaningCN":"方程式；等式（-ion 构成名词）","example":"Solve the equation for x.","exampleCN":"解这个方程求 x。"},{"word":"value","structure":"val- (be worth) + -ue (noun)","meaning":"the worth of something","meaningCN":"价值（val- 表有价值）","example":"The value of the house has doubled.","exampleCN":"这栋房子的价值翻了一番。"},{"word":"valid","structure":"val- (be strong) + -id (adjective)","meaning":"sound and acceptable","meaningCN":"有效的；正当的（val- 表强健、有力）","example":"Your ticket is valid for one month.","exampleCN":"你的票一个月内有效。"},{"word":"prevail","structure":"pre- (before) + vail (valere, be strong)","meaning":"to prove stronger and win","meaningCN":"盛行；获胜（pre- 在前 + valere 强）","example":"Common sense finally prevailed.","exampleCN":"常识最终占了上风。"},{"word":"ambivalent","structure":"ambi- (both) + val- (be strong) + -ent","meaning":"having two opposing feelings at once","meaningCN":"矛盾的；有双重感受的（ambi- 两 + val- 强）","example":"She felt ambivalent about moving abroad.","exampleCN":"她对移居国外心情矛盾。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"aequivalentem","structure":"aequus + valere + -entem","meaning":"of equal worth","meaningCN":"等值的；价值相等的"},{"word":"aequus","structure":"aequus (adjective)","meaning":"level, even, equal","meaningCN":"平的；均等的；相等的"},{"word":"valere","structure":"valere (verb)","meaning":"to be strong, to be worth","meaningCN":"强健；有价值"},{"word":"aequalitas","structure":"aequus + -itas","meaning":"equality, evenness","meaningCN":"平等；均等"}]}},{"word":"establish","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/","definition_zh":"建立；设立；确立；证实；确定","definition_en":"to set up something on a firm basis, or to prove that something is true","core_image":"把一根柱子立进地里，让它站住不倒","scene":"The university established a new research centre beside the river.","sceneCN":"这里 establish 是「建立、设立」（第 1 个义项：把机构或制度设立起来）；句意：这所大学在河边建立了一个新的研究中心。图中可辨识物件：研究中心的招牌、施工围挡、河岸、奠基仪式的人群。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"建立；设立；确立；证实"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"establish a company","zh":"创办公司"},{"phrase":"establish relations with","zh":"与……建立关系"},{"phrase":"establish the fact that","zh":"证实……这一事实"},{"phrase":"establish a reputation","zh":"确立声誉"},{"phrase":"the established order","zh":"既定秩序"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"establishes"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"established"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"established"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"establishing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"establishment","pos":"n.","zh":"建立；机构；当权派"},{"word":"established","pos":"adj.","zh":"已确立的；既定的"},{"word":"establishable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可建立的；可证实的"},{"word":"establisher","pos":"n.","zh":"创立者；建立者"},{"word":"stability","pos":"n.","zh":"稳定；稳固（同出 stabilis 词族）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Set up on a firm footing: create an institution","titleCN":"立稳根基：创建机构","definition":"to set up an organization, system, or rule on a lasting basis","definitionCN":"在持久的基础上建立组织、制度或规则","example":"The city established a new public library in 1920.","exampleCN":"该市于 1920 年建立了一座新的公共图书馆。","why":"Latin stabilire 'to make firm' came from stabilis 'steady', from stare 'to stand'. Establishing is first of all making something stand.","whyCN":"拉丁语 stabilire“使稳固”来自 stabilis“稳固”，再来自 stare“站立”。establish 首先是让某物站住。"},{"no":"02","title":"Prove a fact: make it stand as true","titleCN":"证实事实：让它站得住","definition":"to prove or confirm something so that it is accepted as true","definitionCN":"证明或确认某事，使其被接受为真","example":"The study established that the drug was safe.","exampleCN":"这项研究证实了这种药物是安全的。","why":"A fact stands when evidence holds it up. The same image of standing passes from buildings to claims.","whyCN":"事实有证据支撑才站得住。同一个“站立”的意象从建筑转到了主张上。"},{"no":"03","title":"Determine the cause or facts","titleCN":"查明原因与事实","definition":"to find out and confirm the details of an event","definitionCN":"查明并确认某一事件的细节","example":"Investigators established the cause of the fire.","exampleCN":"调查人员查明了火灾的起因。","why":"An investigation puts an explanation on its feet: before it is established, the cause is only a guess that cannot stand.","whyCN":"调查让一个解释站稳：在被 establish 之前，原因只是一个站不住的猜测。"},{"no":"04","title":"Begin a pattern: establish a relationship or custom","titleCN":"开创模式：建立关系或惯例","definition":"to begin something that is meant to continue, such as a relationship or custom","definitionCN":"开始一件打算持续下去的事，如关系或惯例","example":"The two countries established diplomatic relations in 1972.","exampleCN":"两国于 1972 年建立外交关系。","why":"Relations are structures too: once begun and accepted, they stand between the parties.","whyCN":"关系也是一种结构：一旦开始并被接受，它就立在双方之间。"},{"no":"05","title":"Establish a reputation: build a standing","titleCN":"确立声誉：积累立足之地","definition":"to gain recognition for a quality over time","definitionCN":"随着时间推移因某种品质而获得认可","example":"She established a reputation for careful research.","exampleCN":"她以严谨研究确立了声誉。","why":"A reputation is a standing in other people's eyes. The verb builds that standing by repeated proof.","whyCN":"声誉是他在别人眼中的“站立高度”。这个动词通过反复证明来搭建这种站立。"},{"no":"06","title":"Establish oneself: settle into a place or role","titleCN":"安身立命：在某个地方或角色中扎根","definition":"to become accepted and settled in a place, profession, or community","definitionCN":"在一个地方、行业或群体中获得接纳并安定下来","example":"He established himself as a translator in London.","exampleCN":"他在伦敦当翻译站住了脚。","why":"Here the person, not the structure, is made to stand: settling means finding a stable place in a network.","whyCN":"这里被立稳的是人而不是结构：安顿下来就是在关系网中找到稳定的位置。"},{"no":"07","title":"Establish a right or claim: make it recognized","titleCN":"确立权利：使其获得承认","definition":"to make a legal right, claim, or principle officially recognized","definitionCN":"使法律权利、主张或原则获得官方承认","example":"The ruling established a right to clean water.","exampleCN":"该判决确立了一项获得清洁水的权利。","why":"Law gives a claim a footing it did not have before; once recognized, the right stands against later challenges.","whyCN":"法律给了主张一个此前没有的立足点；一旦获得承认，这项权利就能顶住后来的挑战。"},{"no":"08","title":"Established: long recognized and hard to change","titleCN":"established：久已确立、难以更改","definition":"of an adjective, long in place and accepted, sometimes resisting change","definitionCN":"作形容词时指长期存在并被接受，有时含抗拒改变之意","example":"The established church in England dates back to the sixteenth century.","exampleCN":"英格兰的国教可追溯到 16 世纪。","why":"What has stood a long time is 'established'. The established church is the one with legal standing, which is why the word can suggest tradition and authority.","whyCN":"站得久的东西就是 established。established church 指具有法律地位的国教，因此这个词能暗示传统与权威。"},{"no":"09","title":"Establish vs found: making it stand versus starting it","titleCN":"establish 与 found：立稳，还是开端","definition":"to make something secure and accepted, in contrast with found, which stresses the first moment of creating it","definitionCN":"使某物稳固并被接受，与强调“创造的第一刻”的 found 相对","example":"They founded the club in 1990 and spent a decade establishing it.","exampleCN":"他们于 1990 年创办了俱乐部，又花了十年让它站稳。","why":"Found marks the first stone; establish marks the building standing firm. The prefix e- in establish is not a meaning part, so the word's force comes from stabilis alone.","whyCN":"found 标记第一块石头，establish 标记建筑稳稳立住。establish 的词首 e- 不承载意义，这个词的力量完全来自 stabilis。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Establish came from Old French establir in the late 14th century, from Latin stabilire 'to make firm'. The initial e- was added in French and carries no meaning, as in estate.","cn":"establish 于 14 世纪晚期来自古法语 establir，再来自拉丁语 stabilire“使稳固”。词首 e- 是法语加的，不承载意义，estate 也是如此。"},"items":[{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"First recorded in English as 'set up, fix, make firm'.","cn":"最早在英语中记录为“设立、固定、使稳固”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH","en":"From Old French establiss-, present stem of establir 'make stable, set up, build'.","cn":"来自古法语 establiss-，即 establir“使稳定、设立、建造”的现在词干。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"From Latin stabilire 'to make firm', from stabilis 'firm, steady', from stare 'to stand'.","cn":"来自拉丁语 stabilire“使稳固”，再来自 stabilis“稳固的”，最终来自 stare“站立”。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"Stare goes back to PIE *sta- 'to stand', the root behind stand, stable, station and statue.","cn":"stare 可追溯到原始印欧语 *sta-“站立”，同一词根也支撑 stand、stable、station、statue。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The initial e- is not part of the root; it was added in French, as in estate. The established church means the church with legal standing.","cn":"词首 e- 不是词根的一部分，是法语加的，estate 亦然。established church 指具有法律地位的国教。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"establishment","ipa":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃmənt/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the act of establishing, or an organization that has been set up. It is the noun, not the verb.","definitionCN":"建立的行为，或已设立的组织。它是名词，不是动词。"},{"word":"stabilize","ipa":"/ˈsteɪbəlaɪz/","tag":"shared stabil-","definition":"to make something steady. It shares the stabil- root but means keeping balance, not setting up.","definitionCN":"使稳定。它同出 stabil- 词根，但意思是保持平衡，而不是设立。"},{"word":"estate","ipa":"/ɪˈsteɪt/","tag":"same added e-","definition":"a large piece of land or property. It carries the same added e- as establish, from stare 'to stand'.","definitionCN":"大片地产。它带着与 establish 相同的增音 e-，源出 stare“站立”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"found","ipa":"/faʊnd/","tag":"first moment","definition":"to start an organization or city. It marks the first moment, while establish adds lasting firmness.","definitionCN":"创办组织或建立城市。它标记最初一刻，而 establish 额外带有“持久稳固”。"},{"word":"institute","ipa":"/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt/","tag":"formal setup","definition":"to set up a formal system or organization. It is more official and narrower than establish.","definitionCN":"设立正式制度或组织。它比 establish 更官方、范围更窄。"},{"word":"prove","ipa":"/pruːv/","tag":"fact only","definition":"to show that something is true. It covers only the 'establish a fact' sense, not setting up institutions.","definitionCN":"证明某事为真。它只覆盖“证实事实”这一义项，不能指设立机构。"},{"word":"create","ipa":"/kriˈeɪt/","tag":"bring into being","definition":"to bring something into existence. It stresses the new thing, while establish stresses that it then stands firm.","definitionCN":"使某物产生。它强调新事物本身，而 establish 强调它随后稳稳站住。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the stabilis root, the stare family of stable and statue, the added e- shared with estate, and the legal phrase established church.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：stabilis 词根、stable 与 statue 的 stare 词族、与 estate 共享的增音 e-，以及法律短语 established church。"},"normal":[{"en":"stabilis means 'firm' and stare means 'to stand', so establish is literally 'make stand'.","cn":"stabilis 意为“稳固”，stare 意为“站立”，所以 establish 字面就是“使站住”。"},{"en":"stare also gives stable, stability, station and statue, all built on standing.","cn":"stare 也给出 stable、stability、station、statue，它们都建立在“站立”上。"},{"en":"The initial e- is not a prefix with meaning; French added it, and estate carries the same extra vowel.","cn":"词首 e- 不是有意义的前缀；法语加上它，estate 也带着同一个多余元音。"},{"en":"establishment is the noun and established the adjective; established custom means a custom long standing.","cn":"establishment 是名词，established 是形容词；established custom 指长期存在的习俗。"},{"en":"the established church means the church with legal standing, which is why the word can sound traditional and official.","cn":"the established church 指具有法律地位的国教，因此这个词听起来带传统与官方色彩。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a post driven into the ground and tested until it no longer leans.","cn":"想象一根柱子打进地里，反复校正，直到它不再倾斜。"},{"en":"Proof is the same post: a claim is established when evidence keeps it upright.","cn":"证明就是同一根柱子：证据能让主张保持直立，它才算 establish。"},{"en":"A reputation, a right, or a person can also be 'stood up' inside a network of other people.","cn":"声誉、权利或一个人，也可以在一张人际网络中“立起来”。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The school was established by a group of local farmers in 1890.","cn":"这所学校由一群当地农民于 1890 年创办。"},{"en":"The experiment established that the two gases react at room temperature.","cn":"实验证实这两种气体在室温下会反应。"},{"en":"She quickly established herself as the best editor on the team.","cn":"她很快在团队中确立了自己最佳编辑的地位。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一石立起」——一块石头立稳在地里，就算建立起来 → establish 建立、确立","word":"establish"},"root":"源自拉丁语 stabilire“使稳固”← stabilis“稳固”← stare“站立”；词首 e- 是法语增音，核心是“立稳”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of establish all come from one action: putting something into the ground so that it stands. Buildings, facts, reputations, rights and people are all made to stand the same way.","cn":"establish 的九个义项都来自同一个动作：把某物立进地里，让它站住。建筑、事实、声誉、权利和人，都是用同一种方式被立稳的。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a post driven into the ground and standing firm.","cn":"核心意象：一根打进地里、稳稳站住的柱子。"},"chain":["STAND","MAKE FIRM","SET UP","PROVE","GAIN STANDING","KEEP IN PLACE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"BUILDING AND BEGINNING: an institution or relation is set up so that it can stand over time.","cn":"建造与开端：机构或关系被设立起来，以便长期站住。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"PROOF: a fact or cause stands only when evidence holds it upright.","cn":"证明：事实或原因只有证据支撑才站得住。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"STANDING AMONG PEOPLE: a reputation is built in others' eyes, and a person settles into a network.","cn":"人群中的站立：声誉在他人眼中搭建，一个人在关系网中安顿。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"RECOGNITION: a right gains legal standing, and what has long stood becomes established.","cn":"承认：权利获得法律地位，长期站立的东西变成 established。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE CONTRAST: found marks the first stone, establish marks the building standing firm.","cn":"对比：found 标记第一块石头，establish 标记建筑稳稳立住。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Establish is e- (added in French, no meaning) plus stabil- 'firm' plus -ish. The stem also builds establishment and established, while stabilis gives stable, stability and stabilize.","cn":"establish 是 e-（法语增音，无意义）+ stabil-“稳固”+ -ish 构成。同一词干还构成 establishment、established，而 stabilis 给出 stable、stability、stabilize。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin stabilire 'to make firm' comes from stabilis 'firm', from stare 'to stand'. Stabilis also gives stabilimentum, and stare gives statio and statua.","cn":"拉丁语 stabilire“使稳固”来自 stabilis“稳固”，再来自 stare“站立”。stabilis 也给出 stabilimentum，stare 给出 statio 与 statua。"},"items":[{"word":"establish","structure":"e- (added) + stabil- (firm) + -ish (verb)","meaning":"to make firm, set up","meaningCN":"建立；使稳固（e- 为法语增音，-ish 构成动词）","example":"They established the rules at the first meeting.","exampleCN":"他们在第一次会议上确立了规则。"},{"word":"establishment","structure":"establish + -ment (noun)","meaning":"the act of setting up, or the organization set up","meaningCN":"建立；机构；权势集团（-ment 构成名词）","example":"The establishment of the fund took two years.","exampleCN":"该基金的设立花了两年。"},{"word":"established","structure":"establish + -ed (past participle as adjective)","meaning":"long set up and accepted","meaningCN":"已确立的；既定的（-ed 构成形容词）","example":"They moved away from the established route.","exampleCN":"他们偏离了既定路线。"},{"word":"establishable","structure":"establish + -able (adjective)","meaning":"able to be established or proved","meaningCN":"可建立的；可证实的（-able 表能够）","example":"The claim is not establishable from the data.","exampleCN":"这一主张无法由数据证实。"},{"word":"establisher","structure":"establish + -er (person who does)","meaning":"a person who establishes something","meaningCN":"创立者；建立者（-er 表示做该动作的人）","example":"The establisher of the charity remains unknown.","exampleCN":"这家慈善机构的创立者仍不为人知。"},{"word":"stable","structure":"stabilis (firm, steady)","meaning":"steady and not likely to change","meaningCN":"稳定的；稳固的（直接来自 stabilis）","example":"The patient is now in a stable condition.","exampleCN":"病人现在情况稳定。"},{"word":"stability","structure":"stable + -ity (noun)","meaning":"the state of being steady","meaningCN":"稳定；稳固（-ity 构成名词）","example":"The bridge was tested for stability.","exampleCN":"这座桥接受了稳定性测试。"},{"word":"stabilize","structure":"stable + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to make steady","meaningCN":"使稳定（-ize 构成动词）","example":"The crew stabilized the damaged hull.","exampleCN":"船员稳住了受损的船体。"},{"word":"stabilization","structure":"stabilize + -ation (noun)","meaning":"the act of making steady","meaningCN":"稳定化；稳固（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"The stabilization of the cliff took months.","exampleCN":"崖壁的加固花了数月。"},{"word":"unstable","structure":"un- (not) + stable","meaning":"not steady, likely to change","meaningCN":"不稳定的（un- 表否定）","example":"The ladder was unstable on the soft ground.","exampleCN":"梯子在松软的地面上不稳。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"stabilire","structure":"stabilis + -ire (verb)","meaning":"to make firm, establish","meaningCN":"使稳固；建立"},{"word":"stabilis","structure":"stabilis (adjective)","meaning":"firm, steady","meaningCN":"稳固的；稳定的"},{"word":"stare","structure":"stare (verb)","meaning":"to stand, to stay upright","meaningCN":"站立；立住"}]}},{"word":"estimate","ipa_uk":"/ˈestɪmeɪt/","ipa_us":"/ˈestɪmeɪt/","definition_zh":"估算；估计；评价；估价；报价单","definition_en":"to judge the approximate amount, value, or size of something from the information available, or such a judgment itself","core_image":"手边只有半张图纸，先按经验报出一个大概的数","scene":"The contractor looked at the half-built wall and said he could estimate the repair cost by Friday.","sceneCN":"这里 estimate 是「估算（成本）」（第 1 个义项：依据有限信息给出近似数值）；句意：承包商看了看砌了一半的墙，说他周五前能估算出维修费用。图中可辨识物件：砌了一半的砖墙、安全帽、卷尺、记事本上写着的数字。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"估算；估计；评价"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"估价；报价单；估计量"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a rough estimate","zh":"粗略的估计"},{"phrase":"estimate the cost","zh":"估算成本"},{"phrase":"at a conservative estimate","zh":"保守估计"},{"phrase":"a cost estimate","zh":"成本估算；报价单"},{"phrase":"estimate that","zh":"估计（认为）……"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"estimates"},{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"estimates"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"estimated"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"estimated"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"estimating"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"estimation","pos":"n.","zh":"估计；判断；评价"},{"word":"estimator","pos":"n.","zh":"估算者；（统计）估计量"},{"word":"estimable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可估计的；值得尊敬的"},{"word":"overestimate","pos":"v.","zh":"高估"},{"word":"underestimate","pos":"v.","zh":"低估"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Size it up: put a rough number on it","titleCN":"先量个大概：给数量一个近似的数","definition":"to judge the approximate size, amount, or cost of something from the information available","definitionCN":"依据手头有限的信息，判断某物的大致规模、数量或成本","example":"Engineers estimate that the bridge will take three years to complete.","exampleCN":"工程师估计这座桥要三年才能建成。","why":"The verb is recorded from the 1530s with the sense 'to value, appraise', and by the 1580s it also meant 'to judge approximately'. The act starts as pricing something, then loosens into putting a number on anything.","whyCN":"动词义记录于 16 世纪 30 年代，意为“估价、评定”；到 16 世纪 80 年代又指“近似判断”。这个动作最初是给东西定价，后来放宽为给任何事物安上一个数。"},{"no":"02","title":"The written figure: a price quoted in advance","titleCN":"写下来的数：事先报出的价格","definition":"a statement of the likely cost of work or goods, given before the work is done","definitionCN":"在施工或交货之前给出的费用说明、报价","example":"The final bill was twice the original estimate.","exampleCN":"最终的账单是原来报价的两倍。","why":"The noun appears in the 1560s meaning 'valuation, appraisal'. Once the figure is written down for a customer, the estimate becomes the document and the price it names.","whyCN":"名词义出现于 16 世纪 60 年代，意为“估价、评定”。当这个数字为顾客写下来，estimate 就从“一次估算”变成那份文件以及它所标的价格。"},{"no":"03","title":"The statistical estimate: a value read from a sample","titleCN":"统计估计量：从样本读出的值","definition":"in statistics, a value calculated from a sample and used as an approximation of an unknown quantity","definitionCN":"统计学中，由样本算出、用来近似未知总量的数值","example":"The survey produced an estimate of 4.2 million speakers of the language.","exampleCN":"这项调查得出该语言约有 420 万使用者的估计值。","why":"Modern statistics gave the old noun a technical role: the estimate is the number a sample yields when the true total cannot be counted. The everyday 'rough figure' becomes a named quantity in a model.","whyCN":"现代统计学给这个旧名词一个技术身份：当真实总量无法数清时，样本算出的那个数就是 estimate。日常的“大概的数”于是成了模型里有名字的量。"},{"no":"04","title":"In my estimate: the judgment I hold","titleCN":"依我看：我心里作出的判断","definition":"a personal opinion or judgment formed after weighing what is known","definitionCN":"权衡已知情况后形成的个人看法或判断","example":"In my estimate, the delay had less to do with money than with poor planning.","exampleCN":"依我看，延误与其说与钱有关，不如说与规划不善有关。","why":"The noun was recorded in the mid-15c. as 'act of estimating' and also 'mind, intellect, judgment'. The phrase in my estimate keeps that sense of a judgment held rather than a figure measured.","whyCN":"名词在 15 世纪中期记录为“估算行为”，同时也指“心智、判断力”。短语 in my estimate 保留的正是“持有的判断”，而不是“量出的数字”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Estimate that: state what you believe will happen","titleCN":"估计认为：说出你判断会发生的事","definition":"to express an opinion about a future amount or outcome, often followed by a that-clause","definitionCN":"对未来数量或结果表达看法，常接 that 从句","example":"Officials estimate that about 60 people were in the building at the time.","exampleCN":"官员估计当时楼内约有 60 人。","why":"From the 1580s 'approximate judgment' the verb widened from pricing to predicting. A that-clause lets the speaker hand over a figure without claiming exact knowledge.","whyCN":"从 16 世纪 80 年代的“近似判断”起，这个动词从定价扩展到预测。接 that 从句时，说话人交出一个数字，却不宣称自己精确知道。"},{"no":"06","title":"A rough count of a whole: how many are out there","titleCN":"对整体的粗略计数：到底有多少","definition":"a rough calculation of the total number or extent of something that cannot be counted directly","definitionCN":"对无法直接清点的总体数量或规模的粗略推算","example":"A population estimate for the region put the figure at nine million.","exampleCN":"对该地区人口的估算把数字定在九百万。","why":"The noun moves from the price of one thing to the size of a whole group. When counting every member is impossible, a calculated figure stands in for the total.","whyCN":"名词从“一件东西的价钱”移向“一整群的规模”。当无法清点每一个成员时，一个算出来的数字就代行总体。"},{"no":"07","title":"At a rough estimate: the phrase that hedges a figure","titleCN":"粗略估计：给数字加限的固定说法","definition":"in the fixed phrase 'at a rough estimate', used to say that a figure is approximate","definitionCN":"用于固定短语 at a rough estimate，表示所给数字只是约略的","example":"At a rough estimate, the repairs will take six weeks.","exampleCN":"粗略估计，维修要花六周。","why":"The phrase freezes the noun into an adverbial slot. Rough marks the number as one of several possible estimates, which is exactly how the noun has been used since the 1560s.","whyCN":"这个短语把名词固定进状语位置。rough 标明这个数字只是若干可能估算中的一个，这正是 16 世纪 60 年代以来该名词的用法。"},{"no":"08","title":"Appraise a person: weigh someone's worth","titleCN":"评价一个人：掂量他的斤两","definition":"to form a judgment of someone's ability, character, or worth","definitionCN":"对某人的能力、品格或价值作出判断","example":"The coach estimated the young player's potential too low.","exampleCN":"教练低估了这名年轻球员的潜力。","why":"Latin aestimare meant 'to value, rate, appraise', and people as well as goods can be rated. The older 'set a value on' survives in judgments of ability and worth.","whyCN":"拉丁语 aestimare 意为“估价、评定”，而人可以像货物一样被评定。古老的“给……定值”就残留在对能力与价值的判断里。"},{"no":"09","title":"The mind itself: an archaic sense of judgment","titleCN":"心智本身：一个古老义项","definition":"in 15c–16c usage, the faculty of judgment or understanding; now archaic","definitionCN":"在 15 至 16 世纪的用法中指判断力或理解力；现已古旧","example":"The old text speaks of a man of small estimate, meaning weak in judgment.","exampleCN":"那篇古旧文本说 a man of small estimate，意思是判断力薄弱的人。","why":"The noun was recorded in the mid-15c. with the sense 'mind, intellect, judgment'. This sense has dropped out of ordinary use, but it shows that the word once named the faculty which produces an estimate.","whyCN":"名词在 15 世纪中期记录有“心智、理解力、判断力”之义。这个义项已退出日常使用，却说明这个词曾经命名的是产生估算的那种能力。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Estimate comes from Latin aestimare 'to value, rate, appraise', through the past participle aestimatus. Its deeper origin is uncertain, and the word also produced esteem and aim.","cn":"estimate 来自拉丁语 aestimare“估价、评定”，经过去分词 aestimatus 进入英语。它的更深来源不确定，同一个词也产出了 esteem 和 aim。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (BEFORE 1C BC)","en":"Aestimare meant 'to value, rate, appraise'. Its own origin is uncertain; a suggested link with *ais-temos 'one who cuts copper, a coiner' is judged unconvincing by de Vaan, so the root must be marked source uncertain.","cn":"aestimare 意为“估价、评定”。它自身的来源不确定；有说法认为与 *ais-temos“切铜者、铸币者”有关，但 de Vaan 认为不太可信，因此词根只能标为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN (1C BC – 1C AD)","en":"The past participle aestimatus and the noun aestimatio 'valuation' carried the sense of setting a value. Through Old French the same stem also gave esteem and aim.","cn":"过去分词 aestimatus 与名词 aestimatio“估价”都带着“给某物定值”的意思。经古法语，同一词干还产出了 esteem 与 aim。"},{"era":"MID-15c ENGLISH","en":"The noun is recorded as 'act of estimating' and, separately, as 'mind, intellect, judgment'. The second sense is now archaic but shows judgment as the inner act behind the figure.","cn":"名词记录为“估算行为”，另外还指“心智、理解力、判断力”。后一义项现在已古旧，却说明“判断”是这个数字背后的内在动作。"},{"era":"1530s ENGLISH","en":"The verb appears meaning 'to value, appraise'. The first job of the word is pricing: say what a thing is worth.","cn":"动词出现，意为“估价、评定”。这个词最早的工作就是定价：说出一件东西值多少。"},{"era":"1560s–1580s ENGLISH","en":"The noun adds 'valuation, appraisal of price' in the 1560s, and by the 1580s the word also covers 'approximate judgment' of number or size.","cn":"名词在 16 世纪 60 年代增添“估价、对价格的评定”；到 16 世纪 80 年代，这个词也涵盖对数量或规模的“近似判断”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Statistics turns the estimate into a computed quantity, while the written estimate becomes a quotation. The old sense of personal judgment survives in in my estimate.","cn":"统计学把 estimate 变成算出的量，书面的 estimate 则成为报价单。古老的“个人判断”义仍活在 in my estimate 里。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"esteem","ipa":"/ɪˈstiːm/","tag":"same root, different word","definition":"to respect and value someone highly. It shares the Latin stem aestimare with estimate, but it names affection and respect, not a number.","definitionCN":"尊敬；看重。与 estimate 同出拉丁语 aestimare，但它指的是敬重与情感，不是一个数字。"},{"word":"intimate","ipa":"/ˈɪntɪmət/","tag":"near spelling (-timate)","definition":"close and personal, or to hint at something. It shares the -timate ending but has nothing to do with valuing.","definitionCN":"亲密的；暗示。同样以 -timate 结尾，却与“估价”毫无关系。"},{"word":"estimable","ipa":"/ˈestɪməbl/","tag":"shares the estim- stem","definition":"deserving respect, or able to be estimated. It is built on estimate's stem with -able, so the shape is close but the usual meaning is 'worthy'.","definitionCN":"值得尊敬的；可估计的。由 estimate 的词干加 -able 构成，外形相近，但常用义是“值得敬重”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"evaluate","ipa":"/ɪˈvæljueɪt/","tag":"measured vs approximate","definition":"to judge worth or quality against a standard. Evaluate is systematic and formal, while estimate gives an approximate figure from limited information.","definitionCN":"按标准评判价值或质量。evaluate 系统而正式；estimate 只是凭有限信息给出近似数字。"},{"word":"assess","ipa":"/əˈses/","tag":"judge the level","definition":"to judge the level, seriousness, or nature of something, often officially. Assess stresses a judgment of degree, while estimate stresses an approximate number.","definitionCN":"评定程度、严重性或性质，常为官方判断。assess 强调对程度的判断，estimate 强调近似数目。"},{"word":"calculate","ipa":"/ˈkælkjuleɪt/","tag":"exact working out","definition":"to work out an amount exactly from known figures. Calculate needs data and rules; estimate is what you do when the data are incomplete.","definitionCN":"由已知数字精确算出。calculate 需要数据与规则；estimate 则是在数据不全时做的事。"},{"word":"gauge","ipa":"/ɡeɪdʒ/","tag":"sense the scale","definition":"to judge the size, amount, or mood of something that is hard to measure. Gauge is often used for feelings and reactions rather than prices.","definitionCN":"估量难以测量的规模、数量或情绪。gauge 多用于感受与反应，而非价格。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin aestimare family, the shared stem of esteem and aim, the derived verbs overestimate and underestimate, and the fixed phrase at a rough estimate.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 aestimare 词族、esteem 与 aim 的共同词干、派生动词 overestimate 与 underestimate，以及固定短语 at a rough estimate。"},"normal":[{"en":"estimate and esteem share Latin aestimare 'to value, rate'. Esteem is the valuing turned into respect for a person.","cn":"estimate 与 esteem 同出拉丁语 aestimare“估价、评定”。esteem 就是“定值”转向了对人的敬重。"},{"en":"The aestim- stem also gave aim through Old French aesmer, so aiming at a target and estimating a value come from one root.","cn":"aestim- 词干还经古法语 aesmer 产出了 aim，所以“瞄准目标”和“估算价值”出自同一个词根。"},{"en":"The family is transparent: estimation, estimator, overestimate and underestimate all keep the sense of putting a value or number on something.","cn":"这个词族一目了然：estimation、estimator、overestimate、underestimate 都保留着“给某物定值或定数”的意思。"},{"en":"The phrase at a rough estimate is a fixed slot where the noun names an approximate figure.","cn":"短语 at a rough estimate 是一个固定位置，其中的名词指的就是一个近似的数字。"},{"en":"A cost estimate is a document, not a guess: it is the number a builder or an insurer will stand behind.","cn":"a cost estimate 是一份文件，不是随口一猜：它是建筑商或保险公司愿意为之负责的那个数。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Estimate is what you say when you can see part of the thing and still must speak about the whole.","cn":"estimate 是你只看见事物的一部分、却必须谈论整体时所说的话。"},{"en":"The word always carries a small margin of error: it names a figure that admits it may be wrong.","cn":"这个词总带着一点误差的余地：它命名的数字承认自己可能不准。"},{"en":"From pricing goods to judging people to counting a population, the same act returns: set a value on what is not fully known.","cn":"从给货物定价，到评价人，再到清点人口，同一个动作反复出现：给尚未完全知晓的东西定一个值。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Engineers estimate that the bridge will take three years to complete.","cn":"工程师估计这座桥要三年才能建成。"},{"en":"The final bill was twice the original estimate.","cn":"最终的账单是原来报价的两倍。"},{"en":"In my estimate, the delay had less to do with money than with poor planning.","cn":"依我看，延误与其说与钱有关，不如说与规划不善有关。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「爱死提梅特」——先把“梅特”的价钱提一提，掂量着估个准数 → estimate 估算、估价","word":"estimate"},"root":"源自拉丁语 aestimare“估价、评定”，经过去分词 aestimatus 进入英语；aestimare 的深层来源不确定，或与“切铜铸币者”有关，但可信度低。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of estimate, from a rough count to a written quotation and an old sense of mental judgment. The common core is a figure or verdict produced from incomplete information.","cn":"estimate 的九个义项，从粗略计数到书面报价，再到古老的“判断力”义。共同的底层是：用不完整的信息产出一个数字或判断。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a figure guessed from partial evidence.","cn":"核心意象：凭部分证据先估出的那个数。"},"chain":["COUNT WHAT IS KNOWN","GUESS THE REST","NAME A FIGURE","WRITE IT DOWN","JUDGE THE WORTH","STAND ON THE JUDGMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S5","en":"THE ACT OF GUESSING: the verb puts an approximate number on a cost, and a that-clause turns it into a stated opinion.","cn":"估算的动作：动词给成本安上近似数字，that 从句则把它变成说出口的看法。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"THE NUMBER WRITTEN DOWN: a quotation for a customer, and a rough count of a whole population.","cn":"写下来的数字：给顾客的报价，以及对总体人口的粗略计数。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"THE STATISTICAL ESTIMATE: a value computed from a sample to stand in for an unknown total.","cn":"统计估计量：由样本算出、代行未知总量的值。"},{"senses":"S4 · S9","en":"THE JUDGMENT IN THE MIND: a personal opinion in in my estimate, and the archaic sense of the judging faculty itself.","cn":"心中的判断：in my estimate 里的个人看法，以及“判断力本身”的古老义项。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"THE FIGURE AND THE PERSON: the hedged phrase at a rough estimate, and the appraisal of someone's ability.","cn":"数字与人：加限的短语 at a rough estimate，以及对某人能力的评价。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Estimate is built on the Latin stem aestim-; the family is made with -ation, -or, -able and the prefixes over- and under-.","cn":"estimate 建立在拉丁词干 aestim- 上；词族由 -ation、-or、-able 以及前缀 over-、under- 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin aestimare 'to value, rate' produced aestimatio 'valuation' and the participle aestimatus; through Old French the same stem also gave esteem and aim.","cn":"拉丁语 aestimare“估价、评定”产出了 aestimatio“估价”和分词 aestimatus；经古法语，同一词干还产出了 esteem 与 aim。"},"items":[{"word":"estimate","structure":"Latin aestimare (to value, rate)","meaning":"to judge an approximate amount","meaningCN":"估算（直接来自拉丁语 aestimare）","example":"They estimate the repair at two thousand dollars.","exampleCN":"他们估算维修费为两千美元。"},{"word":"estimation","structure":"estimat- + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of estimating, or a judgment","meaningCN":"估计；判断（-ion 构成动作名词）","example":"In their estimation, the plan is too risky.","exampleCN":"在他们看来，这个计划风险太大。"},{"word":"estimator","structure":"estimat- + -or (agent noun)","meaning":"one who estimates; a statistical rule for estimating","meaningCN":"估算者；估计量（-or 表施动者）","example":"The estimator allowed for rising material costs.","exampleCN":"估价师把材料涨价的因素算了进去。"},{"word":"estimable","structure":"estim- + -able (worthy of being valued)","meaning":"deserving respect; able to be estimated","meaningCN":"值得尊敬的；可估计的（-able 表可被……）","example":"She was an estimable scholar and a kind teacher.","exampleCN":"她是一位值得敬重的学者，也是一位和善的老师。"},{"word":"overestimate","structure":"over- (above) + estimate","meaning":"to estimate too high","meaningCN":"高估（over- 表超过）","example":"We overestimated how much time the work would need.","exampleCN":"我们高估了这项工作所需的时间。"},{"word":"underestimate","structure":"under- (below) + estimate","meaning":"to estimate too low","meaningCN":"低估（under- 表不足）","example":"Never underestimate a quiet opponent.","exampleCN":"永远不要低估一个安静的对手。"},{"word":"esteem","structure":"Latin aestimare via Old French estimer","meaning":"to value highly, to respect","meaningCN":"尊敬；看重（同源异形词）","example":"The teacher was held in high esteem by her students.","exampleCN":"这位老师深受学生敬重。"},{"word":"aim","structure":"Old French aesmer, from Latin aestimare","meaning":"to point at a target; a purpose","meaningCN":"瞄准；目标（同源，经古法语）","example":"He aimed at the centre of the board.","exampleCN":"他瞄准靶心。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"aestimare","structure":"aestimare (verb)","meaning":"to value, rate, appraise","meaningCN":"估价；评定"},{"word":"aestimatio","structure":"aestimare + -tio (noun)","meaning":"a valuation, an appraisal","meaningCN":"估价；评价"},{"word":"aestimatus","structure":"past participle of aestimare","meaning":"valued, appraised","meaningCN":"已被估价的"}]}},{"word":"evaluate","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈvæljueɪt/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈvæljueɪt/","definition_zh":"评估；评价；求值；鉴定；估值","definition_en":"to judge the value, quality, or performance of something against a standard, or to work out the value of a mathematical expression","core_image":"把一件东西放上秤盘，对着刻度一格一格读出它的值","scene":"Before the grant was renewed, the committee met to evaluate the literacy programme's results.","sceneCN":"这里 evaluate 是「评估（项目成效）」（第 5 个义项：按目标与标准评定成效）；句意：在拨款续期之前，委员会开会评估这项扫盲项目的成效。图中可辨识物件：会议桌、项目报告、评分表、投影上的柱状图。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"评估；评价；求值；估值"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"evaluate the effectiveness of","zh":"评估……的成效"},{"phrase":"evaluate performance","zh":"评价表现"},{"phrase":"evaluate something against criteria","zh":"对照标准评估某事"},{"phrase":"critically evaluate","zh":"批判性地评估"},{"phrase":"evaluate a patient","zh":"评估病人"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"evaluates"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"evaluated"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"evaluated"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"evaluating"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"evaluation","pos":"n.","zh":"评估；评价；鉴定"},{"word":"evaluator","pos":"n.","zh":"评估者；评审员"},{"word":"evaluative","pos":"adj.","zh":"评价性的；评估的"},{"word":"re-evaluate","pos":"v.","zh":"重新评估"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Judge the worth: measure something against a standard","titleCN":"评定价值：拿标准去量","definition":"to judge the value or quality of something by measuring it against a standard","definitionCN":"依照某个标准衡量，判断某物的价值或质量","example":"The panel will evaluate each proposal against the same criteria.","exampleCN":"评审小组将按同一套标准评估每份提案。","why":"The word was formed in 1831 from evaluation, itself from French évaluer, where é- means 'out' and valuer comes from Latin valere 'to be worth'. Evaluation is literally 'bringing out the worth', so the verb starts as a measured reading of value.","whyCN":"这个词 1831 年由 evaluation 逆构而来，而 evaluation 来自法语 évaluer：é- 意为“出”，valuer 源自拉丁语 valere“有价值”。evaluation 字面就是“把价值取出来”，因此动词的起点是“按标准读出价值”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Mark the work: judge performance","titleCN":"给表现打分：评判做得怎样","definition":"to judge how well someone has performed a task, often giving a grade or rating","definitionCN":"评判某人完成任务的优劣，常给出分数或等级","example":"Teachers evaluate essays for clarity as well as accuracy.","exampleCN":"教师评估作文时既看准确性，也看表达是否清晰。","why":"Once worth is read against a standard, that standard can be a rubric. Judging a performance adds a second party: the evaluator compares what was done with what was required.","whyCN":"一旦价值是照着标准读出的，这个标准就可以是一份评分细则。评判表现又加入了另一方：评估者把“做了什么”与“要求做什么”相对照。"},{"no":"03","title":"Work out the value: evaluate an expression","titleCN":"求出值来：数学里的求值","definition":"in mathematics, to calculate the numerical value of an expression or function for given values","definitionCN":"数学中，代入给定数值后算出一个表达式或函数的值","example":"Evaluate 2x + 3 when x = 4.","exampleCN":"当 x = 4 时，求 2x + 3 的值。","why":"The word was first used in mathematics in 1831, and there it kept the plainest sense of valere: find what the thing is worth, here a number. Substituting values and computing is evaluation with no judgment of quality at all.","whyCN":"这个词 1831 年最初就用于数学，那里保留了 valere 最素朴的意思：求出这东西值多少，此处即一个数。代入数值再计算，是完全没有质量评判的 evaluation。"},{"no":"04","title":"Assess the patient: a clinical reading","titleCN":"评估病人：临床上的读数","definition":"of a doctor, to examine a patient and judge their condition before deciding on treatment","definitionCN":"医生检查病人，在决定治疗方案前判断其状况","example":"The doctor evaluated the patient's breathing before ordering a scan.","exampleCN":"医生先评估了病人的呼吸情况，然后才安排扫描。","why":"Clinical use narrows the standard to the body: signs are measured, a condition is named, and treatment follows. The worth being read here is the state of a person's health.","whyCN":"临床用法把标准缩小到身体：测量体征、判定状况，再据此治疗。这里读出的“值”是一个人的健康状态。"},{"no":"05","title":"Weigh a programme: does it work?","titleCN":"评估项目：它到底有没有用","definition":"to judge how effective a policy, programme, or intervention has been in reaching its aims","definitionCN":"判断某项政策、项目或干预在达成目标上的实际效果","example":"An independent team was hired to evaluate the literacy programme.","exampleCN":"一个独立团队受聘评估这项扫盲项目。","why":"Here the standard is the stated aim. Evaluation compares results with goals, which is why the noun evaluation is so common in policy, education and medicine.","whyCN":"这里的标准是明示的目标。评估把结果与目标相比较，因此名词 evaluation 在政策、教育和医学中如此常见。"},{"no":"06","title":"Weigh the choices: decide whether to act","titleCN":"权衡选项：决定做不做","definition":"to consider the advantages and disadvantages of a possible action before deciding","definitionCN":"在决定之前权衡某一可能行动的利弊","example":"The family evaluated whether to move before the school year began.","exampleCN":"这家人权衡了是否要在学年开始前搬家。","why":"Judgment of worth can be turned toward the future: options are placed side by side and rated. The verb then means a deliberation that ends in a decision.","whyCN":"对价值的判断可以朝向未来：把几个选项并排摆好，逐一打分。动词于是指以决定告终的斟酌。"},{"no":"07","title":"Measure the danger: evaluate risk","titleCN":"量一量危险：评估风险","definition":"to judge the likelihood and seriousness of a possible harm","definitionCN":"判断某种潜在危害发生的可能性与严重程度","example":"Regulators must evaluate the risks of the new drug before approval.","exampleCN":"监管机构必须在批准前评估这种新药的风险。","why":"Risk assessment borrows the same structure: probability and severity are the two scales, and the result is a rating rather than a price.","whyCN":"风险评估借用了同一套结构：可能性与严重性是两把尺子，得出的结果是等级评定，而不是价格。"},{"no":"08","title":"Evaluate against: the standard named in the phrase","titleCN":"对照标准：短语里点明的尺子","definition":"in the pattern 'evaluate something against something', to use the second thing as the measure","definitionCN":"在 evaluate something against something 结构中，以后者作为衡量的尺度","example":"Each application was evaluated against three criteria: need, cost, and impact.","exampleCN":"每份申请都对照三项标准评估：需求、成本与影响。","why":"Against names the surface on which the object is laid. The preposition makes visible what evaluation always needs: a standard held steady while the thing is measured.","whyCN":"against 点明对象被放上去对照的那个“面”。这个介词让 evaluation 始终需要的东西显形：在测量时保持不动的那把标准尺。"},{"no":"09","title":"Put a value on assets: the financial reading","titleCN":"给资产定价：金融里的估值","definition":"in finance, to set or estimate the monetary value of property, a company, or an asset","definitionCN":"金融中，为房产、公司或资产确定或估算货币价值","example":"The bank evaluated the collateral before approving the loan.","exampleCN":"银行在批准贷款前对抵押物作了估值。","why":"Finance returns the word to its root: valere is 'to be worth', and valuers set a money figure. This sense is the closest modern relative of the French évaluer behind the word.","whyCN":"金融把这个词带回词根：valere 就是“值多少”，估价师给出一个货币数字。这一义项是这个词背后法语 évaluer 在现代英语中最亲近的后代。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Evaluate is a young word, formed in 1831 from evaluation (1755) or from French évaluer. Its root is Latin valere 'to be worth, be strong', the same root as value, valid and valor.","cn":"evaluate 是个年轻的词，1831 年由 evaluation（1755）或法语 évaluer 而来。它的词根是拉丁语 valere“有价值、强健”，与 value、valid、valor 同根。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Valere meant 'to be worth, be strong'; the noun valor meant 'worth, courage' and validus meant 'strong'. The root is about having weight or force, not about seeing.","cn":"valere 意为“有价值、强健”；名词 valor 指“价值、勇气”，validus 指“强壮的”。这个词根关乎“有分量、有力”，与“看见”无关。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.–13c.)","en":"Value and valuer carried the Latin stem into French, and English took value from there. The sense is still 'what a thing is worth'.","cn":"value 与 valuer 把拉丁词干带进法语，英语又从法语取来 value。词义仍是“一件东西值多少”。"},{"era":"1755 ENGLISH","en":"Evaluation is recorded as 'the act of valuing'. The French pattern is visible: é- 'out' plus value, so the act is bringing the worth out into the open.","cn":"evaluation 记录为“估价的行为”。法语的构词痕迹可见：é-“出”加 value，所以这个动作就是把价值取出来、摆到明处。"},{"era":"1831 ENGLISH","en":"Evaluate is back-formed from evaluation, or borrowed from French évaluer. Its earliest uses are mathematical: work out the value of an expression.","cn":"evaluate 由 evaluation 逆构，或借自法语 évaluer。它最早的用法是数学上的：求出一个表达式的值。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Evaluation spreads to education, medicine, policy and finance, while evaluate keeps 'judge against a standard' as its core. The noun is older than the verb by about seventy years.","cn":"evaluation 扩散到教育、医学、政策与金融，而 evaluate 始终以“按标准评判”为核心。名词比动词大约早七十年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"evacuate","ipa":"/ɪˈvækjueɪt/","tag":"near sound and spelling","definition":"to move people away from danger, or to empty a space. It differs from evaluate by one consonant and means removal, not judgment.","definitionCN":"撤离；排空。与 evaluate 只差一个辅音，意思却是把人移走，而非评判。"},{"word":"value","ipa":"/ˈvæljuː/","tag":"hidden inside the word","definition":"worth, or to regard something as important. It is the stem inside evaluate, but it does not name the process of judging against a standard.","definitionCN":"价值；重视。它是 evaluate 里藏着的词干，却不表示“按标准评判的过程”。"},{"word":"devalue","ipa":"/ˌdiːˈvæljuː/","tag":"prefix contrast","definition":"to reduce the value of something. De- points down, the opposite direction from the e- 'out' of evaluate: devalue lowers worth, evaluate reads it out.","definitionCN":"贬值；贬低。de- 指向下降，与 evaluate 的 e-“出”方向相反：devalue 让价值降低，evaluate 把价值读出来。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"estimate","ipa":"/ˈestɪmeɪt/","tag":"approximate vs systematic","definition":"to judge a rough amount from limited information. Estimate gives an approximate number; evaluate judges worth or quality against a standard and is more formal.","definitionCN":"凭有限信息给出大致数目。estimate 给的是近似数；evaluate 按标准评判价值或质量，更正式、更强调评估过程与标准。"},{"word":"assess","ipa":"/əˈses/","tag":"rate the level","definition":"to judge the level or seriousness of something, often officially. Assess stresses a judgment of degree, while evaluate stresses measuring worth against criteria.","definitionCN":"评定程度或严重性，常为官方判断。assess 强调判断“到何种程度”；evaluate 强调对照标准衡量价值。"},{"word":"appraise","ipa":"/əˈpreɪz/","tag":"set a price","definition":"to fix a professional value on property, goods, or performance. Appraise is closer to pricing and is usually done by an expert.","definitionCN":"对房产、货物或表现作专业估值。appraise 更靠近“定价”，通常由专家进行。"},{"word":"judge","ipa":"/dʒʌdʒ/","tag":"reach a verdict","definition":"to form an opinion or verdict, often about right and wrong. Judge is more personal and can be moral; evaluate is procedural and standard-based.","definitionCN":"形成看法或裁决，常针对对错。judge 更偏个人、可含道德评判；evaluate 有程序与标准。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the construction e- + value + -ate, the valere family, the 1755 noun that came before the 1831 verb, and the mathematical use of evaluate.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：e- + value + -ate 的构词、valere 词族、先于 1831 年动词的 1755 年名词，以及 evaluate 的数学用法。"},"normal":[{"en":"e- + value + -ate: the word literally says 'value out', bringing the worth into the open.","cn":"e- + value + -ate：这个词字面就是“把价值取出来”，让值显露在明处。"},{"en":"The family is the valere family: value, valid 'strong', valor 'bravery', avail, and equivalent 'of equal worth'.","cn":"这个词族就是 valere 家族：value、valid“有力的”、valor“英勇”、avail，以及 equivalent“等值的”。"},{"en":"evaluation came first in 1755; evaluate was back-formed from it in 1831, so the noun is older than the verb.","cn":"evaluation 于 1755 年先出现；evaluate 在 1831 年由它逆构而成，所以名词比动词年长。"},{"en":"In mathematics, evaluate keeps the plainest sense: substitute the numbers and work out the value.","cn":"在数学里，evaluate 保留了最素朴的意思：代进数字，算出值来。"},{"en":"The phrase evaluate against names the standard, and that is what separates evaluate from a casual opinion.","cn":"短语 evaluate against 点明了标准，而标准正是 evaluate 与随口发表意见的分界线。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Evaluation puts the thing on one side and the standard on the other, then reads across.","cn":"评估把对象放在一边、标准放在另一边，然后横着读过去。"},{"en":"The word is a bridge between two things: what is, and what it is measured against.","cn":"这个词是两样东西之间的桥：实际的样子，与拿来量它的尺子。"},{"en":"From a number in algebra to a pupil's essay to a company's assets, the same move repeats: find the worth and say it.","cn":"从代数里的一个数，到学生的作文，再到公司的资产，同一个动作反复出现：找出值，再说出来。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The panel will evaluate each proposal against the same criteria.","cn":"评审小组将按同一套标准评估每份提案。"},{"en":"Teachers evaluate essays for clarity as well as accuracy.","cn":"教师评估作文时既看准确性，也看表达是否清晰。"},{"en":"Evaluate 2x + 3 when x = 4.","cn":"当 x = 4 时，求 2x + 3 的值。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「依外柳，诶特」——把东西一外溜地翻看一遍，挨个儿评出它值多少 → evaluate 评估","word":"evaluate"},"root":"源自拉丁语 valere“有价值、强健”，经法语 évaluer 与 evaluation（1755）而来，1831 年逆构为动词；核心是“把值读出来”，与 estimate 的 aestimare 不同源。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of evaluate, from a mathematical value to a clinical reading and a financial valuation. The common core is measuring something against a standard and announcing what it is worth.","cn":"evaluate 的九个义项，从数学求值到临床评估、金融估值。共同的底层是：把对象对照某个标准量一量，然后说出它值多少。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a thing laid on a scale beside a fixed standard.","cn":"核心意象：把对象放上天平，旁边立着一把固定的尺。"},"chain":["FIND THE OBJECT","NAME THE STANDARD","MEASURE IT","WEIGH THE EVIDENCE","RECORD THE VALUE","DECIDE WHAT IT IS WORTH"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"OBJECT AND STANDARD: judging worth against criteria, with against naming the standard explicitly.","cn":"对象与标准：对照标准评判价值，against 把标准明确点出来。"},{"senses":"S2 · S9","en":"PERFORMANCE AND ASSETS: a rubric applied to a person's work, and a money figure set on property.","cn":"表现与资产：用评分细则衡量一个人的工作，以及给房产定一个货币数。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"MATHEMATICAL VALUE: substitute the numbers and compute, with no quality judgment at all.","cn":"数学上的值：代入数字计算，全无质量评判。"},{"senses":"S4 · S7","en":"BODY AND RISK: a doctor reads a patient's condition, and regulators rate likelihood and severity.","cn":"身体与风险：医生读出病人的状况，监管者评出可能性与严重性。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"PROGRAMME AND CHOICE: results are compared with aims, and options are weighed before a decision.","cn":"项目与选择：把结果与目标相比，并在决定前权衡选项。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Evaluate is built from the Latin stem val- 'be worth', with the prefix e- 'out' and the verb ending -ate; the family runs through value, valid, valor and equivalent.","cn":"evaluate 由拉丁词干 val-“值”加上前缀 e-“出”和动词后缀 -ate 构成；词族贯穿 value、valid、valor、equivalent。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin valere 'to be worth, be strong' gave valor 'worth, courage' and validus 'strong'; French évaluer added the prefix é- 'out' before English formed evaluation and then evaluate.","cn":"拉丁语 valere“有价值、强健”产出了 valor“价值、勇气”和 validus“强壮的”；法语 évaluer 又加了前缀 é-“出”，英语随后才有 evaluation 与 evaluate。"},"items":[{"word":"evaluate","structure":"e- (out) + value + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to bring out the worth, to judge value","meaningCN":"评估（e- 出 + value 价值 + -ate 动词）","example":"We need to evaluate the cost before we commit.","exampleCN":"在投入之前，我们需要评估成本。"},{"word":"evaluation","structure":"evaluate + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or result of evaluating","meaningCN":"评估；评价（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The evaluation will take three months.","exampleCN":"这次评估要花三个月。"},{"word":"evaluator","structure":"evaluate + -or (agent noun)","meaning":"one who evaluates","meaningCN":"评估者；评审员（-or 表施动者）","example":"Each evaluator scored the samples independently.","exampleCN":"每位评审员独立给样本打分。"},{"word":"evaluative","structure":"evaluate + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"serving to evaluate","meaningCN":"评价性的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The report is descriptive rather than evaluative.","exampleCN":"这份报告是描述性的，而非评价性的。"},{"word":"re-evaluate","structure":"re- (again) + evaluate","meaning":"to evaluate again","meaningCN":"重新评估（re- 表再次）","example":"We re-evaluated the plan after the costs rose.","exampleCN":"成本上涨后，我们重新评估了这个计划。"},{"word":"value","structure":"Latin valere via Old French","meaning":"worth; to hold something dear","meaningCN":"价值；重视（来自拉丁语 valere 经古法语）","example":"The value of the house has doubled.","exampleCN":"这栋房子的价值翻了一番。"},{"word":"valid","structure":"Latin validus, from valere (be strong)","meaning":"strong, sound, legally effective","meaningCN":"有效的；有力的（valere 表强健）","example":"Your ticket is valid for one month.","exampleCN":"你的票一个月内有效。"},{"word":"valor","structure":"Latin valor, from valere","meaning":"courage, worth","meaningCN":"英勇；价值（拉丁语 valor）","example":"He was decorated for valor in battle.","exampleCN":"他因作战英勇而受勋。"},{"word":"equivalent","structure":"equi- (equal) + valere (be worth)","meaning":"of equal worth","meaningCN":"等值的（equi- 相等 + valere 值）","example":"One mile is equivalent to about 1.6 kilometres.","exampleCN":"一英里约等于 1.6 公里。"},{"word":"avail","structure":"Latin valere via Old French","meaning":"to be of use or worth","meaningCN":"有用；效用（同源，经古法语）","example":"His protests were of no avail.","exampleCN":"他的抗议毫无用处。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"valere","structure":"valere (verb)","meaning":"to be worth, be strong","meaningCN":"有价值；强健"},{"word":"valor","structure":"valere + -or (noun)","meaning":"worth, courage","meaningCN":"价值；勇气"},{"word":"validus","structure":"valere + -idus (adjective)","meaning":"strong, sound","meaningCN":"强壮的；有力的"}]}},{"word":"evident","ipa_uk":"/ˈevɪdənt/","ipa_us":"/ˈevɪdənt/","definition_zh":"明显的；显而易见的；清楚的；可见的","definition_en":"easy to see or understand, so that no proof or explanation is needed","core_image":"窗帘拉开，窗台上的裂痕一眼就看得见","scene":"The leak was evident from the water marks spreading across the ceiling.","sceneCN":"这里 evident 是「（从迹象上）明显可见」（第 3 个义项：由可见的痕迹表明）；句意：从天花板上蔓延的水渍可以明显看出漏水。图中可辨识物件：天花板上的水渍、接水的水桶、梯子、手电筒。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"明显的；显而易见的；可见的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"it is evident that","zh":"显然……；很明显……"},{"phrase":"evident from","zh":"从……可以明显看出"},{"phrase":"self-evident","zh":"不言自明的"},{"phrase":"evident to all","zh":"人人可见；众所皆知"},{"phrase":"evident signs of","zh":"……的明显迹象"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more evident"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most evident"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"evidence","pos":"n.","zh":"证据；迹象"},{"word":"evidently","pos":"adv.","zh":"显然；明显地"},{"word":"evidential","pos":"adj.","zh":"证据的；可作为证据的"},{"word":"self-evident","pos":"adj.","zh":"不言自明的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Visible to the eye: the mark you can see","titleCN":"肉眼可见：看得见的痕迹","definition":"clear to the eye because it can be seen directly","definitionCN":"因为能直接看见而清楚显眼","example":"The scar was still evident on his forearm.","exampleCN":"那道疤仍明显地留在他前臂上。","why":"Evident comes from Latin evidentem 'perceivable, clear', built as ex 'out' + videns 'seeing'. Literally it is what can be seen out in the open, so the first sense is plain physical visibility.","whyCN":"evident 来自拉丁语 evidentem“可感知的、清楚的”，由 ex“出”+ videns“看见”构成。字面就是“在明处能被看见的东西”，所以第一个义项是纯粹的物理可见。"},{"no":"02","title":"Clear to the mind: understood at once","titleCN":"心里明白：一下就懂","definition":"easy to understand, so that no explanation is needed","definitionCN":"容易理解，无需解释便明白","example":"The logic of the argument was evident even to beginners.","exampleCN":"这个论证的逻辑连初学者也一看就懂。","why":"The same clarity is transferred from light to ideas. What the eye does with a visible object, the mind does with a proof that needs no further step.","whyCN":"同样的“清楚”从光线转到观念上。眼睛对可见之物所做的事，就是心智对一个无需再推一步的论证所做的事。"},{"no":"03","title":"Read from the signs: evident from the marks","titleCN":"读迹象：从痕迹上看出来","definition":"made clear by visible signs or traces rather than by direct sight of the thing itself","definitionCN":"不是直接看见事物本身，而是由可见的迹象或痕迹表明","example":"The leak was evident from the water marks spreading across the ceiling.","exampleCN":"从天花板上蔓延的水渍可以明显看出漏水。","why":"Evidence is recorded from c.1300 as 'appearance from which something may be inferred'. What is evident shows itself in traces, so the word covers conclusions drawn from what is left behind.","whyCN":"evidence 自约 1300 年记录为“可据以推断的表象”。evident 的东西是通过痕迹显露自身的，因此这个词也涵盖由残留迹象得出的结论。"},{"no":"04","title":"It is evident that: the sentence of inference","titleCN":"显而易见：推断句的固定框架","definition":"in the pattern 'it is evident that', used to state a conclusion which the facts make clear","definitionCN":"在 it is evident that 句型中，陈述一个由事实表明的结论","example":"It was evident that the two sides would never agree.","exampleCN":"很明显，双方永远不会达成一致。","why":"The adjective moves into an impersonal frame. The speaker does not say 'I see it' but presents the conclusion as something anyone can see, which gives the sentence its authority.","whyCN":"这个形容词进入了一个无人称框架。说话人不说“我看见”，而是把结论摆成人人可见的东西，句子的权威感由此而来。"},{"no":"05","title":"Self-evident: true without proof","titleCN":"不言自明：无需证明即为真","definition":"true in itself, needing no argument or evidence to support it","definitionCN":"本身即为真，不需要论证或证据支撑","example":"The right to a fair trial is treated as self-evident in the charter.","exampleCN":"在这份宪章里，获得公正审判的权利被视为不言自明。","why":"The prefix self- adds the idea that the thing shows itself. Nothing outside it has to be produced; the truth is supposed to be visible in the statement alone.","whyCN":"前缀 self- 添上“自身显现”的意思。无需拿出任何外部的东西，真理被假定在陈述本身里就看得见。"},{"no":"06","title":"Evident to all: open for anyone to see","titleCN":"人人可见：公开摆在众人眼前","definition":"publicly clear, so that no one present can miss it","definitionCN":"公开而清楚，在场的人都不可能错过","example":"Her talent was evident to all who heard her sing.","exampleCN":"所有听过她唱歌的人都明显感受到她的才华。","why":"Visibility extends from one viewer to a whole audience. Evident to all means the showing is not private; the same thing is on display for every pair of eyes.","whyCN":"可见性从一个观看者扩展到整群观众。evident to all 意味着这种显现不是私下的；同一样东西摆在每一双眼睛前。"},{"no":"07","title":"Feelings on show: pleasure you cannot hide","titleCN":"情绪外露：藏不住的喜悦","definition":"of an emotion, showing clearly in someone's face or behaviour","definitionCN":"指情绪清楚地写在某人脸上或举止上","example":"His relief was evident the moment the results arrived.","exampleCN":"结果一到，他的宽慰就明显写在脸上。","why":"Emotions reach the face before they reach speech. Evident names that outward showing, which is why it so often pairs with words like pleasure, relief and disappointment.","whyCN":"情绪先到达脸，再到达语言。evident 命名的正是这种向外的显露，因此它常与 pleasure、relief、disappointment 这类词搭配。"},{"no":"08","title":"Signs of illness: symptoms you can see","titleCN":"病征明显：看得见的症状","definition":"of a medical sign, clearly present and observable","definitionCN":"指医学体征清楚地存在、可以被观察到","example":"The doctor noted evident signs of dehydration.","exampleCN":"医生注意到明显脱水迹象。","why":"Clinical language keeps the plain visual sense. A sign is evident because it is simply there to be seen, before any test turns it into a number.","whyCN":"临床语言保留了最朴素的视觉义。体征之所以 evident，是因为它就在那里、可以被看见，尚未被任何检验变成一个数字。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Evident comes from Latin evidens 'perceivable, clear', built from ex 'out' and videns, the present participle of videre 'to see'. The same root, PIE *weid- 'to see', lies behind video, vision and wit.","cn":"evident 来自拉丁语 evidens“可感知的、清楚的”，由 ex“出”和 videre“看见”的现在分词 videns 构成。同一词根 PIE *weid-“看”也藏在 video、vision 和 wit 里。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (BEFORE 1C BC)","en":"The root *weid- meant 'to see, to know'. Seeing and knowing are one act in this root, which is why a word for visibility can also mean clear to the mind.","cn":"词根 *weid- 意为“看见、知道”。在这个词根里，看见与知道是同一个动作，因此一个表“可见”的词也能表示“心里明白”。"},{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Videre meant 'to see'; its present participle videns is 'seeing'. With ex 'out' the compound evidens meant 'perceivable, clear, manifest'.","cn":"videre 意为“看见”，其现在分词 videns 即“看见的”。加上 ex“出”，复合词 evidens 意为“可感知的、清楚的、显明的”。"},{"era":"c.1300 ENGLISH","en":"Evidence is recorded as 'appearance from which something may be inferred'. The noun names the visible trace, not yet the legal proof it later becomes.","cn":"evidence 记录为“可据以推断的表象”。这个名词命名的是可见的痕迹，还不是它后来变成的法律证据。"},{"era":"LATE 14c ENGLISH","en":"Evident enters English from Old French with the sense 'clear to the eye or to the mind'. Both the physical and the intellectual readings arrive at once.","cn":"evident 经古法语进入英语，意为“对眼睛或心智来说清楚的”。物理的读法与智性的读法同时到来。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Self-evident is a later compound of self and evident, and the frame it is evident that turns the adjective into a marker of inference in academic prose.","cn":"self-evident 是较晚由 self 与 evident 组成的复合词；it is evident that 这一框架则把形容词变成学术写作中的推断标记。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"evidence","ipa":"/ˈevɪdəns/","tag":"same family, noun","definition":"facts or traces that show something is true. It shares the whole stem with evident but is the noun for the material, while evident is the adjective for the clarity.","definitionCN":"证据；迹象。与 evident 共享整个词干，但它是名词，指那些材料；evident 是形容词，指那种清楚。"},{"word":"evidently","ipa":"/ˈevɪdəntli/","tag":"adverb form","definition":"clearly, or as the facts show. It modifies a whole statement, while evident must attach to a noun or follow it is.","definitionCN":"显然；明显地。它修饰整个陈述，而 evident 必须修饰名词或跟在 it is 之后。"},{"word":"provident","ipa":"/ˈprɒvɪdənt/","tag":"near spelling (pro-vident)","definition":"careful about the future, saving for it. It has the same -vident tail from videns 'seeing', but pro- 'forward' makes it 'seeing ahead'.","definitionCN":"有远见的；节俭的。它同样以 videns“看见”带来的 -vident 结尾，但前缀 pro-“向前”使它成为“向前看”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"obvious","ipa":"/ˈɒbviəs/","tag":"closest synonym","definition":"so clear that it needs no explanation. It is the closest everyday match for evident, though evident is a little more formal and often takes that-clauses.","definitionCN":"明显得无需解释。它是 evident 最接近的日常同义词，不过 evident 稍正式，且常接 that 从句。"},{"word":"apparent","ipa":"/əˈpærənt/","tag":"seeming vs seen","definition":"clear at first sight, but sometimes only seemingly so. Apparent can hint that the surface may not be the truth, while evident claims that the thing really shows.","definitionCN":"初见即明显，但有时只是表面上如此。apparent 可暗示表象未必真实；evident 则断言事物确实显露出来。"},{"word":"plain","ipa":"/pleɪn/","tag":"plain and direct","definition":"easy to see or understand, said in everyday speech. Plain is more conversational and often describes facts; evident is more formal and can describe feelings or signs.","definitionCN":"明显；清楚。plain 更口语，常形容事实；evident 更正式，也可形容情绪或迹象。"},{"word":"obviously","ipa":"/əˈbviəsli/","tag":"adverb, not an adjective","definition":"an adverb meaning 'as anyone can see'. Evident is the adjective: you say it is evident that, not it is evidently that.","definitionCN":"副词，意为“显然”。evident 是形容词：要说 it is evident that，而不是 it is evidently that。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin construction e- + vid + -ent, the *weid- family of video, vision and visible, and the pair evidence and evident.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语构词 e- + vid + -ent，*weid- 词族的 video、vision、visible，以及 evidence 与 evident 这一对。"},"normal":[{"en":"e- (out) + vid (see) + -ent: the word says 'that can be seen out in the open'.","cn":"e-（出）+ vid（看）+ -ent：这个词说的就是“在明处能被看见的”。"},{"en":"The *weid- family is wide: video, vision, visible, visit and wit all carry the old sense of seeing or knowing.","cn":"*weid- 词族很广：video、vision、visible、visit、wit 都带着古老的“看见或知道”之义。"},{"en":"evidence is the trace, evident is the clarity of the trace. The noun gives you the thing to look at, the adjective tells you it can be seen.","cn":"evidence 是那道痕迹，evident 是痕迹的清楚。名词给你看的东西，形容词告诉你它看得见。"},{"en":"self-evident is built by adding self- to evident: the thing shows itself, so no proof is required.","cn":"self-evident 由 self- 加 evident 构成：事物自己显现，因此无需证明。"},{"en":"Two frames fix the adjective: it is evident that states a conclusion, and evident from names the traces that lead to it.","cn":"两个框架固定住这个形容词：it is evident that 陈述结论，evident from 点明引出结论的痕迹。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Evident is the moment before explanation: the thing has already shown itself and the argument has not yet begun.","cn":"evident 是解释之前的那一刻：事物已经自己显现，论证尚未开始。"},{"en":"The word assumes a shared light: what one person sees clearly is supposed to be visible to the next.","cn":"这个词假定有一盏共用的灯：一个人看得清楚的东西，也被假定为下一个人看得见。"},{"en":"From a scar to a proof to a feeling on a face, the same claim repeats: no one needs to be told.","cn":"从一道疤，到一个证明，再到脸上的一丝情绪，同一个主张反复出现：不必再告诉任何人。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"It was evident from her tone that she disagreed.","cn":"从她的语气可以明显看出她并不同意。"},{"en":"The benefits of the new route are self-evident.","cn":"这条新路线的益处不言自明。"},{"en":"His relief was evident the moment the results arrived.","cn":"结果一到，他的宽慰就明显写在脸上。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「艾维登特」——哎，维登特就站在那儿，一眼就看得见 → evident 明显的、显而易见的","word":"evident"},"root":"源自拉丁语 evidens“可感知、清楚的”，由 ex“出”+ videns（videre“看见”的分词）构成，根在 PIE *weid-“看”；核心是“摆在明处、一眼可见”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of evident, from a scar on the skin to a truth that needs no proof. The common core is a thing that shows itself, so that seeing and understanding happen at the same moment.","cn":"evident 的八个义项，从皮肤上的一道疤到无需证明的真理。共同的底层是“事物自己显现”，于是看见与明白在同一刻发生。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a curtain pulled back, with the mark already in plain sight.","cn":"核心意象：窗帘拉开，那道痕迹已经摆在那里。"},"chain":["OPEN THE CURTAIN","SEE THE SIGN","READ THE MEANING","KNOW WITHOUT PROOF","SHOW IT TO OTHERS","NEED NO EXPLANATION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6","en":"THE EYE AND THE CROWD: a mark visible on the body, and the same clarity shared by a whole audience.","cn":"眼睛与人群：身上看得见的痕迹，以及被整群观众共享的同一种清楚。"},{"senses":"S2 · S4","en":"UNDERSTANDING AND THE THAT-CLAUSE: an idea clear at once, and the impersonal frame that states the conclusion.","cn":"理解与 that 从句：一下就看懂的思路，以及陈述结论的无人称框架。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"READING THE SIGNS: what the traces left behind make clear, before the thing itself is seen.","cn":"读迹象：在看见事物本身之前，由留下的痕迹表明的东西。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"SELF-EVIDENT: the truth shows itself, so no outside proof is needed at all.","cn":"不言自明：真理自己显现，因此完全不需要外部证明。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"FEELINGS AND SYMPTOMS: what the face shows before speech, and the clinical sign that is simply there.","cn":"情绪与症状：说话之前脸上显露的东西，以及就摆在那里的临床体征。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Evident is built with the prefix e- 'out', the root vid- 'see' and the adjective ending -ent; its family fills out with -ence, -ly, -ial and the compound self-.","cn":"evident 由前缀 e-“出”、词根 vid-“看”和形容词后缀 -ent 构成；词族再由 -ence、-ly、-ial 以及复合前缀 self- 填满。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin videre 'to see' gave the participle videns and the noun evidentia 'clearness'; the root reaches back to PIE *weid- 'to see, know', which also produced vision and video.","cn":"拉丁语 videre“看见”产出了分词 videns 和名词 evidentia“清楚”；这个词根可上溯到 PIE *weid-“看见、知道”，vision 与 video 也由此而来。"},"items":[{"word":"evident","structure":"e- (out) + vid- (see) + -ent (adjective)","meaning":"able to be seen, clear","meaningCN":"明显的；可见的（e- 出 + vid 看 + -ent 形容词）","example":"The damage was evident at a glance.","exampleCN":"损坏一眼就能看出来。"},{"word":"evidence","structure":"e- (out) + vid- (see) + -ence (noun)","meaning":"that which shows or proves something","meaningCN":"证据；迹象（-ence 构成名词）","example":"There is little evidence to support the claim.","exampleCN":"几乎没有证据支持这一说法。"},{"word":"evidently","structure":"evident + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"clearly, as the facts show","meaningCN":"显然；明显地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He was evidently tired after the trip.","exampleCN":"旅行之后他显然累了。"},{"word":"evidential","structure":"evidence + -ial (adjective)","meaning":"serving as evidence","meaningCN":"证据的；可作为证据的（-ial 构成形容词）","example":"The fingerprints are evidential in this case.","exampleCN":"在这个案子里，指纹具有证据价值。"},{"word":"self-evident","structure":"self- + evident","meaning":"true without proof","meaningCN":"不言自明的（self- 表自身）","example":"The need for clean water is self-evident.","exampleCN":"对清洁水的需求是不言自明的。"},{"word":"video","structure":"Latin videre 'to see'","meaning":"a recorded image for viewing","meaningCN":"视频（直接来自拉丁语 videre“看见”）","example":"The video shows how the machine works.","exampleCN":"这段视频展示了这台机器如何运转。"},{"word":"vision","structure":"Latin visio, from videre","meaning":"sight; a forward-looking idea","meaningCN":"视觉；远见（拉丁语 visio）","example":"She had a clear vision of the city's future.","exampleCN":"她对这座城市的未来有清晰的远见。"},{"word":"visible","structure":"Latin visibilis, from videre","meaning":"able to be seen","meaningCN":"可见的（-ible 表可被……）","example":"The comet is visible to the naked eye.","exampleCN":"这颗彗星肉眼可见。"},{"word":"provide","structure":"pro- (forward) + videre (to see)","meaning":"to see ahead, hence to supply what is needed","meaningCN":"提供；预备（pro- 向前 + videre 看）","example":"The school provides free meals.","exampleCN":"这所学校提供免费餐食。"},{"word":"provident","structure":"pro- (forward) + vid- + -ent","meaning":"seeing ahead, careful with the future","meaningCN":"有远见的；节俭的","example":"A provident family saves for hard times.","exampleCN":"有远见的一家人会为困难时期存钱。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"videre","structure":"videre (verb)","meaning":"to see","meaningCN":"看见"},{"word":"videns","structure":"present participle of videre","meaning":"seeing","meaningCN":"看见的"},{"word":"evidentia","structure":"evident- + -ia (noun)","meaning":"clearness, obviousness","meaningCN":"清楚；明显"}]}},{"word":"evolve","ipa_uk":"/ɪˈvɒlv/","ipa_us":"/ɪˈvɑːlv/","definition_zh":"演化；逐步发展；演变；制定；释放（气体、热）","definition_en":"to develop gradually over a long period, especially by natural processes, or to work something out step by step","core_image":"一卷慢慢铺开的书轴，图案随展开一点点变出新样子","scene":"Finches on the isolated island evolve thicker beaks over many generations.","sceneCN":"这里 evolve 是「（物种）演化」（第 1 个义项：经自然选择长期渐变）；句意：孤岛上的雀鸟经过许多代演化出更厚的喙。图中可辨识物件：孤岛、喙形不同的雀鸟、种子、时间轴箭头。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"演化；逐步发展；演变；制定"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"evolve from","zh":"由……演化而来"},{"phrase":"evolve into","zh":"演变成……"},{"phrase":"gradually evolve","zh":"逐步演变"},{"phrase":"evolve a strategy","zh":"逐步拟定一项策略"},{"phrase":"evolve resistance","zh":"（生物）演化出抗药性"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"evolves"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"evolved"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"evolved"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"evolving"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"evolution","pos":"n.","zh":"演化；进化；演变"},{"word":"evolutionary","pos":"adj.","zh":"演化的；进化论的"},{"word":"evolutionist","pos":"n.","zh":"进化论者"},{"word":"evolvement","pos":"n.","zh":"发展；演变（较少用）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Species change: evolution by natural selection","titleCN":"物种渐变：自然选择下的演化","definition":"of a species, to change gradually over generations through natural processes","definitionCN":"指物种经过许多世代，在自然过程中逐渐改变","example":"Bacteria can evolve resistance to antibiotics within a few years.","exampleCN":"细菌能在几年之内演化出对抗生素的耐药性。","why":"The biological sense is recorded from 1832, when Lyell applied the word to species changing by natural processes toward a higher state. The old image of unfolding now stretches across generations.","whyCN":"生物学义项记录于 1832 年，当时 Lyell 把这个词用于物种经自然过程向更高状态变化。古老的“展开”意象，这时被拉长到许多世代之间。"},{"no":"02","title":"Slow development: a society or system takes shape","titleCN":"缓慢发展：社会或制度逐渐成形","definition":"of a system, society, or institution, to develop gradually over time","definitionCN":"指制度、社会或机构随时间逐步发展","example":"The village evolved from a fishing settlement into a busy port.","exampleCN":"这个村庄从一个渔村演变成繁忙的港口。","why":"From the 1640s evolve meant 'to unfold, open out, expand'. A society does not jump into a new form; it opens out stage by stage, the way a scroll is unrolled.","whyCN":"自 17 世纪 40 年代起，evolve 意为“展开、铺开、扩展”。社会不会一跃变成新形态，而是一段一段地展开，像书轴被慢慢铺开。"},{"no":"03","title":"Work it out: evolve a plan or method","titleCN":"逐步想出：拟定方案或方法","definition":"to work out or develop something such as a plan, theory, or method through gradual thought","definitionCN":"通过逐步思考形成计划、理论或方法","example":"The committee evolved a compromise that no one had expected.","exampleCN":"委员会逐步形成了一个谁也没料到的折中方案。","why":"The transitive use keeps the Latin sense 'bring forth, unfold'. Thinking a plan out is an unfolding in the mind: parts are opened one after another until a whole method appears.","whyCN":"及物用法保留了拉丁语“带出、展开”的意思。把方案想出来，是心智里的一次展开：一部分一部分打开，直到整套方法出现。"},{"no":"04","title":"Evolve into: become a new form","titleCN":"演变成：长成另一种形态","definition":"to change until something becomes a different and usually more developed form","definitionCN":"变化到成为另一种形态，通常更发达","example":"The small workshop evolved into a global manufacturer.","exampleCN":"这个小作坊演变成了全球性制造商。","why":"Into names the end of the unfolding. The word marks a direction rather than a sudden replacement: the new form is what the old form opened into.","whyCN":"into 点明展开的终点。这个词标记的是方向，而不是突然替换：新形态是旧形态展开后所成为的东西。"},{"no":"05","title":"Evolve from: trace the descent","titleCN":"由……演化而来：追溯来路","definition":"to have developed from an earlier or simpler source","definitionCN":"由更早或更简单的来源发展而来","example":"Birds evolved from a group of small dinosaurs.","exampleCN":"鸟类由一群小型恐龙演化而来。","why":"From names the starting point of the same roll. If a form unfolds out of an earlier one, then the earlier one is where the process began.","whyCN":"from 点明同一卷轴的起点。若一种形态是从更早的形态中展开出来的，那么更早的那个就是过程开始的地方。"},{"no":"06","title":"Iteration: technology that evolves","titleCN":"迭代：技术一步步演进","definition":"of a design, product, or technology, to improve through repeated small changes","definitionCN":"指设计、产品或技术经反复的小改动而改进","example":"The phone's design has evolved steadily since its first release.","exampleCN":"这款手机的设计自首次发布以来稳步演进。","why":"Modern engineering borrows the biological shape: versions succeed one another, small changes accumulate, and the later model is the earlier one unfolded further.","whyCN":"现代工程借用了生物学的形状：版本彼此接替，小改动累积，后来的型号就是先前型号进一步展开的样子。"},{"no":"07","title":"Personal change: a person grows into someone new","titleCN":"个人成长：长成新的自己","definition":"of a person or their views, to change and mature gradually","definitionCN":"指人或其观念逐渐改变、成熟","example":"She evolved as a writer over the next decade.","exampleCN":"在接下来的十年里，她作为一名作家不断成长。","why":"The metaphor moves inward: a person is also something that unfolds. Skills and views open out with time, and the later self is contained in the earlier one.","whyCN":"这个隐喻转向内在：人也是一样会展开的东西。技艺与观念随时间铺开，后来的自己已包含在先前的自己里。"},{"no":"08","title":"Language change: words evolve","titleCN":"语言变化：词义也在演化","definition":"of a language or word, to change form or meaning over time","definitionCN":"指语言或词语随时间改变形式或意义","example":"The word's meaning evolved from 'shelter' to 'household'.","exampleCN":"这个词的意义从“庇护所”演变为“一家人”。","why":"Language is a record of slow unfolding: each generation nudges a form or a sense, and the change is visible only afterwards. Evolution here is gradual and undirected.","whyCN":"语言是缓慢展开的记录：每一代人都轻轻推动形式或意义，变化只有回头看才看得见。这里的演化是渐进的、无方向的。"},{"no":"09","title":"Chemistry: evolve a gas or heat","titleCN":"化学：放出气体或热","definition":"in chemistry, to produce and release a gas, heat, or other substance","definitionCN":"化学中指产生并释放气体、热或其他物质","example":"The reaction evolves a colourless gas at room temperature.","exampleCN":"这个反应在室温下放出一种无色气体。","why":"The Latin evolvere could mean 'roll out, bring forth'. Chemistry keeps that physical sense: the substance is rolled out of the reaction, not developed over time.","whyCN":"拉丁语 evolvere 可指“滚出、带出”。化学保留了这一物理义：物质是被反应“滚出来”的，而不是随时间发展出来的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Evolve comes from Latin evolvere 'to roll out, unroll a scroll; unfold; develop', built from ex 'out' and volvere 'to roll'. The root is PIE *wel- 'to turn', and the biological sense dates only from 1832.","cn":"evolve 来自拉丁语 evolvere“滚出、展开书卷；铺开；发展”，由 ex“出”和 volvere“滚”构成。词根是 PIE *wel-“转”，而生物学义项直到 1832 年才出现。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (BEFORE 1C BC)","en":"The root *wel- meant 'to turn, to roll'. Everything in this family is some form of turning or rolling, from a wheel to a scroll.","cn":"词根 *wel- 意为“转、滚”。这个词族里的一切都是某种转动或滚动，从车轮到书轴。"},{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Volvere meant 'to roll'; evolvere, with ex 'out', meant 'to roll out, unroll a scroll, bring forth, unfold'. The image is a written roll opening as it is read.","cn":"volvere 意为“滚”；加上 ex“出”的 evolvere 意为“滚出、展开书卷、带出、铺开”。意象是一卷文字在被阅读时慢慢打开。"},{"era":"1620s ENGLISH","en":"Evolution is recorded as 'an unrolling, the opening of what was rolled up'. The noun keeps the physical image before it takes on any biological meaning.","cn":"evolution 记录为“展开、把卷起之物打开”。这个名词在获得任何生物学含义之前，先保留了物理意象。"},{"era":"1640s ENGLISH","en":"The verb evolve appears meaning 'to unfold, open out, expand'. It can still be used of a scroll, a plan, or a story.","cn":"动词 evolve 出现，意为“展开、铺开、扩展”。它仍可用于书轴、计划或故事。"},{"era":"1832 ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'develop by natural processes to a higher state' is recorded in 1832, in the biological writing associated with Lyell. Species now unfold across generations.","cn":"“经自然过程发展到更高状态”这一义项记录于 1832 年，见于与 Lyell 相关的生物学写作。物种这时是在世代之间展开的。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Evolution covers species, technologies, languages and persons, while chemistry keeps the older physical sense of releasing a gas. The unrolling image underlies all of them.","cn":"evolution 涵盖物种、技术、语言与人，而化学保留了“放出气体”这一更古老的物理义。所有义项底下都是那幅“展开卷轴”的图。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"involve","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɒlv/","tag":"same stem, different prefix","definition":"to include someone or something as a necessary part. It shares volvere 'roll' with evolve, but in- 'in' means rolling something into the matter.","definitionCN":"包含；使卷入。与 evolve 共享 volvere“滚”，但 in-“向内”指把某物卷进事情里。"},{"word":"revolve","ipa":"/rɪˈvɒlv/","tag":"same stem, different prefix","definition":"to turn around a centre. Re- 'back' means rolling back round, the literal turning that evolve's root also carries.","definitionCN":"旋转；围绕。re-“回”指滚回去、绕回来，正是 evolve 的词根也带着的字面转动。"},{"word":"devolve","ipa":"/dɪˈvɒlv/","tag":"same stem, different prefix","definition":"to pass power or duty down to a lower level. De- 'down' makes it a rolling downward, not an unfolding forward.","definitionCN":"下放（权力）；移交。de-“向下”使它成为向下滚，而不是向前展开。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"develop","ipa":"/dɪˈveləp/","tag":"broader, less directional","definition":"to grow or improve into a fuller form. Develop is broader and covers deliberate growth and improvement; evolve stresses gradual unfolding and, in biology, change across generations.","definitionCN":"发展；开发。develop 更宽泛，包含有意的成长与改进；evolve 强调逐步展开，在生物学上指跨世代的改变。"},{"word":"progress","ipa":"/prəˈɡres/","tag":"implies improvement","definition":"to move forward toward a better state. Progress carries a value judgment that things are getting better; evolve is neutral and simply says a form is unfolding.","definitionCN":"进展；进步。progress 含“越来越好”的价值判断；evolve 是中性的，只说一种形态在展开。"},{"word":"unfold","ipa":"/ʌnˈfəʊld/","tag":"the literal image","definition":"to open something folded, or to be revealed gradually. Unfold is often used of stories and plans and keeps the physical image; evolve has grown into biology and systems.","definitionCN":"展开；逐渐显露。unfold 多用于故事与计划，保留物理意象；evolve 已长入生物学与系统领域。"},{"word":"transform","ipa":"/trænsˈfɔːm/","tag":"sudden and complete","definition":"to change something completely in form. Transform stresses a sharp, thorough change; evolve stresses slow accumulation with the old form still visible in the new.","definitionCN":"彻底改变形态。transform 强调剧烈而彻底的变化；evolve 强调缓慢累积，旧形态仍留在新形态里。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin construction e- + volv + -e, the volvere family of involve, revolve and devolve, the 1832 biological sense, and the chemistry use evolve a gas.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语构词 e- + volv + -e，volvere 词族的 involve、revolve、devolve，1832 年的生物学义，以及化学里的 evolve a gas。"},"normal":[{"en":"e- (out) + volv (roll) + -e: the word says 'roll out', the way a scroll is unrolled to be read.","cn":"e-（出）+ volv（滚）+ -e：这个词说的就是“滚出来”，像书轴被展开来读。"},{"en":"The volvere family is easy to hear: involve, revolve, devolve, revolution and volume all turn or roll.","cn":"volvere 词族一听就懂：involve、revolve、devolve、revolution、volume 都在转或在滚。"},{"en":"Chemistry keeps the literal sense: evolve a gas means the gas is rolled out of the reaction.","cn":"化学保留了字面义：evolve a gas 指气体被反应“滚出来”。"},{"en":"The biological sense is dated: 1832, in Lyell's circle, so the species meaning is much younger than the word itself.","cn":"生物学义项是有年份的：1832 年，在 Lyell 的圈子里，所以“物种演化”义比这个词本身年轻得多。"},{"en":"Two prepositions mark the direction: evolve from is the source, evolve into is the new form.","cn":"两个介词标出方向：evolve from 是来源，evolve into 是新形态。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Evolve is time made visible: nothing jumps, everything opens a little further.","cn":"evolve 是被看得见的时间：没有东西跳跃，一切都再展开一点。"},{"en":"The word keeps the old form inside the new one, the way an unrolled scroll still shows the earlier lines.","cn":"这个词让旧形态留在新形态里，就像展开的书轴上仍看得见前面的字行。"},{"en":"Species, languages, phones and people all do the same thing: accumulate small changes until the shape is different.","cn":"物种、语言、手机和人都在做同一件事：累积小改变，直到形状变得不同。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Bacteria can evolve resistance to antibiotics within a few years.","cn":"细菌能在几年之内演化出对抗生素的耐药性。"},{"en":"The small workshop evolved into a global manufacturer.","cn":"这个小作坊演变成了全球性制造商。"},{"en":"The committee evolved a compromise that no one had expected.","cn":"委员会逐步形成了一个谁也没料到的折中方案。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一窝舞」——一窝小虫绕着圈慢慢跳，跳着跳着就变出新模样 → evolve 逐步演化","word":"evolve"},"root":"源自拉丁语 evolvere“滚出、展开书卷、铺开”，由 ex“出”+ volvere“滚”（PIE *wel-“转”）构成；核心是“把卷起的东西一点点展开”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of evolve, from species changing across generations to a gas released in a test tube. The common core is an unrolling: something folded or potential opens out until a new form appears.","cn":"evolve 的九个义项，从物种跨世代改变到试管里放出的气体。共同的底层是一次展开：被卷起或尚在潜在状态的东西铺开来，直到新形态出现。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a scroll rolled open, its pattern changing as it spreads.","cn":"核心意象：一卷书轴被铺开，图案随着展开而变。"},"chain":["ROLL IT OUT","SPREAD IT OPEN","ADD A SMALL CHANGE","KEEP THE CHANGE","TAKE A NEW FORM","BECOME SOMETHING ELSE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S9","en":"FROM SPECIES TO GASES: biological change over generations, and the older physical sense of a substance rolled out of a reaction.","cn":"从物种到气体：跨世代的生物变化，以及物质被反应“滚出来”的更古老物理义。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"GRADUAL DEVELOPMENT: a society or system opening out stage by stage, and a product improving version by version.","cn":"逐步发展：社会或制度一段段展开，产品一版版改进。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"WORKING OUT A FORM: a plan or method unfolded deliberately in the mind.","cn":"想出形态：在头脑里有意展开一个方案或方法。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"INTO AND FROM: the new form it becomes, and the earlier source it came out of.","cn":"变成与来自：它所变成的新形态，以及它由之而来的更早来源。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"PERSON AND LANGUAGE: a self maturing over years, and a word's sense drifting over centuries.","cn":"人与语言：一个人经年成熟，一个词的词义经世纪漂移。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Evolve is built with the prefix e- 'out', the root volv- 'roll' and the verb ending -e; its family spreads through -tion, -tionary, -tionist and the prefixed verbs involve, revolve and devolve.","cn":"evolve 由前缀 e-“出”、词根 volv-“滚”和动词词尾 -e 构成；词族通过 -tion、-tionary、-tionist 以及带前缀的 involve、revolve、devolve 铺开。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin volvere 'to roll' gave evolvere 'to roll out, unroll, unfold' and the noun evolutio; the same verb sits inside involvere, revolvere and devolvere.","cn":"拉丁语 volvere“滚”产出了 evolvere“滚出、展开、铺开”和名词 evolutio；同一个动词也藏在 involvere、revolvere、devolvere 里。"},"items":[{"word":"evolve","structure":"e- (out) + volv- (roll) + -e (verb)","meaning":"to roll out, unfold, develop gradually","meaningCN":"逐步演化（e- 出 + volv 滚）","example":"The language evolved over three centuries.","exampleCN":"这种语言在三个世纪里逐步演变。"},{"word":"evolution","structure":"evolut- + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the process of unfolding or gradual change","meaningCN":"演化；进化（-ion 构成名词）","example":"Evolution explains the diversity of species.","exampleCN":"进化论解释了物种的多样性。"},{"word":"evolutionary","structure":"evolution + -ary (adjective)","meaning":"relating to evolution","meaningCN":"演化的；进化论的（-ary 构成形容词）","example":"The change has an evolutionary advantage.","exampleCN":"这种变化具有演化上的优势。"},{"word":"evolutionist","structure":"evolution + -ist (person)","meaning":"one who studies or supports evolution","meaningCN":"进化论者（-ist 表人）","example":"The debate pitted an evolutionist against a critic.","exampleCN":"这场辩论让一位进化论者对阵一位批评者。"},{"word":"involve","structure":"in- (in) + volvere (roll)","meaning":"to roll something in, hence to include","meaningCN":"包含；使卷入（in- 向内 + volvere 滚）","example":"The job involves a lot of travel.","exampleCN":"这份工作需要经常出差。"},{"word":"revolve","structure":"re- (back) + volvere (roll)","meaning":"to roll back round, to turn around a centre","meaningCN":"旋转（re- 回 + volvere 滚）","example":"The moon revolves around the earth.","exampleCN":"月球绕地球旋转。"},{"word":"devolve","structure":"de- (down) + volvere (roll)","meaning":"to roll down, to pass power downward","meaningCN":"下放；移交（de- 向下 + volvere 滚）","example":"The budget was devolved to local councils.","exampleCN":"预算被下放到地方议会。"},{"word":"revolution","structure":"re- (back) + volut- + -ion","meaning":"a turning over, a complete change","meaningCN":"革命；巨变（re- 回 + volvere 滚）","example":"The industrial revolution changed the cities.","exampleCN":"工业革命改变了城市。"},{"word":"volume","structure":"Latin volumen 'roll of writing', from volvere","meaning":"a book; the amount of space taken up","meaningCN":"卷；体积（拉丁语 volumen 指书卷）","example":"The library holds three thousand volumes.","exampleCN":"这座图书馆藏书三千卷。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"volvere","structure":"volvere (verb)","meaning":"to roll, to turn","meaningCN":"滚；转"},{"word":"evolvere","structure":"ex- (out) + volvere","meaning":"to roll out, unroll, unfold","meaningCN":"滚出；展开；铺开"},{"word":"evolutio","structure":"evolut- + -io (noun)","meaning":"an unrolling, an unfolding","meaningCN":"展开；铺开"},{"word":"volumen","structure":"volvere + -men (noun)","meaning":"a roll of writing, a book","meaningCN":"书卷"}]}},{"word":"exceed","ipa_uk":"/ɪkˈsiːd/","ipa_us":"/ɪkˈsiːd/","definition_zh":"超过；超出；胜过；突破（纪录）；越出（权限）","definition_en":"to go beyond a limit, amount, or expectation, or to be greater than something else","core_image":"脚步跨过画在地上的那条界线，一只脚落在界外","scene":"The generator's noise levels exceed the legal limit at night.","sceneCN":"这里 exceed 是「超出（法定限度）」（第 6 个义项：超过允许的安全或法定上限）；句意：夜间这台发电机的噪声水平超出了法定上限。图中可辨识物件：发电机、噪声计读数、法规告示牌、地上画出的界线。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"超过；超出；胜过"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"exceed expectations","zh":"超出预期"},{"phrase":"exceed the speed limit","zh":"超速"},{"phrase":"exceed one's authority","zh":"越权"},{"phrase":"exceed by","zh":"超出（多少）"},{"phrase":"far exceed","zh":"远远超过"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"exceeds"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"exceeded"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"exceeded"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"exceeding"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"excess","pos":"n.","zh":"过量；过度；（adj.）过多的"},{"word":"excessive","pos":"adj.","zh":"过度的；过分的"},{"word":"exceedingly","pos":"adv.","zh":"极其；非常"},{"word":"exceeding","pos":"adj.","zh":"非常的；极度的（较书面）"},{"word":"exceedance","pos":"n.","zh":"超出量（环境与工程术语）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Go past the number: exceed a limit","titleCN":"越过数字：超过某个限值","definition":"to be greater than a fixed number or limit","definitionCN":"大于某个固定的数值或限额","example":"Drivers who exceed the speed limit are fined.","exampleCN":"超速的司机会被罚款。","why":"Exceed comes from Latin excedere 'to go out, go beyond', built from ex 'out' and cedere 'to go'. The first sense is literal: a line is drawn, and something walks past it.","whyCN":"exceed 来自拉丁语 excedere“走出、越过”，由 ex“出”和 cedere“走”构成。最基本的义项是字面的：画了一条线，某样东西走了过去。"},{"no":"02","title":"Greater in quantity: exports exceed imports","titleCN":"数量更多：出口大于进口","definition":"to be larger in number or amount than something else","definitionCN":"在数量或金额上大于另一事物","example":"Demand for the course far exceeded the number of places available.","exampleCN":"这门课的需求远远超过可提供的名额。","why":"When two quantities are compared, the larger one has walked past the smaller. The image of crossing a line becomes a comparison with no line at all.","whyCN":"当两个量被比较时，较大的那个“走过了”较小的那个。跨过界线的意象于是变成不带界线的比较。"},{"no":"03","title":"Beyond expectation: more than anyone hoped","titleCN":"超出预期：比期望的更多","definition":"to be greater or better than what was expected or hoped for","definitionCN":"超过预期或期望的程度","example":"The film exceeded all expectations at the box office.","exampleCN":"这部电影的票房超出了所有人的预期。","why":"Expectation is an invisible line drawn by the mind. What exceeds it goes past that line, which is why the verb so often carries a tone of surprise.","whyCN":"预期是心智画下的一条看不见的线。超过它的东西越过了那条线，因此这个动词常带惊讶的语气。"},{"no":"04","title":"Beyond one's authority: a legal overstep","titleCN":"越出权限：法律上的越界","definition":"to do more than one's official power or right allows","definitionCN":"做了超出自己职权或权利允许范围的事","example":"He exceeded his authority when he signed the contract alone.","exampleCN":"他独自签下合同，超出了自己的权限。","why":"Authority is a boundary drawn around a role. Going past it is not a matter of size but of jurisdiction, and the word keeps its legal tone.","whyCN":"权限是画在一个角色周围的一道边界。越过它不是大小问题，而是管辖范围问题，因此这个词保留了法律语气。"},{"no":"05","title":"Over the budget: money and time run out","titleCN":"超出预算：钱和时间不够用","definition":"to spend more money or take more time than was planned","definitionCN":"花费的钱或占用的时间超过原计划","example":"The project exceeded its budget by two million dollars.","exampleCN":"这个项目超出预算两百万美元。","why":"A budget is a line written into a plan. Once spending passes it, the plan no longer holds, and the verb names that practical failure rather than a moral one.","whyCN":"预算是写进计划里的一条线。一旦开支越过它，计划就不再成立；这个动词命名的是实务上的失控，而非道德过失。"},{"no":"06","title":"Past the safe level: legal and safety limits","titleCN":"越过安全线：法定与安全上限","definition":"to be higher than the level that is legally or medically considered safe","definitionCN":"高于法律或医学上认为安全的水平","example":"The generator's noise levels exceed the legal limit at night.","exampleCN":"夜间这台发电机的噪声水平超出了法定上限。","why":"Regulation turns safety into a number. Above that number, the thing is no longer merely large; it is unlawful or dangerous, so exceed gains an official edge.","whyCN":"法规把安全变成一个数字。高于这个数字，事物就不只是“大”，而是违法或危险，于是 exceed 带上了一层官方意味。"},{"no":"07","title":"Outdo a person: exceed someone in courage","titleCN":"胜过某人：在勇气上超过他","definition":"in literary use, to surpass another person in a quality or achievement","definitionCN":"在文学用法中，指在某项品质或成就上胜过他人","example":"No one exceeded her in patience with the students.","exampleCN":"在对学生的耐心上，无人能超过她。","why":"The older comparative sense is about persons, not numbers. To exceed someone is to walk past them on the same road, which is why the usage sounds literary today.","whyCN":"较古老的比较义关乎人，而非数字。超过某人就是在同一条路上走到他前面，因此这种用法今天听来偏文学。"},{"no":"08","title":"Exceed by: name the margin","titleCN":"超出多少：把差额说出来","definition":"in the pattern 'exceed by an amount', to state how far past the limit something goes","definitionCN":"在 exceed by + 数量 结构中，说明超出限度多少","example":"The temperature exceeded the average by four degrees.","exampleCN":"气温比平均值高出四度。","why":"By measures the distance walked past the line. The preposition turns the image into a figure, so the margin itself becomes the point of the sentence.","whyCN":"by 量出越过界线之后走过的距离。这个介词把意象变成一个数字，差额本身于是成了句子的重点。"},{"no":"09","title":"Break the record: exceed the best so far","titleCN":"打破纪录：超过此前最好的成绩","definition":"to go beyond a previous record or the best result so far","definitionCN":"超过先前的纪录或迄今最好的成绩","example":"Her final jump exceeded the world record by three centimetres.","exampleCN":"她最后一跳超出世界纪录三厘米。","why":"A record is the line left by the best attempt so far. Going beyond it is the purest form of the image: someone else's mark is on the ground, and the new attempt lands past it.","whyCN":"纪录是迄今最好的尝试留在地上的那条线。越过它就是这一意象最纯粹的形式：别人的记号留在地上，新的尝试落在它之外。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Exceed comes from Latin excedere 'to go out, go beyond, surpass', built from ex 'out' and cedere 'to go'. The cedere here means going, not yielding, and the same verb underlies proceed, precede, recede and secede.","cn":"exceed 来自拉丁语 excedere“走出、越过、胜过”，由 ex“出”和 cedere“走”构成。这里的 cedere 是“走”，不是“割让”；同一个动词也构成 proceed、precede、recede、secede。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE (BEFORE 1C BC)","en":"The root *ked- meant 'to go, to yield'. The two ideas travel together in the family: a step forward, and the giving way that a step can also mean.","cn":"词根 *ked- 意为“走、让”。这两个意思在这个词族里同行：向前一步，以及一步也可能带来的退让。"},{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Cedere meant 'to go, withdraw, yield'; excedere, with ex 'out', meant 'to go out, go beyond, overstep, surpass'. The core image is a step taken past a boundary.","cn":"cedere 意为“走、退、让”；加上 ex“出”的 excedere 意为“走出、越过、逾越、胜过”。核心意象是跨过边界的一步。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Old French exceder carried the sense 'to go beyond, surpass' and passed it into English with the same outward movement.","cn":"古法语 exceder 带着“越过、胜过”的意思，并把同样的“向外走”的动势传给了英语。"},{"era":"LATE 14c ENGLISH","en":"Exceed is recorded as 'to go beyond, surpass'. From the start it is a verb of crossing, used for limits, amounts and other people.","cn":"exceed 记录为“越过、胜过”。从一开始它就是“跨越”的动词，用于限度、数量与他人。"},{"era":"15c–16c ENGLISH","en":"The cedere family fills out: proceed 'go forward', precede 'go before', recede 'go back', concede 'give way together', accede 'go to', secede 'go apart'.","cn":"cedere 词族逐渐齐全：proceed“向前走”、precede“走在前面”、recede“向后退”、concede“一同让步”、accede“走向”、secede“分开走”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Excess and excessive are built on the same stem and name the amount beyond the line, while exceed remains the act of going past it. The cedere sense here is always 'go', never 'grant'.","cn":"excess 与 excessive 建在同一词干上，命名的是界线之外的那个量；exceed 则始终是“走过去”的动作。这里的 cedere 始终是“走”，绝不是“授予”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"excess","ipa":"/ɪkˈses/","tag":"same family, other part of speech","definition":"an amount that is more than needed or allowed. It is the noun or adjective for the surplus, while exceed is the verb for the act of going past.","definitionCN":"过量；过多的。它是名词或形容词，指多出来的那部分；exceed 是动词，指越过的动作。"},{"word":"excel","ipa":"/ɪkˈsel/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to be very good at something, or to do better than others. It comes from ex- plus cellere 'to rise', and it carries praise; exceed carries no idea of being excellent.","definitionCN":"擅长；胜过。它来自 ex- 加 cellere“高起”，含赞赏；exceed 完全不含“优秀”之义。"},{"word":"accede","ipa":"/əˈsiːd/","tag":"same cedere family, different prefix","definition":"to agree to a request, or to take up an office. Ac- 'to' plus cedere 'go' means going to something, not going past it.","definitionCN":"同意；就任。ac-“向”加 cedere“走”意为走向某物，而不是越过它。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"excess","ipa":"/ɪkˈses/","tag":"the surplus, not the act","definition":"the amount by which one thing is more than another, or behaviour that goes too far. It names the surplus left beyond the line; exceed names the crossing itself.","definitionCN":"超出量；过度行为。它命名的是界线之外多出来的部分；exceed 命名的是跨越本身。"},{"word":"excel","ipa":"/ɪkˈsel/","tag":"excellence, not overstepping","definition":"to be outstandingly good or to surpass others in skill. Excel is built on cellere 'to rise high' and implies excellence; exceed only says a limit was passed.","definitionCN":"出类拔萃；在技艺上胜过。excel 建立在 cellere“高起”上，暗含优秀；exceed 只说要越过了某条界线。"},{"word":"surpass","ipa":"/səˈpɑːs/","tag":"better than","definition":"to be or do better than someone or something. Surpass usually implies doing better, while exceed is neutral and prefers numbers, limits and expectations.","definitionCN":"胜过；优于。surpass 通常含“做得更好”，exceed 中性，多与数字、限度和预期搭配。"},{"word":"overtake","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈteɪk/","tag":"catch up and pass","definition":"to catch up with and pass a moving person or vehicle. Overtake needs a moving object on the same route; exceed needs only a limit or a figure.","definitionCN":"追上并超过（移动中的人或车）。overtake 需要同一路线上的移动对象；exceed 只需要一个限度或数字。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin construction ex- + cedere, the cedere family of proceed, precede, recede, concede, accede and secede, and the derived excess and excessive.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语构词 ex- + cedere，cedere 词族的 proceed、precede、recede、concede、accede、secede，以及派生的 excess 与 excessive。"},"normal":[{"en":"ex- (out) + cede (go): the word says 'go out', step past the line.","cn":"ex-（出）+ cede（走）：这个词说的就是“走出去”，跨过那条线。"},{"en":"The cedere family is a set of directions: proceed forward, precede before, recede back, concede together, accede to, secede apart.","cn":"cedere 词族是一组方向：proceed 向前、precede 在前、recede 向后、concede 一同、accede 朝向、secede 分开。"},{"en":"excess and excessive are the same stem: excess is the amount left beyond the line, excessive is the quality of going too far.","cn":"excess 与 excessive 是同一词干：excess 是界线之外剩下的量，excessive 是“过头”的性质。"},{"en":"Two phrases split the sense neatly: exceed expectations is good, exceed the speed limit is not.","cn":"两个短语把这个词分得很清楚：exceed expectations 是好事，exceed the speed limit 不是。"},{"en":"The pattern exceed by turns the crossing into a measured margin: exceed by four degrees, by two million dollars.","cn":"exceed by 的句式把“跨越”变成一个量出的差额：高出四度、超出两百万美元。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Exceed is a line plus a step: first someone draws the boundary, then something walks past it.","cn":"exceed 是一条线加一步：先有人画下边界，再有东西走了过去。"},{"en":"The word is neutral about good and bad: the same crossing can be a record or a fine.","cn":"这个词对好坏保持中立：同一次跨越，可以是纪录，也可以是罚单。"},{"en":"Limits, budgets, authority and expectations are all lines of one kind, and exceed is what happens to every one of them.","cn":"限度、预算、权限与预期都是同一类的线，而 exceed 就是它们各自被越过时发生的事。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Demand for the course far exceeded the number of places available.","cn":"这门课的需求远远超过可提供的名额。"},{"en":"He exceeded his authority when he signed the contract alone.","cn":"他独自签下合同，超出了自己的权限。"},{"en":"The film exceeded all expectations at the box office.","cn":"这部电影的票房超出了所有人的预期。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一克西的」——限一克，你偏要多一克，一下就超了标 → exceed 超过、超出","word":"exceed"},"root":"源自拉丁语 excedere“走出、越过、胜过”，由 ex“出”+ cedere“走”（PIE *ked-）构成；核心是“跨过界线的一步”，cedere 在此是“走”而非“割让”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of exceed, from a speed limit to a broken record. The common core is a boundary already drawn, and something stepping past it.","cn":"exceed 的九个义项，从超速到打破纪录。共同的底层是：界线已经画好，而某样东西跨了过去。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one foot landing beyond the line on the ground.","cn":"核心意象：一只脚落在画在地上的界线之外。"},"chain":["STEP TO THE EDGE","PUT ONE FOOT OVER","LEAVE THE LINE BEHIND","GO PAST THE NUMBER","GO PAST THE RULE","GO PAST THE EXPECTATION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"NUMBER AND QUANTITY: passing a fixed limit, and being larger than another amount.","cn":"数字与数量：越过固定限值，以及在数量上大于另一项。"},{"senses":"S3 · S9","en":"EXPECTATION AND RECORD: the invisible line drawn by hope, and the visible line left by the best attempt.","cn":"预期与纪录：希望画下的看不见的线，以及最好成绩留下的看得见的线。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"AUTHORITY AND LAW: overstepping a role, and rising above the level the law calls safe.","cn":"权限与法律：越出角色边界，以及高于法律认定的安全水平。"},{"senses":"S5 · S8","en":"BUDGET AND MARGIN: spending past the plan, and the by-phrase that measures how far.","cn":"预算与差额：开支越过计划，以及量出越过多少的 by 结构。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"OUTDOING A PERSON: walking past someone on the same road, the older literary comparison.","cn":"胜过某人：在同一条路上走到别人前面，这是较古老的文学比较。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Exceed is built with the prefix ex- 'out' and the root ced- 'go'; the family spreads through -cess, -cessive and -ceed, and through the many prefixed verbs of the cedere group.","cn":"exceed 由前缀 ex-“出”和词根 ced-“走”构成；词族通过 -cess、-cessive、-ceed 以及 cedere 群里大量带前缀的动词铺开。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin cedere 'to go, withdraw, yield' gave excedere 'go beyond' and the noun excessus 'a going beyond'; the same verb sits inside procedere, praecedere, recedere, concedere, accedere and secedere.","cn":"拉丁语 cedere“走、退、让”产出了 excedere“越过”和名词 excessus“越过”；同一个动词也藏在 procedere、praecedere、recedere、concedere、accedere、secedere 里。"},"items":[{"word":"exceed","structure":"ex- (out) + ced- (go)","meaning":"to go out, go beyond","meaningCN":"超过；越过（ex- 出 + ced 走）","example":"The cost must not exceed the budget.","exampleCN":"成本不得超过预算。"},{"word":"excess","structure":"ex- (out) + cess- (going)","meaning":"an amount beyond what is needed","meaningCN":"过量；超额（cess 为 cedere 的分词词干）","example":"There is an excess of supply over demand.","exampleCN":"供给超过需求。"},{"word":"excessive","structure":"excess + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"going too far, more than is proper","meaningCN":"过度的；过分的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The hotel charges excessive prices.","exampleCN":"这家酒店收费过高。"},{"word":"exceedingly","structure":"exceeding + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"to a very great degree","meaningCN":"极其；非常（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The task proved exceedingly difficult.","exampleCN":"这项任务极其困难。"},{"word":"exceedance","structure":"exceed + -ance (noun)","meaning":"the amount by which a limit is exceeded","meaningCN":"超出量（环境与工程术语）","example":"The report measures ozone exceedance in the city.","exampleCN":"这份报告测量了该市的臭氧超标量。"},{"word":"proceed","structure":"pro- (forward) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go forward, to continue","meaningCN":"前进；继续（pro- 向前 + cedere 走）","example":"The meeting proceeded as planned.","exampleCN":"会议按计划进行。"},{"word":"precede","structure":"pre- (before) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go before","meaningCN":"先于；在……之前（pre- 在前 + cedere 走）","example":"A short introduction precedes each chapter.","exampleCN":"每章前有一段简短的引言。"},{"word":"recede","structure":"re- (back) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go back, to move away","meaningCN":"后退；退缩（re- 向后 + cedere 走）","example":"The flood water began to recede.","exampleCN":"洪水开始退去。"},{"word":"concede","structure":"con- (together) + cedere (yield)","meaning":"to give way, to admit","meaningCN":"让步；承认（con- 一同 + cedere 让）","example":"She conceded that the plan had failed.","exampleCN":"她承认这个计划失败了。"},{"word":"accede","structure":"ac- (to) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go to, to agree or take office","meaningCN":"同意；就任（ac- 朝向 + cedere 走）","example":"The government acceded to the treaty.","exampleCN":"政府加入了该条约。"},{"word":"secede","structure":"se- (apart) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go apart, to withdraw from a union","meaningCN":"退出；脱离（se- 分开 + cedere 走）","example":"The region voted to secede from the union.","exampleCN":"该地区投票决定脱离联邦。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cedere","structure":"cedere (verb)","meaning":"to go, withdraw, yield","meaningCN":"走；退；让"},{"word":"excedere","structure":"ex- (out) + cedere","meaning":"to go out, go beyond, surpass","meaningCN":"走出；越过；胜过"},{"word":"excessus","structure":"excedere + -tus (noun)","meaning":"a going beyond, departure","meaningCN":"越过；离开"}]}},{"word":"exclude","ipa_uk":"/ɪkˈskluːd/","ipa_us":"/ɪkˈskluːd/","definition_zh":"排除；挡在外面；不包括；不予考虑；排斥","definition_en":"to keep someone or something out of a place, group, list, or possibility","core_image":"一扇门在来人面前合上，把他留在外面","scene":"会场门口，保安拿着名单，门紧闭着。 The guard checked the list at the hall door and excluded the reporters who had no invitation.","sceneCN":"这里 exclude 是「挡在外面」（第 1 个义项：把人挡在某地之外）；句意：保安在会场门口核对名单，把没有邀请函的记者挡在门外。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"排除；挡在外面；不包括；不予考虑"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"exclude somebody from something","zh":"把某人排除在某事之外"},{"phrase":"exclude the possibility","zh":"排除某种可能性"},{"phrase":"be excluded from school","zh":"被停学；被拒于校门之外"},{"phrase":"the price excludes tax","zh":"价格不含税"},{"phrase":"social exclusion","zh":"社会排斥（名词搭配）"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"excludes"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"excluded"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"excluded"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"excluding"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"exclusion","pos":"n.","zh":"排除；排斥；被排除在外"},{"word":"exclusive","pos":"adj.","zh":"独有的；排他的；高级的"},{"word":"exclusively","pos":"adv.","zh":"专门地；仅仅；唯一地"},{"word":"exclusivity","pos":"n.","zh":"排他性；独家性"},{"word":"exclusionary","pos":"adj.","zh":"排斥性的；排除在外的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Shut the gate: keep someone out","titleCN":"关门挡人：把人留在外面","definition":"to keep a person or animal out of a place by barring the way","definitionCN":"把人或动物挡在某地之外，不让其进入","example":"Security excluded the protesters from the hall.","exampleCN":"保安把抗议者挡在大厅之外。","why":"Latin excludere is ex 'out' + claudere 'to shut'. The image is literal: a door is closed in front of the person, so entry is refused.","whyCN":"拉丁语 excludere 由 ex「出」+ claudere「关闭」构成。意象是字面的：门在来人面前合上，进入被拒绝。"},{"no":"02","title":"Leave out of a set or a total","titleCN":"不在其中：不把某物算进去","definition":"to not include something in a total, list, or group","definitionCN":"不把某物计入总数、名单或群体","example":"The quoted price excludes delivery.","exampleCN":"报价不含运费。","why":"A set is a room with a door: what is not admitted stays outside the count. The same 'shut out' gesture now works on numbers and items.","whyCN":"一个集合就像有门的房间：没被放进来的东西留在计数之外。同一个“关在外面”的动作，现在作用于数字和条目。"},{"no":"03","title":"Bar from a competition or a privilege","titleCN":"取消资格：禁止参加","definition":"to disqualify or forbid someone from taking part in an event or enjoying a right","definitionCN":"取消某人参赛资格，或禁止其享有某项权利","example":"The athlete was excluded from the final after a false start.","exampleCN":"那名运动员抢跑后被取消决赛资格。","why":"Rules act as gatekeepers. Breaking a rule closes the door to the event, so exclusion becomes a formal penalty rather than a physical push.","whyCN":"规则充当守门人。违反规则就把通往比赛的门关上，于是“排除”变成正式处罚，而不只是物理上的推挡。"},{"no":"04","title":"Rule out as impossible","titleCN":"排除可能：认为不会成立","definition":"to decide that something cannot be true or does not apply, especially in research or diagnosis","definitionCN":"判定某事不可能成立或不适用，尤用于研究或诊断","example":"The doctors could not exclude a viral infection.","exampleCN":"医生无法排除病毒感染。","why":"Possibilities are candidates waiting at the door. To exclude one is to refuse it entry into the diagnosis or the explanation, not to destroy it.","whyCN":"各种可能性是等在门口的候选者。排除一个，就是拒绝它进入诊断或解释，而不是把它消灭掉。"},{"no":"05","title":"Suspend a pupil from school","titleCN":"停学：把学生逐出校门","definition":"in British education, to suspend a pupil formally from school as a punishment","definitionCN":"英国教育用语，作为惩罚正式令学生停学","example":"He was excluded from school for a week after the fight.","exampleCN":"打架之后，他被停学一周。","why":"Here the school building is the literal place. The pupil is kept outside the gate for a set time, so the old physical image returns as a disciplinary measure.","whyCN":"这里校舍就是字面意义上的地点。学生被挡在校门外一段时间，古老的物理意象以纪律处分的形式回来了。"},{"no":"06","title":"Drop from an analysis","titleCN":"剔除数据：不纳入统计","definition":"to remove a case, value, or group from a calculation or study","definitionCN":"把某个案例、数值或群体从计算或研究中去掉","example":"The researchers excluded outliers from the sample.","exampleCN":"研究者把异常值从样本中剔除。","why":"The data set is a container with a boundary. Anything excluded is left outside the count so that it cannot pull the result.","whyCN":"数据集是一个有边界的容器。被剔除的东西留在计数之外，因此无法拉动结果。"},{"no":"07","title":"Cut off from a will or a right","titleCN":"剥夺继承：从权利中排除","definition":"in law, to deprive someone of a share, right, or benefit by explicit terms","definitionCN":"法律上以明文条款剥夺某人的份额、权利或利益","example":"The will explicitly excludes his eldest son.","exampleCN":"这份遗嘱明确把长子排除在外。","why":"A will draws a line around the family property. Exclusion keeps one person beyond that line, and the door is now made of legal words.","whyCN":"遗嘱在家族财产周围画出一条界线。排除把某个人留在界线之外，此时的门是由法律文字做成的。"},{"no":"08","title":"Shut a group out of society","titleCN":"社会排斥：挡在公共生活之外","definition":"to keep a group from full participation in social or public life","definitionCN":"使某群体无法充分参与社会生活或公共生活","example":"Poor transport excludes many disabled people from work.","exampleCN":"交通不便把许多残障人士挡在工作之外。","why":"Society is a shared room. Exclusion leaves a group on the doorstep, not by choice but through barriers such as stairs, cost, or prejudice.","whyCN":"社会是一间共享的房间。排斥把某个群体留在门口，不是因为他们不想进，而是因为台阶、费用或偏见等障碍。"},{"no":"09","title":"Close a session to the public","titleCN":"闭门会议：不对公众开放","definition":"to bar the public or the press from a meeting or from access to a record","definitionCN":"不允许公众或媒体进入会议，或查阅某项记录","example":"The committee met behind closed doors and excluded the press.","exampleCN":"委员会闭门开会，把记者排除在外。","why":"The door is literal again: the room is closed, and those outside cannot enter. This is the oldest physical sense applied to institutions.","whyCN":"门又回到字面意义：房间关闭，外面的人进不来。这是最古老的物理义项被用到机构上。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Exclude is a Latin compound whose two parts are still transparent: ex- 'out' plus claudere 'to shut'. It has meant 'shut out' since the 14th century, and the same door appears in include, conclude and preclude.","cn":"exclude 是一个两个成分仍然清晰的拉丁复合词：ex-「出」加 claudere「关闭」。自 14 世纪起它就表示“关在外面”，同一扇门也出现在 include、conclude、preclude 里。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Excludere meant 'to shut out, shut off; prevent from entering', built from ex 'out' + claudere 'to close, shut' (past participle clausus).","cn":"excludere 意为“挡在外面、关在外面、阻止进入”，由 ex「出」+ claudere「关闭」构成（过去分词 clausus）。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"Claudere is traced to PIE *klau- 'hook, peg, nail', the same source as Latin clavis 'key'. The link to a door bar is easy to see: a peg or bolt holds the door shut.","cn":"claudere 可追溯到原始印欧语 *klau-“钩、栓、钉”，与拉丁语 clavis“钥匙”同源。与门闩的联系很直观：一根栓子把门顶住。"},{"era":"MID-14C.","en":"English first records the verb as 'to shut out, keep out; debar'. The physical sense and the figurative sense of debarring a person arrived together.","cn":"英语最早记录的动词义是“关在外面、挡在外面；禁止”。物理义与“取消某人资格”的比喻义一并出现。"},{"era":"MID-15C.","en":"The adjective exclusive appears in the mid-15c., meaning 'excluding, restrictive'. It later adds the commercial sense of goods or rights reserved to one seller or group.","cn":"形容词 exclusive 于 15 世纪中期出现，意为“排除的、限制性的”。后来又添上“商品或权利只留给一个卖家或群体”的商业义。"},{"era":"1822","en":"The social sense 'not admitting outsiders, reserved for a select circle' is recorded in 1822: an exclusive club is literally a club that shuts others out.","cn":"社会义“不接纳外人、只留给精选圈子”记录于 1822 年：an exclusive club 字面上就是“把别人关在门外的俱乐部”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The family keeps the same door: include shuts in, conclude shuts fully, preclude shuts before, and a recluse is shut away. Exclude is not related to exceed, where the root is cedere 'to go'.","cn":"词族保留同一扇门：include 关在里面，conclude 完全关闭，preclude 事前关上门，recluse 是被关起来的人。exclude 与 exceed 无关，后者的词根是 cedere“走”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares spelling or word parts with exclude; the second group shares meaning. Form is checked first, then sense.","cn":"第一组与 exclude 共享拼写或构词成分；第二组与它共享词义。先看词形，再看词义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"preclude","ipa":"/prɪˈkluːd/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to prevent something from happening in advance. Pre- 'before' shuts the door earlier; exclude simply keeps someone or something out.","definitionCN":"预先阻止某事发生。pre-“在前”把门更早关上；exclude 只是把人或物挡在外面。"},{"word":"include","ipa":"/ɪnˈkluːd/","tag":"opposite prefix","definition":"to contain or count something in. In- 'in' + claudere 'shut' means shut inside, the exact mirror image of exclude.","definitionCN":"包含；把某物算进去。in-“内”+ claudere“关”意为关在里面，正是 exclude 的镜像。"},{"word":"exclusive","ipa":"/ɪkˈskluːsɪv/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"reserved for a few and shutting others out. It describes the closed door or the group behind it, not the act of shutting.","definitionCN":"只留给少数人的；排他的。它描述那扇关着的门或门后的群体，而不是“关”这个动作。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"eliminate","ipa":"/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt/","tag":"remove completely","definition":"to get rid of something completely. Exclude only keeps it out of a group or count; eliminate removes or destroys it.","definitionCN":"彻底清除某物。exclude 只是把它挡在群体或计数之外；eliminate 是把它去掉或消灭。"},{"word":"rule out","ipa":"/ruːl aʊt/","tag":"possibility","definition":"to decide that a possibility is not true. It targets possibilities; exclude can target people, items, data, or possibilities.","definitionCN":"判定某种可能性不成立。它的对象是可能性；exclude 的对象可以是人、条目、数据或可能性。"},{"word":"omit","ipa":"/əˈmɪt/","tag":"leave out","definition":"to fail or choose to leave something out of a list or account. Omit is often accidental or stylistic; exclude is usually a deliberate boundary.","definitionCN":"遗漏或有意省略。omit 常是疏忽或文体选择；exclude 通常是刻意划出的边界。"},{"word":"ban","ipa":"/bæn/","tag":"official order","definition":"to forbid something by an official order. Ban is a legal prohibition; exclude can be a rule, a guest list, or a physical barrier.","definitionCN":"以官方命令禁止。ban 是法律禁令；exclude 可以是规则、名单或物理障碍。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real word parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Ex- 'out' is the same prefix in exit, eject, export and exhale: all of them move something out.","cn":"ex-“出”也是 exit、eject、export、exhale 的前缀：它们都把东西往外送。"},{"en":"Claudere 'to shut' also gives include, conclude, preclude, recluse, clause, close and closet.","cn":"claudere“关闭”还生出 include、conclude、preclude、recluse、clause、close、closet。"},{"en":"Include is the same door seen from inside: in- 'in' + claudere 'shut' = shut inside, while exclude = shut outside.","cn":"include 是同一扇门从里面看：in-“内”+ claudere“关”= 关在里面；exclude 则是关在外面。"},{"en":"An exclusive club is literally a club that shuts others out; the social sense of exclusive dates from 1822.","cn":"an exclusive club 字面上就是“把别人关在门外的俱乐部”；exclusive 的社会义可追溯至 1822 年。"},{"en":"Do not confuse exclude with exceed: exceed is ex- + cedere 'to go', so it means to go beyond a limit, not to shut a door.","cn":"不要把 exclude 和 exceed 混淆：exceed 是 ex- + cedere“走”，意为越过限度，不是关门。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One door, two directions. Closing it keeps a person outside; opening it lets the person in. Include and exclude are the same hinge.","cn":"一扇门，两个方向。合上，人留在外面；打开，人进到里面。include 与 exclude 是同一个铰链。"},{"en":"A guest list is a wall made of names. Every name left off is outside the room, whether the name is a person, a tax, a data point, or a possibility.","cn":"名单是一堵用名字砌成的墙。每个没写上去的名字都在房间外，不管它代表的是人、税、数据点还是可能性。"},{"en":"Exclusion can be a guard at a door, a rule on a form, or a city without ramps. The image never changes: a threshold that some cannot cross.","cn":"排斥可以是门口的保安、表格上的一条规则，或一座没有坡道的城市。意象始终不变：一道有些人跨不过去的门槛。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The club excluded women from membership until 1979.","cn":"那家俱乐部直到 1979 年都把女性排除在会员之外。"},{"en":"We cannot exclude the possibility that the sample was contaminated.","cn":"我们不能排除样本被污染的可能性。"},{"en":"The price excludes the service charge.","cn":"这个价格不含服务费。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一克斯路德」——门口“路德”一下被关死，人进不去 → exclude 关在外面、排除","word":"exclude"},"root":"源自拉丁语 excludere「关在外面」，由 ex「出」+ claudere「关闭」构成，核心动作是合上门、不让人或物进来。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of exclude, all one threshold: a door closes and something stays outside — a person, a price item, a competitor, a possibility, a pupil, a data point, an heir, a social group, or the press.","cn":"exclude 的九个义项都围绕同一道门槛：门合上，某样东西留在外面——人、价格项目、参赛者、可能性、学生、数据点、继承人、社会群体或记者。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a door closes in front of someone or something and keeps it outside.","cn":"核心意象：一扇门在人/物面前合上，把它留在外面。"},"chain":["CLOSE THE DOOR","KEEP OUTSIDE","LEAVE OFF THE LIST","BAR FROM TAKING PART","REFUSE AS A POSSIBILITY","CUT OFF FROM THE WHOLE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S9","en":"THE PHYSICAL THRESHOLD: a guard keeps a person out, and a closed session keeps the press out.","cn":"物理门槛：保安把人挡在门外，闭门会议把记者挡在门外。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"THE COUNT AND THE SAMPLE: a price item or an outlier is left outside the total.","cn":"计数与样本：价格项目或异常值被留在总数之外。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"THE RULE AND THE SCHOOL: a broken rule or a school punishment closes the door to taking part.","cn":"规则与学校：违规或校方处分把参加的门关上。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"THE POSSIBILITY: a candidate explanation is refused entry into the diagnosis.","cn":"可能性：候选解释被拒绝进入诊断。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"LAW AND SOCIETY: a will draws a line around property, and barriers draw a line around public life.","cn":"法律与社会：遗嘱在财产周围划线，障碍在公共生活周围划线。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Exclude is a live Latin compound: ex- 'out' plus the claud- stem 'shut'. English adds ordinary suffixes to the finished verb, and the same stem builds a large family.","cn":"exclude 是一个仍可分析的拉丁复合词：ex-“出”加 claud- 词干“关闭”。英语在成品动词后加普通后缀，同一词干还构成一个庞大的词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin claudere 'to shut' has the past participle clausus and the related noun claustrum 'bolt, enclosure'. Its PIE source *klau- 'hook, peg' also gives clavis 'key'.","cn":"拉丁语 claudere“关闭”的过去分词是 clausus，相关名词 claustrum 意为“门闩、围合之处”。其原始印欧语来源 *klau-“钩、栓”还生出 clavis“钥匙”。"},"items":[{"word":"exclude","structure":"ex- (out) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"to shut out, keep from entering","meaningCN":"关在外面；排除（ex- 出 + claudere 关闭）","example":"The rules exclude late entries.","exampleCN":"规则把迟交的报名排除在外。"},{"word":"exclusion","structure":"exclude + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of keeping someone or something out","meaningCN":"排除；排斥（-ion 构成动作名词）","example":"His exclusion from the team surprised everyone.","exampleCN":"他被排除在队外，让所有人都很意外。"},{"word":"exclusive","structure":"exclude + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"restricted to a few; not shared","meaningCN":"独有的；排他的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The magazine got an exclusive interview.","exampleCN":"这家杂志拿到了独家采访。"},{"word":"exclusively","structure":"exclusive + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"only; for one purpose or group","meaningCN":"专门地；仅仅（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The fund is used exclusively for research.","exampleCN":"这笔基金只用于研究。"},{"word":"exclusivity","structure":"exclusive + -ity (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being exclusive","meaningCN":"排他性；独家性（-ity 构成性质名词）","example":"The brand sells exclusivity as much as clothes.","exampleCN":"这个品牌卖的不只是衣服，还有“独家感”。"},{"word":"include","structure":"in- (in) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"to shut inside; to contain as part of a whole","meaningCN":"包含；把……算在内（in- 内 + claudere 关）","example":"The tour includes lunch.","exampleCN":"这个旅行团包含午餐。"},{"word":"conclude","structure":"con- (fully) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"to close completely; to end or infer","meaningCN":"结束；得出结论（con- 完全 + claudere 关闭）","example":"The meeting concluded at noon.","exampleCN":"会议在中午结束。"},{"word":"preclude","structure":"pre- (before) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"to shut the door beforehand; to prevent","meaningCN":"预先阻止（pre- 在前 + claudere 关闭）","example":"Bad weather precluded a second attempt.","exampleCN":"恶劣天气使第二次尝试无法进行。"},{"word":"recluse","structure":"re- (back) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"a person who has shut himself away from others","meaningCN":"隐居者（re- 回 + claudere 关闭，被关回去的人）","example":"The writer lived as a recluse for ten years.","exampleCN":"这位作家隐居了十年。"},{"word":"clause","structure":"clausa (a closed formula, from claudere)","meaning":"a separate part of a sentence or a contract","meaningCN":"从句；条款（原指封闭成句的公式）","example":"Read the clause about late payment.","exampleCN":"读一下关于逾期付款的条款。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"claudere","structure":"claudere (verb)","meaning":"to shut, close","meaningCN":"关闭"},{"word":"clausus","structure":"claudere + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"shut, closed","meaningCN":"被关上的"},{"word":"claustrum","structure":"claudere + -trum (instrument or place)","meaning":"bolt, bar; enclosed place","meaningCN":"门闩；围合之处"},{"word":"clavis","structure":"PIE *klau- (hook, peg)","meaning":"key","meaningCN":"钥匙"},{"word":"excludere","structure":"ex- (out) + claudere (to shut)","meaning":"to shut out","meaningCN":"关在外面"}]}},{"word":"exhibit","ipa_uk":"/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/","ipa_us":"/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/","definition_zh":"展示；展出；表现出（症状、特质）；出示（证据）；展品","definition_en":"to hold something out for people to see, or an object shown in a museum or a court","core_image":"把手里握着的东西举到众人眼前","scene":"展厅中央的玻璃展柜里放着一枚青铜镜，射灯照着说明标签。 The museum exhibited a bronze mirror in the centre of the hall, with a label giving its date.","sceneCN":"这里 exhibit 是「展出」（第 1 个义项：把物件公开放到观众眼前）；句意：博物馆在展厅中央展出一枚青铜镜，旁边的标签写着它的年代。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"展示；展出；表现出（症状、特质）；出示（证据）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"展品；（法庭上的）证物"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"exhibit signs of","zh":"表现出……的迹象"},{"phrase":"exhibit A","zh":"甲号证物；最明显的证据"},{"phrase":"on exhibit","zh":"正在展出"},{"phrase":"exhibit a work at a gallery","zh":"在画廊展出作品"},{"phrase":"exhibit evidence in court","zh":"在法庭上出示证据"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"exhibits"},{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"exhibits"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"exhibited"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"exhibited"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"exhibiting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"exhibition","pos":"n.","zh":"展览；展览会；表现"},{"word":"exhibitor","pos":"n.","zh":"参展者；展出者"},{"word":"exhibited","pos":"adj.","zh":"展出的；表现出的（分词形容词）"},{"word":"exhibitionism","pos":"n.","zh":"表现欲；露阴癖（语境分化）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Put an object on public view","titleCN":"公开展出：把物件摆到观众眼前","definition":"to show an object such as a painting or a machine in a museum, gallery, or public place","definitionCN":"在博物馆、画廊或公共场所展出绘画、机器等物件","example":"The gallery exhibits his early paintings.","exampleCN":"这家画廊展出他的早期画作。","why":"Latin exhibere is ex 'out' + habere 'to hold': the object held in the hand is held out toward viewers. A museum simply makes that gesture permanent.","whyCN":"拉丁语 exhibere 是 ex「出」+ habere「持、握」：把手中握着的东西朝观众举出去。博物馆只是把这个动作变成长期状态。"},{"no":"02","title":"Show a sign, symptom, or quality","titleCN":"表现出：显露迹象、症状或特质","definition":"to show a visible sign of a condition, feeling, or quality","definitionCN":"显露某种状况、情绪或品质的可见迹象","example":"The patient exhibited a mild fever and a cough.","exampleCN":"这名病人表现出轻度发热和咳嗽。","why":"What is inside the body is held out for the doctor to see. The symptom leaves the hidden interior and becomes something observable.","whyCN":"身体内部的东西被“举出来”给医生看。症状离开隐藏的内部，变成可观察的东西。"},{"no":"03","title":"Present evidence to a court","titleCN":"当庭出示：把证据举给法庭看","definition":"to submit a document or object to a court so that it can be considered as evidence","definitionCN":"向法庭提交文件或物件，供其作为证据考虑","example":"The defence exhibited the contract to the jury.","exampleCN":"辩方向陪审团出示了那份合同。","why":"A courtroom is a formal viewing room. To exhibit is to hold the item out so that judge, jury and lawyers can all see the same thing.","whyCN":"法庭是一个正式的“观看室”。exhibit 就是把物件举出来，让法官、陪审团和律师都看到同一件东西。"},{"no":"04","title":"A displayed object: the exhibit","titleCN":"展品：被摆出来观看的物件","definition":"a thing displayed in a museum, gallery, or exhibition","definitionCN":"陈列在博物馆、画廊或展览中的物件","example":"One exhibit was a bronze mirror from the Han dynasty.","exampleCN":"其中一件展品是汉代青铜镜。","why":"The verb turns into a noun: once an object has been held out, the object itself becomes an exhibit. The action and the thing share one form.","whyCN":"动词转成名词：物件一旦被举出去，它本身就成了一件 exhibit。动作和事物共用同一个词形。"},{"no":"05","title":"A labelled item of evidence","titleCN":"编号证物：法庭上贴标签的物证","definition":"an object or document produced in court and formally labelled for the record","definitionCN":"在法庭上出示并按记录正式编号、贴标签的物件或文件","example":"The knife was marked Exhibit 5.","exampleCN":"那把刀被标为第 5 号证物。","why":"The noun sense dates from the 1620s, when an object shown in court was called an exhibit. The label fixes the object so that everyone can refer to it.","whyCN":"名词义始于 1620 年代，当时法庭上出示的物件被称为 exhibit。标签把物件固定下来，使所有人都能指认同一样东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"Exhibit A: the clearest proof","titleCN":"甲号证据：最明显的例证","definition":"in extended use, the most obvious example or proof of a problem","definitionCN":"引申用法，指某个问题最明显、最有力的例证","example":"The empty shelves are exhibit A of the supply failure.","exampleCN":"空荡荡的货架就是供应链失灵最明显的证据。","why":"In court, Exhibit A is usually the first and strongest item. Since 1906 the phrase has escaped the courtroom and labels any obvious proof.","whyCN":"在法庭上，Exhibit A 通常是第一件、也最有力的证物。自 1906 年起，这个说法走出法庭，用来标记任何显而易见的证据。"},{"no":"07","title":"Manifest a trait: technical use","titleCN":"显现性状：生物学等技术用法","definition":"of a species, cell, or system, to show a particular characteristic in an observable way","definitionCN":"指物种、细胞或系统以可观察的方式显现某种特征","example":"The species exhibits an unusual mating display.","exampleCN":"这个物种表现出一种不寻常的求偶展示。","why":"Science uses the same 'hold out for inspection': a trait that can be seen is held out by the organism for the observer to record.","whyCN":"科学沿用同一个“举出来供检查”的动作：能被看见的性状，由生物体“举”给观察者记录。"},{"no":"08","title":"Take part in a fair with a stand","titleCN":"参展：在展会上设摊展示","definition":"of a company or artist, to show goods or works at an exhibition or trade fair","definitionCN":"指公司或艺术家在展览会或交易会上展出商品或作品","example":"Local firms exhibited at the trade fair.","exampleCN":"本地企业在交易会上参展。","why":"The subject now does the holding: the firm holds its goods out to buyers. The museum sense and the market sense are one gesture in different settings.","whyCN":"现在轮到主语来“举”：企业把商品举给买家看。博物馆义和市场义，是同一动作在不同场合的样子。"},{"no":"09","title":"On exhibit: the fixed phrase","titleCN":"正在展出：固定短语 on exhibit","definition":"in the phrase be on exhibit, to be on public display for a period of time","definitionCN":"用于 be on exhibit，表示在一段时间内公开展出","example":"Her sketches are on exhibit until June.","exampleCN":"她的速写正在展出，将持续到六月。","why":"On exhibit turns the noun into a state: the object is not just shown once, it is held out continuously for a season.","whyCN":"on exhibit 把名词变成一种状态：物件不是被展示一次，而是在一整段时间里持续“举在外面”。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Exhibit is Latin ex- 'out' + habere 'to hold': to hold something out for others to see. The verb arrived in the 15th century; the noun, first a courtroom object, is a 17th-century development.","cn":"exhibit 是拉丁语 ex-“出”+ habere“持、握”：把东西举出去给别人看。动词 15 世纪进入英语；名词最初指法庭上的物件，是 17 世纪的发展。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Exhibere meant 'to hold out, present, offer; show'. Its past participle exhibitus is the direct source of English exhibit.","cn":"exhibere 意为“举出、呈交、提供、展示”。其过去分词 exhibitus 是英语 exhibit 的直接来源。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"Habere 'to hold, have' goes back to PIE *ghabh- 'to take, hold, seize'. The same root gives able, habit, inhabit and prohibit.","cn":"habere“持、有”可追溯到原始印欧语 *ghabh-“取、握、抓”。同一词根还生出 able、habit、inhabit、prohibit。"},{"era":"MID-15C.","en":"The English verb is first recorded as 'to present to view, display'. The original gesture is still visible: something is held out in the hand.","cn":"英语动词最早记录为“呈现于视野、展示”。原来的动作仍然可见：某物被握在手中举出去。"},{"era":"1620S","en":"The noun appears in the 1620s for 'a document or object produced in a court as evidence'. The courtroom took the verb's gesture and made it a thing.","cn":"名词于 1620 年代出现，指“法庭上作为证据出示的文件或物件”。法庭把动词的动作变成了一个物件。"},{"era":"1862","en":"The museum sense 'an object displayed in an exhibition' is recorded in 1862, when public museums and international fairs were expanding.","cn":"博物馆义“展览中陈列的物件”记录于 1862 年，正值公共博物馆和世界博览会扩张的时期。"},{"era":"1906","en":"Exhibit A, originally the first labelled item in a case, acquires the transferred sense 'the clearest proof' in 1906 and passes into general speech.","cn":"Exhibit A 原指案件中的第一件编号证物，1906 年获得“最明显的证据”这一转义，并进入日常语言。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is close in spelling or word parts; the second is close in meaning. Sound and form first, then sense.","cn":"第一组在拼写或构词成分上接近；第二组在词义上接近。先看音形，再看意义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"explicit","ipa":"/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/","tag":"same prefix, different root","definition":"clear and fully stated. It has ex- too, but its root is plicare 'to fold', so explicit means unfolded and plain, not held out to view.","definitionCN":"清楚说明的。它同样有 ex-，但词根是 plicare“折叠”，所以 explicit 是“展开而明白”，不是“举出来展示”。"},{"word":"exhibition","ipa":"/ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn/","tag":"same root, event","definition":"a public show or fair as a whole. An exhibit is one thing or one act; an exhibition is the event that contains many of them.","definitionCN":"展览会；整场公开展示。exhibit 是一件展品或一次展示；exhibition 是包含许多展品的那场活动。"},{"word":"inhibit","ipa":"/ɪnˈhɪbɪt/","tag":"opposite direction","definition":"to hold back or restrain. In- 'in' + habere 'hold' means hold in, the reverse of exhibit's hold out.","definitionCN":"抑制；约束。in-“内”+ habere“握”意为握在里面，与 exhibit 的“举出去”方向相反。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"display","ipa":"/dɪˈspleɪ/","tag":"neutral showing","definition":"to arrange something so that it can be seen. It is neutral and common; exhibit is more formal and suggests a public show or a court.","definitionCN":"陈列；摆出来让人看见。它中性而常用；exhibit 更正式，带有公开展出或法庭的意味。"},{"word":"show","ipa":"/ʃəʊ/","tag":"general verb","definition":"to let someone see something. It is the broadest word; exhibit is narrower and usually public or evidential.","definitionCN":"给某人看某物。它是最宽泛的词；exhibit 范围更窄，通常指公开或作为证据的展示。"},{"word":"demonstrate","ipa":"/ˈdemənstreɪt/","tag":"prove by showing","definition":"to show clearly by reasoning or a practical example, often to prove a point. Exhibit only puts something in view; it does not have to prove anything.","definitionCN":"通过推理或实例清楚展示，常为证明某点。exhibit 只是把东西放到视野里，不一定承担证明功能。"},{"word":"present","ipa":"/prɪˈzent/","tag":"formal offer","definition":"to offer or submit something formally, including evidence. Exhibit stresses placing it in the viewers' sight; present stresses handing it over.","definitionCN":"正式呈交或提交，包括证据。exhibit 强调放进观众视野；present 强调交到对方手里。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Ex- 'out' + habere 'hold' = hold out. Exhibit is the hand stretched toward the viewer.","cn":"ex-“出”+ habere“握”= 举出去。exhibit 就是那只伸向观众的手。"},{"en":"Habere 'to hold' also gives ability, habit, inhabit, inhibit and prohibit; each is a different way of holding.","cn":"habere“握”还生出 ability、habit、inhabit、inhibit、prohibit；每一个都是一种“握”的方式。"},{"en":"Museum and courtroom share the noun: an exhibit is an object held out for people to inspect.","cn":"博物馆和法庭共用这个名词：exhibit 是被举出来供人检查的物件。"},{"en":"Exhibit A became a fixed phrase for the clearest proof after its use as the first labelled item in court.","cn":"Exhibit A 在法庭上原指第一件编号证物，后来固定为“最明显的证据”。"},{"en":"Do not confuse exhibit with explicit: exhibit has habere 'hold', while explicit has plicare 'fold'. One holds out, the other unfolds.","cn":"不要把 exhibit 和 explicit 混淆：exhibit 的词根是 habere“握”，explicit 的词根是 plicare“折”。一个是举出去，一个是展开。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A hand closes around an object and lifts it into the light. That lift is the whole word; the noun is the object after it has been lifted.","cn":"一只手握住物件，把它举到光里。这一“举”就是整个词；名词义则是被举起来之后的那个物件。"},{"en":"The same object can be held out in a gallery, a courtroom or a trade stand. The room changes, but the gesture does not.","cn":"同一件东西可以在画廊、法庭或交易会的展台上被举出来。房间变了，动作没变。"},{"en":"A symptom is also something held out: the body displays a sign so that someone can read it.","cn":"症状同样是被“举出来”的东西：身体展示一个信号，好让别人读到它。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The museum will exhibit forty photographs by the artist.","cn":"博物馆将展出这位艺术家的四十幅摄影作品。"},{"en":"Several patients exhibited the same rash.","cn":"几名病人都表现出同样的皮疹。"},{"en":"The letter was marked Exhibit 3 and shown to the jury.","cn":"那封信被标为第 3 号证物，出示给陪审团。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一个贼逼他」——把贼“比特”揪出来举给大家看 → exhibit 展示、出示","word":"exhibit"},"root":"源自拉丁语 exhibitus，是 exhibere「举出、呈交、展示」的过去分词，由 ex「出」+ habere「持、握」构成。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of exhibit share one gesture: something is held out for others to see — an artwork, a symptom, a document in court, a labelled evidence item, a trait, goods at a fair.","cn":"exhibit 的九个义项共享同一个动作：把某物举出去给别人看——艺术品、症状、法庭文件、编号证物、生物性状、交易会上的商品。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand holds an object out toward the eyes of others.","cn":"核心意象：一只手把物件举向别人的眼睛。"},"chain":["HOLD OUT","BRING INTO VIEW","PUT ON SHOW","SHOW A SIGN","OFFER AS PROOF","BECOME THE OBJECT ITSELF"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"PUBLIC SHOW: a museum holds out a work, and a firm holds out its goods at a fair.","cn":"公开展示：博物馆把作品举出来，企业在交易会上把商品举出来。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"THE VISIBLE SIGN: a symptom or a biological trait is held out by the body for an observer.","cn":"可见信号：症状或生物性状由身体“举”给观察者。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"THE COURT: a document is held out to the jury, and the labelled object becomes Exhibit 5.","cn":"法庭：文件被举给陪审团，编号后的物件成为第 5 号证物。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"THE OBJECT AND THE PROOF: the displayed thing becomes a noun, and Exhibit A becomes the clearest proof.","cn":"物件与证据：被展出的东西变成名词，Exhibit A 变成最明显的证据。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE CONTINUOUS STATE: on exhibit keeps the object held out for a whole season.","cn":"持续状态：on exhibit 让物件整段时间保持在观众眼前。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Exhibit is built from the Latin prefix ex- 'out' and the verb habere 'to hold'. English adds -ion, -or and participial -ed to make the family.","cn":"exhibit 由拉丁前缀 ex-“出”和动词 habere“持、握”构成。英语加 -ion、-or 和分词 -ed 构成词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin habere 'to hold, have' yields habitus 'state, demeanor', habitare 'to dwell', habilis 'handy, able', and the compound exhibitus 'held out'.","cn":"拉丁语 habere“持、有”生出 habitus“状态、举止”、habitare“居住”、habilis“顺手的、有能力的”，以及复合形式 exhibitus“被举出的”。"},"items":[{"word":"exhibit","structure":"ex- (out) + habere (to hold)","meaning":"to hold out; to show publicly","meaningCN":"举出；公开展示（ex- 出 + habere 握）","example":"They exhibit local crafts at the fair.","exampleCN":"他们在展会上展出本地手工艺品。"},{"word":"exhibition","structure":"exhibit + -ion (noun of action or event)","meaning":"a public show; an exhibition","meaningCN":"展览；展览会（-ion 构成动作或事件名词）","example":"The exhibition runs until Sunday.","exampleCN":"展览持续到周日。"},{"word":"exhibitor","structure":"exhibit + -or (person or thing that acts)","meaning":"a person or company that exhibits","meaningCN":"参展者；展出者（-or 表示施动者）","example":"Each exhibitor was given a small stand.","exampleCN":"每位参展者分到一个小展台。"},{"word":"inhibit","structure":"in- (in) + habere (to hold)","meaning":"to hold in; to restrain","meaningCN":"抑制；约束（in- 内 + habere 握，握在里面不让动）","example":"Fear can inhibit learning.","exampleCN":"恐惧会抑制学习。"},{"word":"prohibit","structure":"pro- (before, in front) + habere (to hold)","meaning":"to hold off; to forbid","meaningCN":"禁止（pro- 在前 + habere 握，挡在前面）","example":"The law prohibits smoking indoors.","exampleCN":"法律禁止室内吸烟。"},{"word":"inhabit","structure":"in- (in) + habitare (to dwell)","meaning":"to live in a place","meaningCN":"居住于；栖息于（in- 内 + habitare 居住）","example":"Bats inhabit the cave.","exampleCN":"蝙蝠栖息在这个洞穴里。"},{"word":"habit","structure":"Latin habitus (state, bearing, dress)","meaning":"a settled way of behaving","meaningCN":"习惯；习性（来自“持守的状态”）","example":"Reading every night became a habit.","exampleCN":"每晚阅读成了习惯。"},{"word":"habitual","structure":"habit + -ual (adjective)","meaning":"done regularly, by habit","meaningCN":"习惯性的；惯常的（-ual 构成形容词）","example":"He is a habitual early riser.","exampleCN":"他习惯早起。"},{"word":"habitat","structure":"Latin habitat '(it) dwells'","meaning":"the natural home of a plant or animal","meaningCN":"栖息地；生境（拉丁语“它居住”）","example":"Wetlands are the bird's natural habitat.","exampleCN":"湿地是这种鸟的天然栖息地。"},{"word":"ability","structure":"Latin habilis (handy, able) + -ity","meaning":"the power to do something","meaningCN":"能力（habilis 顺手、能握住 + -ity 性质名词）","example":"She has the ability to learn quickly.","exampleCN":"她有快速学习的能力。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"habere","structure":"habere (verb)","meaning":"to hold, have","meaningCN":"持；握；有"},{"word":"habitus","structure":"habere + -tus (past participle used as noun)","meaning":"state, condition, bearing","meaningCN":"状态；举止"},{"word":"habitare","structure":"habere + -itare (frequentative verb)","meaning":"to dwell, live","meaningCN":"居住；栖息"},{"word":"exhibitus","structure":"ex- + habere + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"held out, presented","meaningCN":"被举出的；被呈交的"},{"word":"habilis","structure":"habere + -ilis (able to be)","meaning":"handy, manageable, able","meaningCN":"顺手的；能掌握的；有能力的"}]}},{"word":"expand","ipa_uk":"/ɪkˈspænd/","ipa_us":"/ɪkˈspænd/","definition_zh":"扩大；扩展；膨胀；展开；详述","definition_en":"to spread out, become larger in size or range, or say more about something","core_image":"折叠的地图被双手向两边铺满桌面","scene":"物理课上，老师把金属球放进火里，说：Heat makes the ball expand.","sceneCN":"这里 expand 是「膨胀」（第 2 个义项：受热后体积变大）；句意：热使金属球膨胀。图中可辨识物件：金属球、酒精灯、卡尺、温度计。","pos":[{"tag":"v.","zh":"扩大；扩展；膨胀；展开；详述"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"expand into new markets","zh":"扩展到新市场"},{"phrase":"expand on a point","zh":"就某一点展开说明"},{"phrase":"expand production","zh":"扩大生产"},{"phrase":"expand one's horizons","zh":"开阔眼界"},{"phrase":"expand rapidly","zh":"迅速扩张"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（动词）","form":"expands"},{"label":"过去式（动词，已经发生）","form":"expanded"},{"label":"过去分词（动词，完成／被动）","form":"expanded"},{"label":"现在分词（动词，进行体）","form":"expanding"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"expansion","pos":"n.","zh":"扩张；膨胀；扩大"},{"word":"expansive","pos":"adj.","zh":"广阔的；扩张的；开朗的"},{"word":"expanse","pos":"n.","zh":"广阔的区域；一片"},{"word":"expandable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可扩展的；可膨胀的"},{"word":"expansionism","pos":"n.","zh":"扩张主义"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Unfold what was folded","titleCN":"展开：把折起的东西铺开","definition":"to open something out so that its full surface can be seen","definitionCN":"把折叠的东西打开，使完整表面可见","example":"He expanded the map on the table.","exampleCN":"他把地图在桌上展开。","why":"Latin expandere is ex 'out' + pandere 'to spread'. The most literal case is a folded sheet opened outward until its whole surface lies flat.","whyCN":"拉丁语 expandere 是 ex「出」+ pandere「铺开」。最字面的情形就是一张折起的纸向外打开，直到整个表面平铺。"},{"no":"02","title":"Increase in volume: heat and air","titleCN":"体积膨胀：受热或充气","definition":"to become larger in volume, especially when heated or filled with air","definitionCN":"体积变大，尤指受热或充气时","example":"Metals expand when they are heated.","exampleCN":"金属受热时会膨胀。","why":"The same spreading happens at a scale too small to see: molecules move apart and the object takes more room without gaining any material.","whyCN":"同一种“铺开”发生在肉眼看不见的尺度：分子彼此远离，物体占据更大空间，却没有增加任何材料。"},{"no":"03","title":"Grow to cover more ground","titleCN":"地域扩张：向更多地方铺开","definition":"to increase in area, especially of a city, forest, or built-up region","definitionCN":"面积增大，尤指城市、森林或建成区域","example":"The city expanded north of the river.","exampleCN":"这座城市向河以北扩张。","why":"A city is a surface on the map. Growth pushes its edge outward, exactly as a stain spreads across paper.","whyCN":"城市是地图上的一个面。增长把它的边缘往外推，正如污渍在纸上扩散。"},{"no":"04","title":"Increase the scale of a business","titleCN":"扩大业务：把经营范围铺得更广","definition":"to increase the size, reach, or activity of a company or organization","definitionCN":"扩大公司或组织的规模、覆盖范围或活动量","example":"The firm expanded into two new markets.","exampleCN":"这家公司扩展到了两个新市场。","why":"A business is an area of activity. Expanding it means adding branches, staff and markets, so the same outward spread happens in economic space.","whyCN":"业务是一片活动区域。扩大业务就是增加分支、人员和市场，同一种向外的铺开发生在经济空间里。"},{"no":"05","title":"Broaden one's experience","titleCN":"开阔眼界：让经验的面变宽","definition":"to make one's knowledge or experience wider, especially through travel or new activity","definitionCN":"扩大知识或经验的范围，尤指通过旅行或新活动","example":"Living abroad expanded her view of the world.","exampleCN":"在国外生活开阔了她对世界的看法。","why":"The mind is treated as a surface that can be stretched. New places and ideas add width to what a person can see.","whyCN":"心智被当作一个可以撑开的平面。新的地方和观念，为一个人能看到的范围增加宽度。"},{"no":"06","title":"Expand on a point: say more","titleCN":"详述：把一个点铺成一段话","definition":"in the phrase expand on, to add more detail or explanation to what was said","definitionCN":"用于 expand on，表示对已说的内容补充更多细节或解释","example":"Could you expand on your second point?","exampleCN":"你能详细说说第二点吗？","why":"A short remark is folded up; expanding it lays the same idea out in longer form. Speech repeats the gesture of opening a folded sheet.","whyCN":"一句简短的话是折起来的；展开它，就是把同一个想法用更长的形式铺开。言语重复了打开折纸的动作。"},{"no":"07","title":"Multiply out an algebraic expression","titleCN":"展开式子：把括号乘开","definition":"in mathematics, to rewrite an expression by multiplying out its brackets","definitionCN":"数学中把括号乘开，改写一个表达式","example":"Expand (a + b) squared.","exampleCN":"把 (a + b) 的平方展开。","why":"A bracketed expression is compressed notation. Expanding it spreads the hidden terms into the open, just as a folded page is opened.","whyCN":"带括号的表达式是压缩的写法。展开它，就是把藏起来的项铺到明面上，正如打开一页折纸。"},{"no":"08","title":"The lungs expand: body cavities widen","titleCN":"肺部扩张：身体腔隙变宽","definition":"of the lungs, chest, or a passage, to become wider or fill with air","definitionCN":"指肺、胸腔或通道变宽或充气","example":"The lungs expand as you breathe in.","exampleCN":"吸气时肺会扩张。","why":"Breathing is the body's own unfolding: the chest wall moves outward and the lungs take in volume, then contract again.","whyCN":"呼吸是身体自己的“铺开”：胸廓向外移动，肺吸入体积，然后再收缩回去。"},{"no":"09","title":"The universe expands","titleCN":"宇宙膨胀：空间本身在拉开","definition":"in cosmology, of space itself, to increase in scale over time","definitionCN":"宇宙学中指空间本身随时间尺度增大","example":"The universe has been expanding since the Big Bang.","exampleCN":"自大爆炸以来，宇宙一直在膨胀。","why":"The largest possible version of the same image: space is the sheet, and it stretches in every direction without spreading into anything outside itself.","whyCN":"同一个意象的最大版本：空间就是那张纸，它向各个方向拉伸，却并没有铺到自身之外的任何东西上。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Expand entered English in the early 15th century through Old French from Latin expandere, ex 'out' + pandere 'to spread'. Its physical 'spread out' sense came first; the business and cosmological senses are modern extensions.","cn":"expand 于 15 世纪早期经古法语进入英语，来自拉丁语 expandere，由 ex「出」+ pandere「铺开」构成。物理上的“铺开”义最先出现；商业和宇宙学义是现代扩展。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Expandere meant 'to spread out, unfold, expand', from ex 'out' + pandere 'to spread, unfold'.","cn":"expandere 意为“铺开、展开、扩张”，由 ex「出」+ pandere「铺开、伸展」构成。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"Pandere is explained as a nasalized form of PIE *pete- 'to spread'. The same root family includes Latin patere 'to be open' and the English word 'patent'.","cn":"pandere 被解释为原始印欧语 *pete-“铺展”的鼻化形式。同根词族还包括拉丁语 patere“敞开”和英语 patent。"},{"era":"EARLY 15C.","en":"English takes the verb from Anglo-French espaundre and Old French espandre. The first recorded senses are 'to spread out, lay open, unfold'.","cn":"英语从英法语 espaundre 和古法语 espandre 借入这个动词。最早记录的义项是“铺开、摊开、展开”。"},{"era":"1650S","en":"The adjective expansive appears in the 1650s, meaning 'having a wide extent'. It later also describes a person who is open and generous.","cn":"形容词 expansive 于 1650 年代出现，意为“范围广阔的”。后来也形容人开朗、慷慨。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Expansion and expansive extend the image to gases, markets, empires and the universe, while contract remains the opposite: one spreads out, the other draws in.","cn":"expansion 和 expansive 把意象扩展到气体、市场、帝国和宇宙；而 contract 始终是反义：一个向外铺开，一个向内收拢。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is selected for spelling and word parts; the second for meaning. Form comes first, then sense.","cn":"第一组按拼写和构词成分挑选；第二组按词义挑选。先看词形，再看词义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"expend","ipa":"/ɪkˈspend/","tag":"different root","definition":"to spend or use up money, energy, or time. It is ex- + pendere 'to weigh, pay', not pandere 'to spread'.","definitionCN":"花费或用尽金钱、精力、时间。它是 ex- + pendere“称重、支付”，不是 pandere“铺开”。"},{"word":"expanse","ipa":"/ɪkˈspæns/","tag":"noun, same root","definition":"a wide continuous area of land, sea, or sky. It is the noun of extent, while expand is the act of making that extent.","definitionCN":"一大片连续的土地、海面或天空。它是“范围”的名词，expand 则是把范围撑开的动作。"},{"word":"expansion","ipa":"/ɪkˈspænʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the process or result of expanding. It names the growth; expand names the action that produces it.","definitionCN":"扩张、膨胀的过程或结果。它命名增长本身；expand 命名产生增长的动作。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"extend","ipa":"/ɪkˈstend/","tag":"length or time","definition":"to make something longer or continue it in time. Extend works along a line; expand spreads outward in all directions.","definitionCN":"使某物变长，或延长时间。extend 沿一条线延伸；expand 向四面八方铺开。"},{"word":"enlarge","ipa":"/ɪnˈlɑːdʒ/","tag":"make bigger","definition":"to make something larger, especially a photo, room, or organ. Enlarge stresses size; expand stresses range, volume, or scope.","definitionCN":"使某物变大，尤指照片、房间或器官。enlarge 强调尺寸；expand 强调体积、范围或规模。"},{"word":"swell","ipa":"/swel/","tag":"natural growth","definition":"to become larger and rounder, often from liquid or injury. Swell is usually natural or unwanted; expand can be deliberate.","definitionCN":"变大变圆，常因液体或受伤。swell 通常是自然的或非本意的；expand 可以是有意为之。"},{"word":"dilate","ipa":"/daɪˈleɪt/","tag":"opening widens","definition":"to become wider, especially of pupils, blood vessels, or a passage. Dilate is narrow and medical; expand is general.","definitionCN":"变宽，尤指瞳孔、血管或通道。dilate 范围窄，偏医学；expand 是通用词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Ex- 'out' + pandere 'spread' = spread out. A map, a lung and a business all move outward from the same centre.","cn":"ex-“出”+ pandere“铺开”= 向外铺开。地图、肺和业务都从同一个中心往外走。"},{"en":"Pandere is a nasalized form of PIE *pete- 'to spread'; the same family gives expanse and expansive.","cn":"pandere 是原始印欧语 *pete-“铺展”的鼻化形式；同族词还有 expanse 和 expansive。"},{"en":"Expansion is the noun, expandable means able to be expanded, and an expanse is a wide open area.","cn":"expansion 是名词，expandable 意为可扩展的，an expanse 指一片开阔区域。"},{"en":"The opposite in physics and economics is contract: expand opens outward, contract draws inward.","cn":"物理和经济中的反义词是 contract：expand 向外打开，contract 向内收拢。"},{"en":"Do not confuse expand with expend: expend is ex- + pendere 'weigh, pay', so it means to spend, not to spread.","cn":"不要把 expand 和 expend 混淆：expend 是 ex- + pendere“称重、支付”，意为花费，不是铺开。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A folded map lies in a small square; two hands pull the edges apart until the paper is wider than the table. That is expand.","cn":"一张折好的地图只占一个小方块；两只手把边缘拉开，直到纸比桌面还宽。这就是 expand。"},{"en":"Heat pushes molecules apart, a brand pushes into new markets, a speaker pushes a point into paragraphs: all three move outward from a centre.","cn":"热把分子推开，品牌把业务推进新市场，说话者把一个论点铺成几段话：三者都从中心向外移动。"},{"en":"To expand on an idea is to unfold it in speech: what was folded into one sentence is laid out in a page.","cn":"expand on an idea 就是在言语中把它展开：折进一句话里的内容，被铺成一整页。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He expanded the map on the table so that everyone could see the route.","cn":"他把地图在桌上展开，让所有人都能看到路线。"},{"en":"The company plans to expand into two new markets this year.","cn":"公司计划今年扩展到两个新市场。"},{"en":"Could you expand on your second point?","cn":"你能详细说说第二点吗？"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一克斯盼大」——一心盼着它变大 → expand 扩大、膨胀","word":"expand"},"root":"源自拉丁语 expandere「铺开、展开」，由 ex「出」+ pandere「铺开、伸展」（原始印欧语 *pete-“铺展”的鼻化形式）构成。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of expand, one movement outward: a folded surface opens, a heated body takes more room, a city or firm reaches farther, a speaker lays out a point, and space itself stretches.","cn":"expand 的九个义项共享一个向外的动作：折起的平面打开，受热的物体占更多空间，城市或公司伸得更远，说话者把一个点铺开，空间本身也在拉伸。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: something folded or bounded is spread outward and takes more room.","cn":"核心意象：原本折起或有边界的东西向外铺开，占据更大空间。"},"chain":["FOLDED SMALL","SPREAD OUT","TAKE MORE SPACE","GROW IN REACH","LAY OUT IN DETAIL","PUSH THE BOUNDARY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"UNFOLDING ON PAPER: a map is opened flat, and a bracketed expression is multiplied out into the open.","cn":"纸面展开：地图被摊平，带括号的表达式被乘开铺到明面上。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"THE BODY TAKES ROOM: heated metal and breathing lungs both increase in volume.","cn":"物体占据空间：受热的金属和呼吸的肺都增大体积。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"THE MAP AND THE MARKET: a city spreads across ground, and a firm spreads across markets.","cn":"地图与市场：城市在地面上铺开，公司在市场上铺开。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"THE WIDER MIND: experience adds width, and an idea is unfolded in more words.","cn":"更宽的心智：经验增加宽度，一个想法被更多话语展开。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE LARGEST SCALE: the universe is the sheet that stretches in every direction.","cn":"最大尺度：宇宙就是那张向各个方向拉伸的纸。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Expand is a transparent Latin compound: ex- 'out' plus the pand- stem 'spread'. English builds the family with -sion, -ive, -able and -ism.","cn":"expand 是一个透明的拉丁复合词：ex-“出”加 pand- 词干“铺开”。英语用 -sion、-ive、-able、-ism 构成词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin pandere 'to spread, unfold' has the compound expandere and the participle expansus; the noun expansio and the English relatives all grow from that stem.","cn":"拉丁语 pandere“铺开、展开”有复合形式 expandere 和分词 expansus；名词 expansio 及英语同族词都从这个词干长出来。"},"items":[{"word":"expand","structure":"ex- (out) + pandere (to spread)","meaning":"to spread out, enlarge","meaningCN":"铺开；扩大；膨胀（ex- 出 + pandere 铺开）","example":"Air expands as it warms.","exampleCN":"空气受热会膨胀。"},{"word":"expansion","structure":"expand + -sion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or result of expanding","meaningCN":"扩张；膨胀（-sion 构成动作名词）","example":"The expansion of the airport took five years.","exampleCN":"机场的扩建花了五年。"},{"word":"expansive","structure":"expand + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"wide in extent; tending to expand","meaningCN":"广阔的；扩张的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The house has an expansive garden.","exampleCN":"这栋房子有一个宽敞的花园。"},{"word":"expanse","structure":"ex- + pans- (pandere) + -e (noun)","meaning":"a wide continuous area","meaningCN":"广阔区域；一片（由“铺开”转为名词）","example":"A flat expanse of ice lay ahead.","exampleCN":"前方是一片平坦的冰原。"},{"word":"expandable","structure":"expand + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be expanded","meaningCN":"可扩展的；可膨胀的（-able 表能够）","example":"The bag is expandable.","exampleCN":"这个包可以扩容。"},{"word":"expansionism","structure":"expansion + -ism (doctrine or practice)","meaning":"the policy of territorial or economic expansion","meaningCN":"扩张主义（-ism 表示主义、做法）","example":"The history course covers nineteenth-century expansionism.","exampleCN":"这门历史课涉及 19 世纪的扩张主义。"},{"word":"expansionist","structure":"expansion + -ist (person or policy)","meaning":"supporting or relating to expansion","meaningCN":"扩张主义的；扩张主义者（-ist 表示人或主张）","example":"The regime pursued expansionist aims.","exampleCN":"该政权追求扩张目标。"},{"word":"expansively","structure":"expansive + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a broad, open, or generous way","meaningCN":"开阔地；开朗慷慨地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He gestured expansively at the valley.","exampleCN":"他豪爽地朝山谷一挥手。"},{"word":"expansiveness","structure":"expansive + -ness (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being expansive","meaningCN":"广阔；开朗（-ness 构成性质名词）","example":"The expansiveness of the plain surprised them.","exampleCN":"平原的辽阔让他们吃惊。"},{"word":"expansionary","structure":"expansion + -ary (adjective)","meaning":"tending to expand economic activity","meaningCN":"扩张性的（-ary 构成形容词，常用于经济政策）","example":"The bank adopted an expansionary policy.","exampleCN":"央行采取了扩张性政策。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"pandere","structure":"pandere (verb)","meaning":"to spread out, unfold","meaningCN":"铺开；展开"},{"word":"expandere","structure":"ex- (out) + pandere (to spread)","meaning":"to spread out, expand","meaningCN":"向外铺开；扩张"},{"word":"expansus","structure":"expandere + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"spread out","meaningCN":"被铺开的"},{"word":"expansio","structure":"expandere + -io (noun of action)","meaning":"a spreading out","meaningCN":"铺开；扩张"}]}},{"word":"expert","ipa_uk":"/ˈekspɜːt/","ipa_us":"/ˈekspɜːrt/","definition_zh":"专家；能手；行家；熟练的；内行的","definition_en":"a person with deep knowledge or skill in a field, or having such knowledge and skill","core_image":"同一件事反复试过千遍、磨出茧的一双手","scene":"法庭上，证人席旁摆着几张影像片和骨骼示意图。 The expert told the court that the crack had been caused by the fall.","sceneCN":"这里 expert 是「专家证人」（第 3 个义项：在法庭上提供专业意见的专家）；句意：这位专家在法庭上说，裂痕是摔倒造成的。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"专家；能手；行家"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"熟练的；内行的；专家的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"an expert on something","zh":"某领域的专家"},{"phrase":"expert advice","zh":"专家建议"},{"phrase":"expert witness","zh":"专家证人"},{"phrase":"expert opinion","zh":"专家意见"},{"phrase":"expert hands","zh":"熟练的手；行家之手"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（名词，多于一个）","form":"experts"},{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more expert"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most expert"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"expertise","pos":"n.","zh":"专业知识；专长；专门技能"},{"word":"expertly","pos":"adv.","zh":"熟练地；内行地"},{"word":"expertness","pos":"n.","zh":"熟练；精通"},{"word":"nonexpert","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"非专家（的）；外行（的）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A person who knows a field deeply","titleCN":"专家：把某个领域摸透的人","definition":"a person with a high level of knowledge or skill in a particular subject","definitionCN":"在某一学科或领域拥有高水平知识或技能的人","example":"She is a leading expert on marine mammals.","exampleCN":"她是海洋哺乳动物方面的顶尖专家。","why":"Latin expertus means 'tried, tested'. An expert is not someone who has merely read about a field but someone whose knowledge has been tested by the work itself.","whyCN":"拉丁语 expertus 意为“试过的、验过的”。专家不是只在书上读过某个领域的人，而是其知识被实际工作检验过的人。"},{"no":"02","title":"A specialist called in to advise","titleCN":"顾问专家：被请来出主意的人","definition":"a specialist whose advice is sought on a practical problem","definitionCN":"就实际问题被请来提供建议的专门人才","example":"The company hired an expert to review its security.","exampleCN":"公司请了一位专家来审查安保。","why":"The tested knowledge becomes useful to others. A person who has already walked the ground is called in so that others do not have to repeat every trial.","whyCN":"被检验过的知识对别人有了用处。已经走过这条路的人被请进来，别人就不必把每一次试验都重做一遍。"},{"no":"03","title":"Expert witness in court","titleCN":"专家证人：在法庭上提供专业判断","definition":"a witness allowed to give an opinion based on special knowledge rather than on what was directly seen","definitionCN":"获准依据专门知识、而非亲眼所见来提供意见的证人","example":"The expert testified that the crack came from a fall.","exampleCN":"这位专家作证说，裂痕是摔倒造成的。","why":"The legal sense is recorded from 1825. The courtroom needs knowledge that no ordinary witness could supply, so the tested person is placed in the witness box.","whyCN":"这一法律义记录于 1825 年。法庭需要普通证人无法提供的知识，于是把“被检验过的人”放进了证人席。"},{"no":"04","title":"Skilled through long practice","titleCN":"熟练的：练出来的手","definition":"adjective: highly skilled or experienced in doing something","definitionCN":"形容词：做某事极为熟练或经验丰富","example":"He is an expert driver.","exampleCN":"他是一位熟练的司机。","why":"The same past participle becomes an adjective: hands that have done the task many times are expert hands, whether or not the person is called an expert.","whyCN":"同一个过去分词又变成形容词：反复做过这件事的手就是 expert hands，不管这个人是否被称为专家。"},{"no":"05","title":"Based on special knowledge","titleCN":"专家的：依据专门知识作出的","definition":"adjective: coming from or based on specialized knowledge","definitionCN":"形容词：来自专门知识或以其为依据的","example":"He gave expert advice on restoring the roof.","exampleCN":"他就修复屋顶给出了专家建议。","why":"Advice is expert when it carries the weight of trials the listener has not run. The adjective marks the source of the knowledge.","whyCN":"建议之所以是 expert，是因为它承载着听者没有做过的那些试验。形容词标记的是知识的来源。"},{"no":"06","title":"Done with mastery: an expert performance","titleCN":"精湛的：做得像行家一样","definition":"adjective: done with great skill and control, especially in art, sport, or surgery","definitionCN":"形容词：以极高技能与控制力完成，尤指艺术、运动或手术","example":"She gave an expert performance despite the pressure.","exampleCN":"尽管压力很大，她的表演依然精湛。","why":"The noun's 'tested person' becomes a quality of the action itself. A performance is expert when it looks as if trained hands are guiding every move.","whyCN":"名词“被检验过的人”变成了动作本身的品质。当每一个动作都像由训练有素的手在引导时，表演就是 expert。"},{"no":"07","title":"Expert system: knowledge in a machine","titleCN":"专家系统：装进机器里的专业知识","definition":"adjective, technical: designating a computer program that reproduces the decisions of a human specialist","definitionCN":"形容词技术用法：指能重现人类专家判断的计算机程序","example":"The clinic uses an expert system to flag drug interactions.","exampleCN":"这家诊所使用专家系统来标记药物相互作用。","why":"The knowledge of the tested specialist is written into rules. The machine inherits the adjective, though it has never tried anything itself.","whyCN":"被检验过的专家的知识被写成规则。机器继承了形容词，尽管它自己从未“试”过任何事。"},{"no":"08","title":"Expert in, on, at: the fixed patterns","titleCN":"固定搭配：expert in / on / at","definition":"in fixed phrases, expert in or on a field, and expert at doing something","definitionCN":"固定短语中，expert in/on 接领域，expert at 接做某事","example":"She is expert at avoiding direct questions.","exampleCN":"她很擅长回避直接提问。","why":"The preposition shows where the tested skill sits: in a subject, on a topic, at a performance. The adjective keeps the same 'proved by practice' core.","whyCN":"介词显示被检验的技能落在哪里：in 接学科，on 接话题，at 接具体表现。形容词仍保留“经实践验证”的内核。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Expert comes from Latin expertus, the past participle of experiri 'to try, test'. The adjective arrived first, in the late 14th century, meaning 'taught by experience'; the person-noun followed in the early 15th century.","cn":"expert 来自拉丁语 expertus，即 experiri“尝试、检验”的过去分词。形容词先到，14 世纪晚期意为“由经验教会的”；指人的名词随后于 15 世纪早期出现。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Experiri meant 'to try, test'. Its past participle expertus meant 'tried, tested, experienced', and peritus meant 'experienced, skilled'.","cn":"experiri 意为“尝试、检验”。其过去分词 expertus 意为“试过的、验过的、有经验的”，peritus 意为“有经验的、熟练的”。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"The root is traced to PIE *per- 'to try, risk'. The idea of danger and trial is built into the word: knowledge comes from attempts that could fail.","cn":"词根可追溯到原始印欧语 *per-“试、冒险”。危险与试炼的观念就嵌在词里：知识来自可能失败的尝试。"},{"era":"LATE 14C.","en":"The English adjective is first recorded as 'experienced, taught by experience, skilled'. It describes a person or a hand that has been tested.","cn":"英语形容词最早记录为“有经验的、由经验教会的、熟练的”。它描述一个被检验过的人或一双被检验过的手。"},{"era":"EARLY 15C.","en":"The noun appears as 'a person wise through experience'. The adjective's tested quality is now attached to a person who can be consulted.","cn":"名词出现，意为“靠经验而明智的人”。形容词的“被检验”品质，现在附着在一个可以被请教的人身上。"},{"era":"1825","en":"The legal phrase expert witness is recorded in 1825: a witness selected for professional knowledge rather than for direct observation.","cn":"法律短语 expert witness 记录于 1825 年：证人因专业知识而非亲眼观察被选中。"},{"era":"1868","en":"Expertise, the noun for the knowledge itself, is borrowed from French in 1868. English keeps expert for the person or the adjective and expertise for the body of knowledge.","cn":"指知识本身的名词 expertise 于 1868 年借自法语。英语用 expert 指人或作形容词，用 expertise 指那一整套知识。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares spelling or word parts with expert; the second group shares meaning. Form first, then sense.","cn":"第一组与 expert 共享拼写或构词成分；第二组共享词义。先看词形，再看词义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"expertise","ipa":"/ˌekspɜːˈtiːz/","tag":"noun, not a person","definition":"the knowledge and skill of an expert. Expert is the person or the adjective; expertise is the body of knowledge itself.","definitionCN":"专家的知识与技能。expert 指人或作形容词；expertise 指那一整套知识本身。"},{"word":"experiment","ipa":"/ɪkˈsperɪmənt/","tag":"same root","definition":"a test carried out to find out something. It shares experiri 'to try'; an expert is a person shaped by many such tests.","definitionCN":"为查明某事而做的实验。它共享 experiri“尝试”；专家则是被许多次这样的尝试塑造出来的人。"},{"word":"export","ipa":"/ˈekspɔːt/","tag":"different root","definition":"to carry goods out of a country. It is ex- + portare 'to carry', not periri 'to try'.","definitionCN":"把货物运出国外。它是 ex- + portare“运送”，不是 periri“尝试”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"specialist","ipa":"/ˈspeʃəlɪst/","tag":"narrow field","definition":"a person who concentrates on one branch of a subject, often medicine. Specialist stresses the narrow field; expert stresses the tested level of knowledge.","definitionCN":"专注于某一分支（常指医学）的人。specialist 强调领域窄；expert 强调知识经过检验、水平高。"},{"word":"authority","ipa":"/ɔːˈθɒrəti/","tag":"recognized power","definition":"a person or work recognized as a source of reliable knowledge. Authority adds public recognition; expert adds tested skill.","definitionCN":"被公认为可靠知识来源的人或著作。authority 多了公众认可；expert 多了被检验的技能。"},{"word":"professional","ipa":"/prəˈfeʃənl/","tag":"paid occupation","definition":"a person who works in a skilled occupation. Professional stresses paid status and standards; an expert may be unpaid.","definitionCN":"从事专业技能职业的人。professional 强调受薪身份与行业标准；expert 不一定以此为业。"},{"word":"connoisseur","ipa":"/ˌkɒnəˈsɜː/","tag":"taste and discernment","definition":"a person with expert judgment in art, food, or wine. Connoisseur is about cultivated taste; expert is broader and can be technical.","definitionCN":"在艺术、食物或酒方面有专家判断力的人。connoisseur 强调培养出的品味；expert 范围更广，可以是技术性的。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Experiri 'to try, test' is the core: an expert is a person whose knowledge has been tested by the work.","cn":"experiri“尝试、检验”是核心：专家就是知识被工作检验过的人。"},{"en":"Expertus is the past participle 'tried, proved'. The adjective came first in the late 14th century; the person-noun followed in the early 15th.","cn":"expertus 是过去分词“试过的、验过的”。形容词在 14 世纪晚期先出现，指人的名词在 15 世纪早期跟上。"},{"en":"Expertise is the noun for the knowledge, borrowed from French in 1868. Expert is the person or adjective; expertise is the body of knowledge.","cn":"expertise 是指知识的名词，1868 年借自法语。expert 指人或作形容词；expertise 指那一整套知识。"},{"en":"Expert witness became a legal term in 1825: a witness chosen for knowledge rather than for what he or she saw.","cn":"expert witness 于 1825 年成为法律术语：证人因知识而非亲眼所见被选中。"},{"en":"Do not confuse expert with export: export is ex- + portare 'carry', so it means carry goods out, not tested knowledge.","cn":"不要把 expert 和 export 混淆：export 是 ex- + portare“运送”，意为把货物运出去，不是被检验的知识。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a pair of hands that have repeated one task thousands of times. The knowledge is in the calluses before it is in any certificate.","cn":"想象一双把同一件事重复了上千次的手。知识先长在茧里，然后才写进证书。"},{"en":"A person is not an expert because of a title, but because a test has left a mark. Expertus means proved, not merely trained.","cn":"一个人成为专家，不是因为头衔，而是因为检验留下了痕迹。expertus 意为“被验证过的”，不只是“被训练过的”。"},{"en":"The expert stands at the edge of ordinary knowledge and is called in when the usual route runs out.","cn":"专家站在日常知识的边缘；当常规路径走不通时，人们就把他请进来。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She is a leading expert on marine mammals.","cn":"她是海洋哺乳动物方面的顶尖专家。"},{"en":"The court heard expert testimony on the bullet's path.","cn":"法庭听取了关于子弹轨迹的专家证词。"},{"en":"He gave expert advice on restoring the roof.","cn":"他就修复屋顶给出了专家建议。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「爱克死破特」——把难题“破”到底、试到头的人 → expert 专家、熟练的","word":"expert"},"root":"源自拉丁语 expertus「试过的、验过的」，是 experiri「尝试、检验」的过去分词，词根 per- 含“试、冒险”之意。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of expert, all built on one idea: knowledge proved by trial. The proved person can be consulted, can testify, can guide a hand, or can be written into a machine.","cn":"expert 的八个义项都建立在一个观念上：知识经过试炼而被证明。被证明的人可以被请教、可以作证、可以引导一双手，也可以被写进机器里。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: hands that have tried the same task until the knowledge is proved.","cn":"核心意象：一双手把同一件事试到知识被证明为止。"},"chain":["TRY","TEST","PROVE","KNOW DEEPLY","BE CONSULTED","SPEAK WITH AUTHORITY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"THE TESTED PERSON: deep knowledge turns into a field expert, then into a specialist others consult.","cn":"被检验的人：深厚的知识先成为领域专家，再成为别人请教的顾问。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"THE COURTROOM: knowledge that no ordinary witness has is allowed to speak as expert testimony.","cn":"法庭：普通证人不具备的知识，被允许以专家证词的形式说话。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"THE SKILLED HAND: a person can be an expert driver, and a performance can be expert from start to finish.","cn":"熟练的手：人可以是熟练的司机，一场表演也可以从头到尾都很精湛。"},{"senses":"S5 · S7","en":"KNOWLEDGE THAT TRAVELS: expert advice passes to a client, and an expert system carries it into a machine.","cn":"知识的传递：专家建议传给客户，专家系统把它带进机器。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE PREPOSITIONS: in a field, on a topic, at a performance — each names where the tested skill sits.","cn":"介词搭配：in 接领域，on 接话题，at 接表现——每个都标明被检验的技能落在哪里。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Expert is formed from ex- 'out' and the per- stem of experiri 'to try'. English builds expertise, expertly and expertness directly on the finished word.","cn":"expert 由 ex-“出”和 experiri“尝试”的 per- 词干构成。英语直接在成品词上构成 expertise、expertly、expertness。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin experiri 'to try, test' gives the participle expertus and the noun experientia; peritus 'experienced, tested' shares the same root.","cn":"拉丁语 experiri“尝试、检验”生出分词 expertus 和名词 experientia；peritus“有经验的、经过检验的”共享同一词根。"},"items":[{"word":"expert","structure":"ex- (out) + peritus (tested, experienced)","meaning":"a person proved by experience; skilled","meaningCN":"经经验证明的人；熟练的（ex- 出 + peritus 经过检验的）","example":"They consulted an expert on soil.","exampleCN":"他们请教了一位土壤专家。"},{"word":"expertise","structure":"expert + -ise (French noun of quality or skill)","meaning":"the knowledge or skill of an expert","meaningCN":"专业知识；专长（-ise 构成性质名词，1868 年借自法语）","example":"The job requires technical expertise.","exampleCN":"这份工作需要技术专长。"},{"word":"expertly","structure":"expert + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"with great skill","meaningCN":"熟练地；内行地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She cut the fabric expertly.","exampleCN":"她熟练地剪开了布料。"},{"word":"expertness","structure":"expert + -ness (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being expert","meaningCN":"熟练；精通（-ness 构成性质名词）","example":"The expertness of her stitching was obvious.","exampleCN":"她缝线的熟练程度一目了然。"},{"word":"experiment","structure":"ex- + periri (to try) + -ment (noun)","meaning":"a trial carried out to learn something","meaningCN":"实验；试验（尝试 + 名词后缀）","example":"The experiment failed twice.","exampleCN":"这个实验失败了两次。"},{"word":"experience","structure":"ex- + periri (to try) + -ence (noun)","meaning":"knowledge or skill gained by doing","meaningCN":"经验；经历（由“尝试”得来的知识）","example":"She has ten years of experience.","exampleCN":"她有十年经验。"},{"word":"experiential","structure":"experience + -ial (adjective)","meaning":"based on experience rather than theory","meaningCN":"经验的；体验式的（-ial 构成形容词）","example":"The course is experiential.","exampleCN":"这门课是体验式的。"},{"word":"inexperienced","structure":"in- (not) + experienced (adjective)","meaning":"lacking experience","meaningCN":"无经验的；不老练的（in- 表否定 + 分词形容词）","example":"He was too inexperienced for the role.","exampleCN":"对这个角色来说，他太没经验了。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"experiri","structure":"ex- + periri (to try)","meaning":"to try, test","meaningCN":"尝试；检验"},{"word":"expertus","structure":"experiri + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"tried, tested, proved","meaningCN":"试过的；被验证的"},{"word":"peritus","structure":"per- (trial) + -itus (adjective)","meaning":"experienced, skilled","meaningCN":"有经验的；熟练的"},{"word":"experientia","structure":"experiri + -entia (noun)","meaning":"trial, proof, experience","meaningCN":"试炼；证明；经验"}]}},{"word":"explicit","ipa_uk":"/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/","ipa_us":"/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/","definition_zh":"明确的；清楚的；直言的；露骨的；显式的","definition_en":"stated clearly and in detail, leaving nothing to be inferred or guessed","core_image":"折起的纸被完全摊平，每一道折痕都露出来","scene":"监考老师指着黑板上的规则说：The instructions are explicit: no phones in the exam room.","sceneCN":"这里 explicit 是「明确写明的」（第 1 个义项：完全说清、不留暗示）；句意：规则写得很明确：考场内不许用手机。图中可辨识物件：黑板、规则清单、手机收纳盒、监考老师。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"明确的；清楚的；直言的；露骨的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"explicit instructions","zh":"明确的指示"},{"phrase":"explicit consent","zh":"明确同意"},{"phrase":"explicit warning","zh":"明确的警告"},{"phrase":"sexually explicit","zh":"含有露骨性内容的"},{"phrase":"make something explicit","zh":"把某事明确说出来"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more explicit"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most explicit"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"explicitly","pos":"adv.","zh":"明确地；直截了当地"},{"word":"explicitness","pos":"n.","zh":"明确性；直白程度"},{"word":"explicate","pos":"v.","zh":"解释；阐发（文本或理论）"},{"word":"explication","pos":"n.","zh":"解释；阐释"},{"word":"explicable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可解释的；可说明的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Fully stated: nothing left implied","titleCN":"明确写出：不留任何暗示","definition":"expressed in clear and complete words, with nothing left for the reader to infer","definitionCN":"用清楚完整的话表达，不给读者留下需要推断的空白","example":"The instructions are explicit: no phones in the exam room.","exampleCN":"规则写得很明确：考场内不许用手机。","why":"Latin explicare is ex 'out' + plicare 'to fold'. Explicit is the sheet unfolded: every line that could have stayed hidden is now open to view.","whyCN":"拉丁语 explicare 是 ex「出」+ plicare「折叠」。explicit 就是被展开的那张纸：原本可以藏住的每一行，现在都摊在外面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Precise and unambiguous","titleCN":"确切无歧义：不给第二种读法","definition":"so clearly worded that it can be understood in only one way","definitionCN":"措辞清楚到只有一种理解方式","example":"The doctor gave an explicit warning about mixing the drugs.","exampleCN":"医生对混用这些药物发出了明确警告。","why":"A folded page hides parts of the text. An explicit wording lays the whole sentence flat, so there is no fold left in which a second meaning could hide.","whyCN":"折起的页面会遮住部分文字。明确的措辞把整句话摊平，于是没有一道折痕还能藏住第二种意思。"},{"no":"03","title":"Open about something usually hidden","titleCN":"直言不讳：把通常藏着的话说出来","definition":"willing to state something openly that people often leave unsaid","definitionCN":"愿意公开说出人们通常避而不谈的事","example":"She was explicit about her reasons for leaving.","exampleCN":"她直言不讳地说明了自己离开的原因。","why":"The verb can be reflexive: a person unfolds his own motives instead of leaving them folded inside. Openness is the human version of the same image.","whyCN":"这个词也可以指向人自身：一个人把自己的动机展开，而不是折起来藏在里面。坦率就是同一意象在人的身上的版本。"},{"no":"04","title":"Sexually explicit content","titleCN":"露骨性内容：不加遮掩地呈现","definition":"showing sexual acts or nudity in an open, detailed way","definitionCN":"以公开、详细的方式呈现性行为或裸体","example":"The film is rated for explicit content.","exampleCN":"这部电影因含露骨内容而被分级。","why":"The modern phrase uses 'explicit' for what is shown rather than implied. Nothing is folded away or concealed, and that is exactly why the label warns.","whyCN":"现代短语用 explicit 指“直接呈现而非暗示”的内容。没有什么被折起或遮住，这正是这个标签要警告的地方。"},{"no":"05","title":"Explicit language: open swearing","titleCN":"粗口直出：不加消音的歌词或言语","definition":"containing swear words or crude language that is not edited out","definitionCN":"含有未消音、未删改的粗话或脏话","example":"The album carries an explicit lyrics warning.","exampleCN":"这张专辑带有“含粗口歌词”的警示。","why":"A clean version folds the offensive word away; an explicit version leaves it unfolded in the open. The same contrast between hidden and displayed.","whyCN":"干净版把冒犯性的词折起来藏掉；explicit 版则让它展开在外。仍是“藏”与“露”的同一组对立。"},{"no":"06","title":"Explicit formula: fully specified","titleCN":"显式公式：每一项都写出来","definition":"in mathematics and logic, stated in full form rather than left in shorthand or implication","definitionCN":"数学与逻辑中，以完整形式写出，而不是用简写或隐含","example":"The paper gives an explicit formula for the solution.","exampleCN":"论文给出了解的显式公式。","why":"A formula in shorthand is folded up; an explicit formula multiplies it out so that every term stands visible. This is the algebraic version of unfolding.","whyCN":"简写公式是折起来的；显式公式把它乘开，让每一项都立在外面。这是“展开”的代数版本。"},{"no":"07","title":"Explicit consent: permission in plain terms","titleCN":"明确同意：法律与医疗上的明示许可","definition":"clear, recorded permission given for a specific act, especially in law or medicine","definitionCN":"对某一具体行为给出的清楚、有记录的许可，尤用于法律或医疗","example":"The study required explicit consent from every participant.","exampleCN":"这项研究要求每位参与者明确同意。","why":"Consent that is merely implied can be disputed later. Explicit consent is written out and signed, so the permission cannot be folded back into silence.","whyCN":"仅仅隐含的同意日后可能有争议。explicit consent 被写出来并签署，许可就无法再折回沉默里。"},{"no":"08","title":"Explicit memory: consciously available","titleCN":"外显记忆：能清楚说出来的记忆","definition":"in psychology, a memory that a person can consciously recall and state","definitionCN":"心理学中指人能有意识地回忆并说出的记忆","example":"Explicit memory lets you recall your first day at school.","exampleCN":"外显记忆让你能回想起上学第一天。","why":"What is explicit is laid out where the mind can look at it. Explicit memory is knowledge a person can unfold and describe, unlike a skill that stays folded into the body.","whyCN":"explicit 的东西被铺在心灵能看见的地方。外显记忆是人能展开并描述的知识，不同于折进身体里的技能。"},{"no":"09","title":"The old manuscript explicit: here the book ends","titleCN":"古抄本收尾语：书到此展开完毕","definition":"historical, noun: the closing word or note of a medieval manuscript, marking the end of the text","definitionCN":"历史用法，名词：中世纪抄本末尾的收尾词或题记，标记正文结束","example":"The scribe wrote explicit at the foot of the last page.","exampleCN":"抄写员在最后一页末尾写下了 explicit。","why":"Medieval scribes ended with explicitus est liber, 'the book is unfolded/read out'. The word that marked a completed reading became the label for the end itself.","whyCN":"中世纪抄写员用 explicitus est liber 收尾，意为“书已展开／读完了”。标记“读完”的词，最后变成了“结尾”本身的标签。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Explicit comes from Latin explicare 'to unfold, unravel, explain', ex- 'out' + plicare 'to fold'. The English adjective, meaning 'clear, not ambiguous', is first recorded in the 1610s through French explicite.","cn":"explicit 来自拉丁语 explicare“展开、解开、解释”，由 ex-“出”+ plicare“折叠”构成。英语形容词“清楚、不含糊”于 1610 年代经法语 explicite 进入英语。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Explicare meant 'to unfold, unroll; disentangle; explain'. The image is physical: a folded thing is opened until its parts can be seen.","cn":"explicare 意为“展开、铺开；解开；解释”。意象是物理的：把折起的东西打开，直到各部分都能看见。"},{"era":"PIE","en":"Plicare 'to fold' goes back to PIE *plek- 'to plait, weave, fold'. The same root gives plait, plexus, complex, and the two Latin directions in- and ex-.","cn":"plicare“折叠”可追溯到原始印欧语 *plek-“编织、折叠”。同一词根生出 plait、plexus、complex，以及拉丁语里 in- 与 ex- 两个方向。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Explicitus, a variant past participle of explicare, meant 'unobstructed, clear'. What is unfolded is also unblocked: nothing is left in the way of understanding.","cn":"explicitus 是 explicare 的异体过去分词，意为“无阻碍的、清楚的”。被展开的东西也畅通无阻：理解的道路上没有东西挡着。"},{"era":"1610S","en":"English takes the adjective from French explicite with the sense 'clear, plain, not ambiguous'. It is the opposite of implicit, which is folded in.","cn":"英语从法语 explicite 借入形容词，义为“清楚的、明白的、不含糊的”。它是 implicit 的反面，后者是“折进去的”。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL MANUSCRIPTS","en":"Scribes closed a manuscript with explicitus est liber, 'the book is unfolded / read out'. From that formula, explicit became the word written at the end of a text.","cn":"抄写员用 explicitus est liber“书已展开／读完了”来结束抄本。从这个固定语开始，explicit 成了写在文本末尾的那个词。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the 'nothing hidden' core: explicit instructions, explicit consent, sexually explicit, explicit memory. Its mirror is implicit, in- 'in' + plicare 'fold'.","cn":"现代英语保留“没有隐藏”的内核：explicit instructions、explicit consent、sexually explicit、explicit memory。它的镜像是 implicit，即 in-“内”+ plicare“折”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is close in spelling or word parts; the second is close in meaning. Form first, then sense.","cn":"第一组在拼写或构词成分上接近；第二组在词义上接近。先看词形，再看意义。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"implicit","ipa":"/ɪmˈplɪsɪt/","tag":"exact opposite","definition":"implied but not stated. In- 'in' + plicare 'fold' means folded in, the mirror image of explicit's unfolded.","definitionCN":"隐含而未明说的。in-“内”+ plicare“折”意为折进去，正是 explicit“展开”的镜像。"},{"word":"explicate","ipa":"/ˈeksplɪkeɪt/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"to explain a text or idea in detail. It is the verb; explicit is the adjective for what has been fully laid out.","definitionCN":"详细解释文本或观点。它是动词；explicit 是形容词，形容已被完全铺开的内容。"},{"word":"exploit","ipa":"/ɪkˈsplɔɪt/","tag":"same root, diverged","definition":"to use something for profit, or a bold deed. It comes from Latin explicitum 'something unfolded or settled', but its meaning moved to 'turn to account'.","definitionCN":"利用；开发；也可指功绩。它来自拉丁语 explicitum“被展开或了结之事”，但词义转向“加以利用”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"clear","ipa":"/klɪə/","tag":"easy to understand","definition":"easy to understand or see. Clear can describe a style or a view; explicit stresses that the content is actually stated, not merely easy.","definitionCN":"易懂的；清晰的。clear 可形容文风或视野；explicit 强调内容确实被说出来，而不只是容易懂。"},{"word":"definite","ipa":"/ˈdefɪnət/","tag":"fixed and certain","definition":"fixed, certain, and not likely to change. Definite stresses certainty; explicit stresses complete expression.","definitionCN":"确定的；不会改变的。definite 强调确定性；explicit 强调表达完整。"},{"word":"unambiguous","ipa":"/ˌʌnæmˈbɪɡjuəs/","tag":"one meaning only","definition":"having only one possible meaning. It focuses on the absence of ambiguity; explicit focuses on the presence of full statement.","definitionCN":"只有一种可能含义的。它聚焦于“没有歧义”；explicit 聚焦于“把话完整说出来”。"},{"word":"express","ipa":"/ɪkˈspres/","tag":"legal and formal","definition":"stated openly and specifically, especially in a contract or law. Express is formal and legal; explicit is broader and also covers sexual content.","definitionCN":"明示的，尤用于合同或法律。express 正式且偏法律；explicit 范围更广，也可指露骨内容。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real parts, real phrases and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"真实的构词成分、真实短语和真实同族词，而不是编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Ex- 'out' + plicare 'fold' = unfold. Explicit is the sheet opened flat, with every fold laid out.","cn":"ex-“出”+ plicare“折”= 展开。explicit 就是被摊平的那张纸，每一道折痕都铺开。"},{"en":"The same plicare gives implicit 'folded in', implicate, explicate, complexity and plait.","cn":"同一个 plicare 生出 implicit“折进去”、implicate、explicate、complexity 和 plait。"},{"en":"Medieval scribes ended with explicitus est liber, 'the book is unfolded / read out'; from this the word explicit came to mark the end of a text.","cn":"中世纪抄写员用 explicitus est liber“书已展开／读完了”收尾；由此 explicit 成了标记文本结尾的词。"},{"en":"To make something explicit is the everyday phrase for bringing an unstated rule or feeling into the open.","cn":"make something explicit 是日常短语，意为把没说出口的规则或感受摆到明面上。"},{"en":"Do not confuse explicit with exhibit: exhibit has habere 'hold' and means hold out; explicit has plicare 'fold' and means unfold.","cn":"不要把 explicit 和 exhibit 混淆：exhibit 的词根是 habere“握”，意为举出去；explicit 的词根是 plicare“折”，意为展开。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A letter folded small: implicit keeps it closed, explicit opens it flat and reads every line aloud.","cn":"一封折得很小的信：implicit 让它保持合着，explicit 把它摊平，并逐行读出来。"},{"en":"A rule everyone follows but nobody says is implicit; writing it on the door makes it explicit.","cn":"一条人人都遵守却没人说出口的规则是 implicit；把它写在门上，就变成 explicit。"},{"en":"Every fold has an inside and an outside. Implicit is the inside; explicit is the outside turned toward the reader.","cn":"每道折痕都有里面和外面。implicit 是里面；explicit 是翻向读者的外面。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The instructions were explicit: no phones in the exam room.","cn":"规则写得很明确：考场内不许用手机。"},{"en":"She was explicit about her reasons for leaving.","cn":"她直言不讳地说明了自己离开的原因。"},{"en":"The film is rated for explicit content.","cn":"这部电影因含露骨内容而被分级。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「一克斯普利说」——把折起的话全铺开、普利落落地说明白 → explicit 明确的","word":"explicit"},"root":"源自拉丁语 explicitus「无阻碍的、清楚的」，是 explicare「展开、解开、解释」的异体过去分词，由 ex「出」+ plicare「折叠」构成。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of explicit share one gesture: a folded surface is opened until nothing is hidden — a rule, a warning, a motive, a sexual scene, a swear word, a formula, a consent form, a memory, or the end of a manuscript.","cn":"explicit 的九个义项共享同一个动作：把折起的表面打开，直到没有东西被遮住——规则、警告、动机、性场景、脏话、公式、同意书、记忆，或一部抄本的结尾。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a folded sheet is opened flat so that every line can be read.","cn":"核心意象：折起的纸被完全摊平，每一行都能读到。"},"chain":["FOLD","UNFOLD","LAY FLAT","LEAVE NOTHING HIDDEN","STATE IN PLAIN WORDS","MARK THE END"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"THE OPEN PAGE: a fully stated instruction or warning leaves no second reading.","cn":"摊开的页面：完整写出的指示或警告，不留下第二种读法。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4 · S5","en":"OPENNESS ABOUT THE HIDDEN: a motive, a sexual scene, or a swear word is brought out instead of folded away.","cn":"对隐藏之事的坦白：动机、性场景或脏话被摆出来，而不是折起来藏掉。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"THE FULLY SPECIFIED: an explicit formula writes out every term, and explicit memory can be recalled and stated.","cn":"完整写明：显式公式写出每一项，外显记忆能被回忆并说出。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"THE SIGNED PERMISSION: explicit consent cannot be folded back into silence.","cn":"签署的许可：明确同意无法再折回沉默里。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE OLD COLOPHON: explicitus est liber marked the book as unfolded and finished.","cn":"古老的收尾语：explicitus est liber 标记书已展开、已读完。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Explicit is the adjective from Latin explicare: ex- 'out' plus the plic- stem 'fold'. English builds adverbs, nouns, verbs and negatives on this stem, and the same root runs through implicit, complex and plait.","cn":"explicit 是拉丁语 explicare 的形容词：ex-“出”加 plic- 词干“折”。英语在这个词干上构成副词、名词、动词和否定形式；同一词根也贯穿 implicit、complex 和 plait。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin plicare 'to fold' has the compound explicare 'to unfold, explain' and its participle explicitus; the opposite compound implicare 'to fold in' gives implicit and implicate.","cn":"拉丁语 plicare“折叠”有复合形式 explicare“展开、解释”及其分词 explicitus；反方向的复合形式 implicare“折进去”生出 implicit 和 implicate。"},"items":[{"word":"explicit","structure":"ex- (out) + plicare (to fold) + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"unfolded; clear and fully stated","meaningCN":"展开的；清楚的；明确写出的（ex- 出 + plicare 折）","example":"The rule is explicit.","exampleCN":"规则很明确。"},{"word":"explicitly","structure":"explicit + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a clear, fully stated way","meaningCN":"明确地；直截了当地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She explicitly denied the claim.","exampleCN":"她明确否认了这一说法。"},{"word":"explicitness","structure":"explicit + -ness (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being explicit","meaningCN":"明确性；直白程度（-ness 构成性质名词）","example":"The explicitness of the warning left no doubt.","exampleCN":"警告的明确程度让人毫无怀疑。"},{"word":"explicate","structure":"ex- + plicare + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to unfold the meaning of a text or idea","meaningCN":"解释；阐发（把折叠的含义展开）","example":"The essay explicates the poem line by line.","exampleCN":"这篇文章逐行阐释这首诗。"},{"word":"explication","structure":"explicate + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"a detailed explanation","meaningCN":"解释；阐释（-ion 构成动作名词）","example":"Her explication of the theory was clear.","exampleCN":"她对这个理论的阐释很清楚。"},{"word":"explicable","structure":"explicate + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be explained","meaningCN":"可解释的（-able 表能够）","example":"The error is explicable.","exampleCN":"这个错误是可以解释的。"},{"word":"inexplicable","structure":"in- (not) + explicable (able to be explained)","meaning":"impossible to explain","meaningCN":"无法解释的（in- 表否定 + 可解释的）","example":"The lights failed for inexplicable reasons.","exampleCN":"灯以无法解释的原因熄灭了。"},{"word":"implicit","structure":"in- (in) + plicare (to fold) + -tus","meaning":"folded in; suggested but not stated","meaningCN":"折进去的；隐含的（与 explicit 的“展开”相对）","example":"There was an implicit threat in his tone.","exampleCN":"他的语气里有一种隐含的威胁。"},{"word":"implicate","structure":"in- (in) + plicare (to fold) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to fold someone into a matter; to involve","meaningCN":"牵连；使卷入（把某人折进事件里）","example":"The letter implicated two officials.","exampleCN":"这封信牵连了两名官员。"},{"word":"exploit","structure":"Latin explicitum (something unfolded or settled)","meaning":"to turn something to use; a bold act","meaningCN":"利用；开发；功绩（由“展开、了结之事”转为“加以利用”）","example":"The company exploited a gap in the market.","exampleCN":"这家公司利用了市场空白。"},{"word":"complex","structure":"com- (together) + plectere (to braid, weave)","meaning":"woven together; not simple","meaningCN":"复杂的（com- 共同 + plectere 编织，同属 *plek- 词根）","example":"The problem is more complex than it looks.","exampleCN":"这个问题比看上去更复杂。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"plicare","structure":"plicare (verb)","meaning":"to fold, plait","meaningCN":"折叠；编织"},{"word":"explicare","structure":"ex- (out) + plicare (to fold)","meaning":"to unfold, unravel, explain","meaningCN":"展开；解开；解释"},{"word":"explicitus","structure":"explicare + -tus (variant past participle)","meaning":"unfolded, unobstructed, clear","meaningCN":"展开的；无阻碍的；清楚的"},{"word":"implicare","structure":"in- (in) + plicare (to fold)","meaning":"to fold in, entangle, involve","meaningCN":"折进去；缠住；牵连"},{"word":"plexus","structure":"plectere + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"braided, interwoven","meaningCN":"编织的；交织的"}]}}]);
